s. |\n+| pipavlo82/Chronicle | v0.1 adapter account retained; no additional source integration selected for v0.2 | Retained v0.1 account; no new maturity claim | Supplied entry identity, exact reference strings and historical/current query boundaries inform the continuity adapter. Collection/portfolio aggregate-root construction and verification remain unimplemented. User histories and the Chronicle brand are not imported. |\n+| pipavlo82/conduct-witness | v0.1 methodology account retained; no additional source integration selected for v0.2 | Retained v0.1 account; no new maturity claim | Pinned reproduction, operator separation and workflow attestation remain assurance methodology. Upstream template/verifier code is not treated as independently authored Pavlo code. |\n+| pipavlo82/cross-reference-console | v0.1 optional_interface account retained; no additional source integration selected for v0.2 | Retained v0.1 account; no new maturity claim | Claim identity and signed Cell/lineage boundaries remain a declared optional observation interface. Registry signatures do not supply semantic independence. |\n+| pipavlo82/crystal-receipt | v0.1 runtime account retained; no additional source integration selected for v0.2 | Retained v0.1 account; no new maturity claim | Selected ReceiptOS core canonicalization, integrity, portable evidence and continuity are native adapter candidates. The desktop subtree and captured external evidence are outside the selected source scope. |\n+| pipavlo82/decentralised | v0.1 historical account retained; no additional source integration selected for v0.2 | Retained v0.1 account; no new maturity claim | This old owned fork is accounted for as historical lineage. Its audited default lacks the current signed engagement/outbox implementation and has no root grant. Current public action semantics are sourced separately from Interpoll1. |\n+| pipavlo82/ERCs | v0.1 optional_interface account retained; no additional source integration selected for v0.2 | Retained v0.1 account; no new maturity claim | The fork is a reference corpus with upstream ERC authorship. It is not Pavlo-owned implementation credit or evidence that a draft ERC is accepted. |\n+| pipavlo82/gas-per-secure-bit | v0.1 methodology account retained; no additional source integration selected for v0.2 | Retained v0.1 account; no new maturity claim | Surface/lane/provenance-aware measurement is reusable methodology. This product does not present old gas results as its own runtime measurements or import vendor records. |\n+| pipavlo82/ml-dsa-65-ethereum-verification | v0.1 optional_interface account retained; no additional source integration selected for v0.2 | Retained v0.1 account; no new maturity claim | The parser stub and experimental PR27 remain research/interface references. Structural parsing is not ML-DSA cryptographic verification; the closed unmerged license PR does not change main. |\n+| pipavlo82/pipavlo82.github.io | v0.1 fixture account retained; no additional source integration selected for v0.2 | Retained v0.1 account; no new maturity claim | The published witness-key format is accounted for as fixture/identity interface history. Real published keys are not trusted by the synthetic product demo. |\n+| pipavlo82/pq-receipt-profile | v0.1 optional_interface account retained; no additional source integration selected for v0.2 | Retained v0.1 account; no new maturity claim | The original product provider/vector interface applies attribution/crypto-agility separation. Real backend absence stays UNSUPPORTED; callback declarations and structural vectors do not establish ML-DSA conformance. |\n+| pipavlo82/pqevm-vector-packs | v0.1 methodology account retained; no additional source integration selected for v0.2 | Retained v0.1 account; no new maturity claim | Hash/count container and source-provenance rules inform fresh synthetic vector admission. Imported operands and missing historical source_commit are not repaired or copied. |\n+| pipavlo82/protected-relation-fixtures | prf-main-award-settlement-native-v02 @ `fac26d2e8346aeab08194343b78c345d235c6935`; prf-downstream-native-dependency-transfer-v02 @ `f525737069dc4cef7741f805d08a988912f4454f` | PINNED_SOURCE / STABLE; REIMPLEMENTED_FROM_SPEC / EXPERIMENTAL | Merged-main native synthetic award relation executes. Open PR14 transfer specification is separately pinned EXPERIMENTAL reimplementation. Preserved negative transfer remains a negative product result. |\n+| pipavlo82/quantum-execution-evidence | v0.1 runtime account retained; no additional source integration selected for v0.2 | Retained v0.1 account; no new maturity claim | Provider-neutral, counts-native and request-versus-observation boundaries support a stochastic-domain adapter. Only fresh synthetic evidence is selected, not live provider captures. |\n+| pipavlo82/r4-saas-api | v0.1 optional_interface account retained; no additional source integration selected for v0.2 | Retained v0.1 account; no new maturity claim | The application-specific ECDSA recovery endpoint remains an optional signature interface. Signature recovery is key control, not authoritative subject membership or execution. |\n+| pipavlo82/receiptos-mvp | v0.1 historical account retained; no additional source integration selected for v0.2 | Retained v0.1 account; no new maturity claim | The HMAC receipt/chain/replay seed is retained as historical methodology. Its symmetric trust and local chain do not establish independent public verification. |\n+| pipavlo82/receiptos-pq-lab | v0.1 optional_interface account retained; no additional source integration selected for v0.2 | Retained v0.1 account; no new maturity claim | Extension/backend contracts, HMAC game lineage and adapter refusal reasons remain optional interfaces. Historical Stealth/ATP captures and vendor material are not imported. |\n+| pipavlo82/recomputable-verification-receipts | v0.1 runtime account retained; no additional source integration selected for v0.2 | Retained v0.1 account; no new maturity claim | Native RVR outcomes and recomputation statuses remain separate behind the adapter. Selected upstream profile implementations retain their own terms and vocabularies. |\n+| pipavlo82/relational-security-invariants | rsi-v02-independent-relation-tests @ `3d3038f90c3dd98e79f948398167c5cc3ef2fdd8` | METHODOLOGY_ONLY / STABLE | Detached expectation, positive-control/non-vacuity and relation discipline only; no RSI runtime or independent-oracle certification. |\n+| pipavlo82/semantic-execution-guard | seg-v02-caller-context-binding-method @ `18f595b537017e5ff7b9074366c3065e877488f9` | METHODOLOGY_ONLY / STABLE | Independent consumer-context and exact semantic-boundary methodology only; no guard, onchain execution or deployment transferred. |\n+| Rohiteswar/Solana-SlotMachine | v0.1 no_useful_capability_found account retained; no additional source integration selected for v0.2 | Retained v0.1 account; no new maturity claim | Bounded issue-only relevance/license/source-tree triage found no implementation, executable finding or receipt adapter useful to this product. The contact is retained in the complete scope inventory, not converted into code contribution credit. |\n+| shentonyan/sealed-bid-award-erc | v0.1 optional_interface account retained; no additional source integration selected for v0.2 | Retained v0.1 account; no new maturity claim | The award/settlement specification remains a separately pinned reference. A bounded synthetic relation does not establish a universal incentive or chain-execution guarantee. |\n+| tapiwamakandigona/zimbet | v0.1 no_useful_capability_found account retained; no additional source integration selected for v0.2 | Retained v0.1 account; no new maturity claim | Bounded issue-only relevance/license/source-tree triage found no implementation, executable finding or receipt adapter useful to this product. The contact is retained in the complete scope inventory, not converted into code contribution credit. |\n+| trustless-ai/agent-sdk | v0.1 fixture account retained; no additional source integration selected for v0.2 | Retained v0.1 account; no new maturity claim | The prospective basis-points fixture adoption and SDK interfaces remain optional test/agent integration references. No live SDK deployment is claimed. |\n+| trustless-ai/ccip-router | v0.1 optional_interface account retained; no additional source integration selected for v0.2 | Retained v0.1 account; no new maturity claim | Exact-byte signed observation transport remains an optional gateway. A signed digest does not re-evaluate TSEI or establish independent vantage/finality. |\n+| trustless-ai/cross-reference-console | v0.1 optional_interface account retained; no additional source integration selected for v0.2 | Retained v0.1 account; no new maturity claim | Signed Cell and attribution/lineage rules remain an optional observation interface. Empty lineage and shared code do not establish independence. |\n+| trustless-ai/pq-agent-binding | v0.1 optional_interface account retained; no additional source integration selected for v0.2 | Retained v0.1 account; no new maturity claim | The original bounded key-ID, half-open validity-window and explicit non-revocation gate is implemented before trusted provider invocation. Complete event-time/earliest-anchor-history evaluation remains unimplemented; superseded R1-R3 semantics remain historical. |\n+| trustless-ai/primitives | v0.1 methodology account retained; no additional source integration selected for v0.2 | Retained v0.1 account; no new maturity claim | Registry discovery remains navigation only. Package-present or runner-declared cannot establish performed semantic execution. |\n+| trustless-ai/recompute-kit | trustless-native-scan-v02 @ `1a37bcaf91918fd8a98f164d97d0fddbc28c6755` | PINNED_SOURCE / EXPERIMENTAL | Native selected main scan/check runner executes; source main is STABLE, product integration EXPERIMENTAL. PR57 was OPEN at the source observation; it merged2026-10-11T22:35:33Z into current main3c3923956200d01ab74c2dcbb49b268739943bda. Newly merged reporter behavior is not selected; the historical-main runtime pin is retained. Shared authorship and review-only evidence remain distinct. |\n+| trustless-ai/semantic-abi | semantic-abi-native-neutral-v02 @ `d15c666dfccff17f7350fe97d2fc7b71cb2cbaee` | PINNED_SOURCE / EXPERIMENTAL | Actual neutral runtime; shared Echo-Merlini implementation and Pavlo semantic-model fixes retained. Generic embedding is a bounded product extension, no private/commercial code. |\n+\n+The original public-source exclusions remain: no private Vértice implementation,\n+provider/user captures, application database, legacy desktop or unrelated vendor\n+subtree is imported. New v0.2 copying is exactly fourteen selected files,\n+including four complete original licenses; see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and the\n+three provenance/v02-*.json records. RSI/SEG and PR14 specification use do not\n+copy source bytes. Source pinning establishes identity, not soundness, authority,\n+production readiness, standard acceptance or revenue allocation."},{"sha":"38773704bea15e2d7fbfa75f01e3abd1bf7f6d87","filename":"LICENSING.md","status":"modified","additions":3,"deletions":1,"changes":4,"blob_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/blob/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/LICENSING.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/raw/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/LICENSING.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/contents/LICENSING.md?ref=396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775","patch":"@@ -4,7 +4,9 @@ New repository-authored material is Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 Pavlo Tvardovskyi\n \n Selected native Crystal, RVR and QEV source bytes are preserved unchanged with their LICENSE/NOTICE and exact file-level Git/SHA256 identities. QEV's nested public neutral Semantic ABI retains Apache-2.0 code and CC0 schema rights. Further exact nested native source/license dependencies retain their own notices. See the corresponding `provenance/*-sources.json` files.\n \n-Original Semantic ABI/PRF/Chronicle/Interpoll/product adapters reimplement public relations. No private Vértice implementation or commercial domain adapter is included. Source ideas from unlicensed default-branch R4/PQ/historical repositories are methodology/specification inputs; their code was not copied. Fresh synthetic fixtures avoid captured third-party datasets.\n+Original v0.1 Semantic ABI/PRF/Chronicle/Interpoll/product adapters reimplement public relations. No private Vértice implementation or commercial domain adapter is included. Source ideas from unlicensed default-branch R4/PQ/historical repositories are methodology/specification inputs; their code was not copied. Fresh synthetic fixtures avoid captured third-party datasets.\n+\n+The v0.2 adapters additionally execute selected unchanged public neutral Semantic ABI (Apache-2.0), recompute-kit (CC0-1.0), Interpoll signed-action (Unlicense) and merged-main PRF award relation (MIT) files. Their original license bytes and exact file identities are retained in `vendor/*-v02`, the three `provenance/v02-*.json` integration records and `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`. Product generic-surface/retry/transfer glue remains separately authored Apache-2.0 material. PRF PR14 transfer semantics are an explicitly experimental public-spec reimplementation; no unmerged PR consumer or captured data is silently relicensed.\n \n Installed npm dependency grants are preserved under `vendor/licenses/` and in `provenance/dependencies.json`. Noble curves/hashes, AJV and other MIT packages retain their MIT notices; fast-uri retains BSD-3-Clause. Package presence or license metadata does not imply semantic verification or conformance.\n "},{"sha":"cf4f23d733e150fe6e12532bdf6cdc77936ae82e","filename":"NOTICE","status":"modified","additions":9,"deletions":0,"changes":9,"blob_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/blob/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/NOTICE","raw_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/raw/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/NOTICE","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/contents/NOTICE?ref=396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775","patch":"@@ -3,3 +3,12 @@ Copyright 2026 Pavlo Tvardovskyi\n \n Selected upstream components retain their own notices and licenses in vendor/.\n See PROVENANCE.md and provenance/sources.json for source identities and contribution boundaries.\n+\n+v0.2 selected native components retain separate grants:\n+trustless-ai/semantic-abi: Apache-2.0, including shared neutral runtime contributions.\n+trustless-ai/recompute-kit: CC0-1.0, including shared checker and runner contributions.\n+Interpoll1/decentralised: Unlicense, selected signed public engagement verifier.\n+pipavlo82/protected-relation-fixtures: MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Pavlo Tvardovskyi.\n+Their unchanged license files remain in the corresponding vendor/*-v02 directories.\n+See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md for exact pins and scope. The product Apache grant\n+does not replace these grants or imply sole authorship of shared upstream code."},{"sha":"5ab91b4fc3a45729b52be205dde571290697430f","filename":"PROVENANCE.md","status":"modified","additions":63,"deletions":2,"changes":65,"blob_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/blob/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/PROVENANCE.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/raw/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/PROVENANCE.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/contents/PROVENANCE.md?ref=396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775","patch":"@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@\n # Provenance\n \n-ReceiptOS Verify is a new local repository. The earlier audit documents remain frozen historical evidence. Existing repositories are public read inputs and were not modified for this implementation. All new code and provenance records are confined here.\n+ReceiptOS Verify's public v0.1.0 base is `62cd3e59c8f568496ed087d55f0aec3d63363b0a`. The v0.2 work is an unpushed local continuation. Earlier audit documents remain frozen historical evidence. Existing upstream repositories are public read inputs and were not modified. All new code and provenance records are confined here.\n \n The [release-candidate audit](RELEASE_AUDIT_v0.1.md) separates original saved build observations from fresh candidate findings, fixes and release checks. Frozen saved reports and original attribution evidence remain unchanged.\n \n@@ -20,7 +20,7 @@ Code, specifications, fixtures, load-bearing tests, security findings, reviews,\n \n Crystal roots, RVR semantic/recompute axes, Semantic ABI declarations, PRF guarantees, Chronicle history and domain adapter results retain native meaning. Independent spec reimplementation is labeled separately from vendored runtime code. Private/commercial Vértice code and system-specific adapters are not selected.\n \n-## Selected implementations and status\n+## Historical v0.1 selected implementations and status\n \n There are 21 named implemented slices, including original methods and interfaces, across 12 registered surfaces: 11 bounded executable relations or admission operations and one ledger interface. Audited capability maturity is 2 STABLE, 9 EXPERIMENTAL and 1 INTERFACE_ONLY. CHRONICLE-ADMISSION checks supplied continuity and exact reference strings; CHRONICLE-ROOTS is a future capability. No Artifact/Collection/Portfolio aggregate roots are constructed or verified by the continuity adapter.\n \n@@ -55,3 +55,64 @@ The CLI product `pack`/`verify-capsule` carrier remains an original schema/tree\n The original PQ authority interface has 41 dedicated admission controls in `tests/pq.test.mjs`. Exact key identity, explicit authority fields, nonnegative safe-integer ordered half-open validity windows and explicit non-revocation are required before a trusted provider is called. Caller-provided authority and a provider callback remain premises; no real ML-DSA backend, complete event-time history or earliest-anchor-history conformance is established.\n \n The original saved full product suite records 251/251 with zero failures, cancellations or skips; the original saved corpus records 30/30 and original saved mutation report records fourteen kills. `provenance/sources.json` retains those exact report digests with historical scope. An earlier concurrent cleanup-control failure also remains preserved. The current release gate and corrected-candidate counts are recorded separately in the [release-candidate audit](RELEASE_AUDIT_v0.1.md).\n+\n+## v0.2 executable integrations\n+\n+The additive `v02Integrations` catalog preserves all 43 historical repository\n+accounts and all 74 original capability records. Current source pins do not\n+rewrite earlier snapshots, historical adoption statements, licensing observations\n+or source authorship. [The v0.2 review report](V0_2_REVIEW_REPORT.md) records actual\n+final validation; no old test count is promoted to a new execution observation.\n+\n+| Capability | Exact selected source | Mode and maturity | Executed boundary |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| Public neutral Semantic ABI | `trustless-ai/semantic-abi@d15c666dfccff17f7350fe97d2fc7b71cb2cbaee` | `PINNED_SOURCE`, `EXPERIMENTAL` integration | Unchanged neutral manifest/linker/evaluator runtime plus explicit product generic-surface projection |\n+| Trustless native scan | `trustless-ai/recompute-kit@1a37bcaf91918fd8a98f164d97d0fddbc28c6755` | `PINNED_SOURCE`; source-main relation `STABLE`, product integration `EXPERIMENTAL` | Native scan-subject-binding checker and bounded runner, not the whole upstream corpus |\n+| Interpoll native authorization | `Interpoll1/decentralised@559e47f2cd2ffcbd8ad38293da89448d8ec3152d` (`master`) | `PINNED_SOURCE`, `EXPERIMENTAL` | Exact native Schnorr action verification; historical admission, server execution and SQL atomicity are not established |\n+| Interpoll retry composition | Same current public default pin | `REIMPLEMENTED_FROM_SPEC`, `EXPERIMENTAL` | Caller-selected intent vs accepted action/retries/supplied observation/trace commitment |\n+| PRF award-settlement relation | `pipavlo82/protected-relation-fixtures@fac26d2e8346aeab08194343b78c345d235c6935` | `PINNED_SOURCE`, bounded merged-main relation `STABLE` | Unchanged native Python relation over fresh synthetic tuples |\n+| PRF downstream preservation | PR14 `f525737069dc4cef7741f805d08a988912f4454f`, `OPEN`, unmerged | `REIMPLEMENTED_FROM_SPEC`, `EXPERIMENTAL` | Product exact native-result/dependency transfer; no PR14 wire/runtime conformance claimed |\n+| RSI test discipline | `pipavlo82/relational-security-invariants@3d3038f90c3dd98e79f948398167c5cc3ef2fdd8` | `METHODOLOGY_ONLY`, selected published method `STABLE` | Detached literal expectations, non-vacuity and preserved positive controls; no RSI runner imported |\n+| SEG consumer boundary | `pipavlo82/semantic-execution-guard@18f595b537017e5ff7b9074366c3065e877488f9` | `METHODOLOGY_ONLY`, selected published method `STABLE` | Separately selected consumer context and semantic substitutions; no onchain execution claim |\n+\n+The generic v0.2 core is original product composition. Its public-spec lineage\n+includes Semantic ABI's structured meaning, RVR's independent claim/replay axes,\n+RSI's relation/expectation separation and SEG's consumer binding. Its new schema,\n+authority policy, evidence packaging and projection are not advertised as native\n+wire conformance with those upstreams. Exact new product files are cataloged in\n+`v02ProductExtensions`.\n+\n+### Contributions and licenses\n+\n+[Semantic ABI evidence](provenance/v02-semantic-abi.json) preserves Pavlo's merged\n+semantic-model fixes alongside Echo-Merlini's neutral runtime implementation and\n+other PR contributors. [Trustless evidence](provenance/v02-trustless.json)\n+separates babyblueviper1's scan implementation, Pavlo's executable witness,\n+review and runner failure-classifier implementation, and the shared runner's\n+other contributors. Review-only activity is not described as original code.\n+\n+[Action/PRF evidence](provenance/v02-actions-prf.json) identifies Pavlo's actual\n+signed-action commit `2cfde5efc3d10b56c73e74723d3f328b77f2fc1f`, durable retry\n+commit `a1eb47653aa7b8f0484ab977d75a5db41d226d02`, main award relation commit\n+`717f04b3216c560949331dfc084e2fa6bb5e95bd` and experimental PR14 implementation\n+commit. Repository ownership is never substituted for path-level authorship.\n+No ownership, revenue allocation or sole authorship is inferred.\n+\n+Fourteen selected v0.2 upstream files are copied unchanged, including their four\n+license files: Apache-2.0 neutral Semantic ABI, CC0-1.0 recompute-kit, Unlicense\n+Interpoll and MIT PRF. [Third-party notices](THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md) and the source\n+fragments preserve those grants and SHA256/Git blob identities. No provider\n+captures, application databases, private Vértice code or upstream secrets were\n+imported. `tools/check-provenance-v2.mjs` mechanically checks the 43-row historical\n+boundary, additive mappings, complete new vendor byte closure and legal files.\n+\n+The frozen source fragments record PR57 as OPEN when the adapter was pinned.\n+Independent release audit at `2026-10-11T23:09:39.173Z` found PR57 merged at\n+`2026-10-11T22:35:33Z`, with head `197c6d26e68f85a117dd12a94924a7f959edaef4`\n+and current main `3c3923956200d01ab74c2dcbb49b268739943bda`. These new\n+observations supplement the historical record; they do not rewrite it or repin\n+runtime. The adapter retains `1a37bcaf91918fd8a98f164d97d0fddbc28c6755`, native\n+contract mode null and product interpretation `MAIN_SELF_GRADING`; newly merged\n+reporter behavior is not selected. PRF PR14 remains OPEN at its exact pin.\n+Current-state evidence and audit-only public vectors retain their CC0 source\n+identity in `reports/release-audit-v0.2/domains/current-main-replay.json`."},{"sha":"6672b0bed8f8481de4ebec90cd276bf89345a951","filename":"README.md","status":"modified","additions":14,"deletions":4,"changes":18,"blob_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/blob/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/README.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/raw/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/README.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/contents/README.md?ref=396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775","patch":"@@ -2,7 +2,11 @@\n \n A local verification product that answers **what supplied evidence is allowed to establish for a caller-selected claim**. It preserves native adapter results and adds a separate, versioned product projection.\n \n-**Local experimental v0.1.** This repository has no remote. Existing upstream repositories remain read-only. No private Vértice implementation is included.\n+**Local v0.2 review build, based on public v0.1.0.** Existing upstream repositories remain read-only. No private Vértice implementation is included. V0.2 is unpushed and has no release tag.\n+\n+ReceiptOS Verify does not answer only whether a receipt is intact. It evaluates what supplied evidence actually establishes for a caller-selected claim, within explicit bounded profiles. The v2 contract keeps claim, subject, artifact, authority, scope, policy/version, time, assumptions and dependencies separate. See [generic boundary](docs/generic-claim-boundary.md), [v0.2 architecture](docs/v0.2-architecture.md) and [v0.2 review report](V0_2_REVIEW_REPORT.md).\n+\n+The [independent v0.2 release audit](RELEASE_AUDIT_v0.2.md) records the frozen candidate, independent findings, separate repairs and exact fresh-checkout results.\n \n The [release-candidate audit](RELEASE_AUDIT_v0.1.md) separates the original saved build reports from fresh candidate findings, fixes and release checks. Original saved counts are historical observations, not the current release verdict.\n \n@@ -17,10 +21,14 @@ npm test\n npm run vectors\n npm run mutations\n npm run check:sources\n+npm run vectors:v2\n+npm run mutations:v2\n+npm run demo:v2\n+npm run check:provenance\n npm start\n ```\n \n-The UI listens only at **http://127.0.0.1:8808/**. Verification runs offline once dependencies are installed. It makes no provider, ledger, scanner or model calls. Do not serve it publicly.\n+The UI listens only at **http://127.0.0.1:8808/**. Verification runs offline once dependencies are installed. It makes no external provider, ledger, scanner-service or model calls. The Trustless adapter runs its pinned deterministic toy scanner locally. Do not serve it publicly.\n \n `node tools/reproduce.mjs V02` runs the saved-artifact control twice in a separate local copy and records exact commands, locks, commit and semantic digests in `reports/local-reproduction.json`. That receipt remains unsigned and does not claim a second independent operator.\n \n@@ -45,14 +53,16 @@ Authenticated evidence for A does not establish the caller-selected claim for B.\n \n ## Implemented surfaces\n \n+V0.2 adds versioned executable integrations: the neutral public Semantic ABI linker/validator, the actual main recompute-kit scan checker and conformance runner, Interpoll's native signed-action verification with exact supplied retry traces, and PRF's main award/settlement relation with a separately experimental downstream preservation rule. Native verdicts, replay and product compatibility remain distinct. These are bounded integrations, not whole-upstream conformance or external execution authentication. The adapter retains its pinned historical-main semantics. Independent release audit found PR57 merged at 2026-10-11T22:35:33Z; current recompute-kit main is `3c3923956200d01ab74c2dcbb49b268739943bda`. That newly merged reporter capability is not imported by this adapter. PRF PR14 remains open and separately experimental.\n+\n - Real pinned native Crystal root verification and RVR digest/replay; separate product Ed25519 signature and Git object closure.\n-- Neutral Semantic ABI compatibility, exact PRF guarantee/dependency preservation, and Chronicle historical/current continuity. These are original public-spec reimplementations with explicit product extensions; PRF14 remains experimental and pinned to its open head.\n+- The v1 compatibility path retains neutral Semantic ABI compatibility, PRF guarantee/dependency preservation and Chronicle historical/current continuity as public-spec reimplementations with explicit product extensions. The v2 native upgrades above remain separately versioned; PRF14 remains experimental and pinned to its open head.\n - Recompute-kit execution/report/grade discipline; Interpoll Schnorr signed action and exact retries.\n - Native QEV finite postprocessing and optional counts/RVR/ReceiptOS capabilities, with provider authenticity unestablished.\n - Original portable product capsules/Merkle proofs, human-readable reports, local inspection UI, full provenance.\n - Experimental crypto-provider/temporal-authority, stochastic replay and Ethereum/XRPL/off-chain anchor boundaries. No ML-DSA verifier or live ledger adapter is claimed.\n \n-The registry contains 12 surfaces: 11 bounded executable relations or admission operations and one ledger interface. Capability maturity is 2 STABLE, 9 EXPERIMENTAL and 1 INTERFACE_ONLY; the raw ledger descriptor still uses EXPERIMENTAL. Chronicle checks supplied continuity and exact reference strings; it does not calculate or verify Artifact/Collection/Portfolio aggregate roots.\n+The unchanged v1 registry contains 12 surfaces: 11 bounded executable relations or admission operations and one ledger interface. Its capability maturity is 2 STABLE, 9 EXPERIMENTAL and 1 INTERFACE_ONLY; the raw ledger descriptor still uses EXPERIMENTAL. The four v2 modules upgrade/version those capability families rather than claiming sixteen independent verifiers. Chronicle checks supplied continuity and exact reference strings; it does not calculate or verify Artifact/Collection/Portfolio aggregate roots.\n \n The main Git artifact profile has six mandatory layers; policy cannot omit subject binding. Domain, guarantee and continuity obligations become required when requested. Product projection evaluates these requirements separately from native roots, signatures and replay.\n "},{"sha":"eba48aa67e91c4e3707574c002697f9ec655182a","filename":"RELEASE_AUDIT_v0.2.md","status":"added","additions":446,"deletions":0,"changes":446,"blob_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/blob/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/RELEASE_AUDIT_v0.2.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/raw/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/RELEASE_AUDIT_v0.2.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/contents/RELEASE_AUDIT_v0.2.md?ref=396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,446 @@\n+# ReceiptOS Verify v0.2 - independent release audit\n+\n+**Frozen candidate verdict: NEEDS_TECHNICAL_FIXES.** The exact frozen candidate\n+passed its canonical suite but independently reproduced defects in mutation\n+coverage classification and caller-requirement admission. Those observations\n+were committed before repair. Repairs and their own fresh reproduction are\n+reported separately; this audit does not retrospectively clear the frozen SHA.\n+\n+**Final repaired verdict: READY_TO_PUBLISH_V0_2**, scoped to the repaired, curated source and declared bounded profiles. Exact fresh-tested commit: `eb942148eeb489db809b39e053ec905105cc3056`; tree: `3fa1cea8387f733cab6a0868acf6060ec958b06d`. Its clean clone contained 1795 tracked regular files. Source-lock: `3c7399a199fcff7fd4f381746d0a22071800065a9798b422fd49a36c0889f4e4` (344 files). The final closure child adds only audit/documentation/evidence and refreshes its own source lock; it does not change tested runtime, schemas, tests, vectors, vendors or dependencies. Its final digest/checks are recorded separately in `reports/release-audit-v0.2/closure.json`, avoiding a self-referential report hash.\n+\n+Actual final gate: **707/707 normal, 707/707 no-opt, 707/707 repeat; 68/68 vectors; 14+14 semantic catalogue kills**. Independent final checks: **57/57 generic/adversarial, 3238/3238 projection, 51/51 domain, 16/16 mutation negative controls, 14/14 fresh demos, 30/30 complete v0.1 semantic report comparisons**. These counts describe separate scopes, not additive unique security properties.\n+\n+No upstream repository was modified. No push, publish, tag, PR or merge was\n+performed. Corrections are bounded defect repairs, not new verification\n+features. Private Vertice implementation remains excluded.\n+\n+## A. Exact frozen candidate identity\n+\n+| Field | Independently observed value |\n+| --- | --- |\n+| Commit | `4888a0584369a91075eb2bdbd9a2ff6b99c46588` |\n+| Tree | `d5a6fb8e47db373e59b6ce5ed021f3e1240a09fc` |\n+| Branch | `feat/v0.2-generic-trustless-boundary` |\n+| Initial git status | CLEAN |\n+| Public v0.1.0 peeled base | `62cd3e59c8f568496ed087d55f0aec3d63363b0a` |\n+| Complete tracked regular-file count | **1028** |\n+| Source-lock SHA-256 | `86cf26a39b103ca32344119c2a5a183d7fcf0616b07257bd356435b2b12fbf2a` |\n+| Dependency-lock SHA-256 | `699f2fc389c8d95ad0e5c7f2ef1b3566152b1f9e5123e2ab49cb5c9d59285023` |\n+| Runtime/tool versions | Node22.15.0; Python3.12.10; npm10.9.2; Bun1.3.14 |\n+\n+[Freeze identity](reports/release-audit-v0.2/freeze/identity.json), [tracked\n+inventory](reports/release-audit-v0.2/freeze/tracked-files.json), [fresh committed\n+inventory](reports/release-audit-v0.2/freeze/fresh-tracked-files.json), clean\n+status/working diff and complete diff/path inventory against v0.1.0 preserve the\n+exact starting state. Every tracked regular file has a SHA-256 entry.\n+\n+Four historical v0.1 stdout working files have final CRLF while their committed\n+blobs use LF under Git attributes. They are disclosed individually in the\n+freeze identity; they were not rewritten. Git/source identity was clean, but\n+original working-byte equality with every Git blob is not claimed. The fresh\n+detached checkout was checked against all 1028 committed regular-file blobs.\n+\n+## B. Fresh canonical reproduction\n+\n+The frozen exact candidate was cloned detached into `work/v02-release-audit`,\n+with its own initially absent npm cache and `npm ci --ignore-scripts`. It did\n+not use development node_modules or cached output receipts. Controllers supply\n+only the documented empty `reports/tmp` parent required by unchanged v1 tests.\n+\n+| Gate | Frozen actual | Final repaired actual |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| Canonical normal suite | 624/624;0fail/skip/cancel/todo | `707/707; 0 fail/skip/cancel/todo` |\n+| Canonical no-opt suite | 624/624;0fail/skip/cancel/todo | `707/707; 0 fail/skip/cancel/todo` |\n+| Complete vectors | 68/68 =30v1+38v2 | `68/68 = 30 v1 + 38 v2` |\n+| Legacy mutation catalogue | 14/14 applied semantic catalogue kills | `14/14; all other outcome counts zero` |\n+| v2 mutation catalogue | 14/14 applied semantic catalogue kills | `14/14; all other outcome counts zero` |\n+| Source lock / provenance / legal checks | PASS | `PASS before/after; fresh dependency install` |\n+| CLI demos and diff check | PASS | `PASS; both CLI demo commands; no source drift` |\n+| UI smoke | Six actual browser verdict states | `Unchanged UI; actual repaired rejection and contradiction confirmed` |\n+\n+[Frozen fresh gate](reports/release-audit-v0.2/gate/summary.json) records command\n+arguments, runtime versions, raw stdout/stderr hashes and actual counts. The\n+catalogue successes do not erase the separate false-coverage negative controls.\n+\n+The first repair `1fecfc2587c5d89d350017a2a7a98ca78e933b9f` reproduced\n+**703/703 tests but only66/68 vectors**: its schema narrowed I03/I08 semantic\n+classifications. This was recorded in checkpoint `40fcaa7` before correction.\n+Correction `3df769c...` adds four regression tests. The final exact curated clone independently reproduced **707/707** normal, no-opt and repeat, with **68/68** unchanged vectors. Full command receipts are in [final fresh gate](reports/release-audit-v0.2/repair/final/summary.json).\n+\n+## C. Generic-boundary audit\n+\n+57/57 independently authored fresh composed probes passed on the frozen\n+candidate, first repair and final exact eb942 clone. Final [core receipts](reports/release-audit-v0.2/repair/independent-final/core/results/summary.json) and [domain receipts](reports/release-audit-v0.2/repair/independent-final/domains/summary.json) retain their actual identities. Fixtures use an audit-owned canonical\n+encoder, Node Ed25519, raw Git object hashing, literal RVR outcomes and directly\n+constructed Crystal roots; no product fixture builder supplied expected product\n+verdicts. Full exact inputs, layer results, literal oracles and digests are in\n+[core receipts](reports/release-audit-v0.2/core/results/summary.json).\n+\n+| Attack | Observed bounded result |\n+| --- | --- |\n+| A01 subject identity | SUBJECT_MISMATCH / CONTRADICTED |\n+| A02 artifact identity | ARTIFACT_MISMATCH / CONTRADICTED |\n+| A03 authority | AUTHORITY_MISMATCH / CONTRADICTED |\n+| A04 scope expansion | SCOPE_MISMATCH / CONTRADICTED |\n+| A05 policy ID and policy version | POLICY_MISMATCH / CONTRADICTED |\n+| A06 claim and subject versions | VERSION_MISMATCH / CONTRADICTED |\n+| A07 time outside half-open interval | TIME_MISMATCH / CONTRADICTED |\n+| A08 absent assumption | INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE; accepted-premise positive succeeds |\n+| A09 missing dependency | DEPENDENCY_MISSING / INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE |\n+| A10 contradicted dependency | DEPENDENCY_CONTRADICTED / CONTRADICTED; exact positive succeeds |\n+| A11 simultaneous mismatches | All observed mismatch reasons remain visible; integrity does not mask them |\n+| A12 absent/null | Required absence/null rejected; optional digest absence contradicts and null rejects |\n+| A13 duplicate/conflicting declarations | Duplicate semantic JSON/dependency/result identities rejected |\n+| A14 formatting/canonicalization | Whitespace/member ordering/CRLF document formatting equivalent; NFC/NFD IDs remain distinct |\n+| A15 same digest, incompatible semantics | Added provider-authentication scope contradicts unchanged digest evidence |\n+\n+Time uses a caller-selected instant, not a live trusted clock. Assumptions and\n+dependency statuses are accepted consumer premises, not externally proven\n+truth. Scope relation is exact canonical equality, not general entailment. Git\n+membership is proven for `git-artifact`; matching commit labels attached to an\n+opaque generic subject are not independently proven Git membership.\n+\n+## D. Semantic ABI audit\n+\n+Public neutral pin `d15c666dfccff17f7350fe97d2fc7b71cb2cbaee` resolves to the\n+observed main. Exact reused paths are `runner/src/classes.mjs`, `linker.mjs`,\n+`manifest.mjs` and `evaluate.mjs`, with their retained Apache-2.0 grant.\n+Integration is PINNED_SOURCE with an EXPERIMENTAL product embedding; public\n+native manifest validation/linking/pair evaluation actually executes.\n+\n+Native result, requested/observed surfaces, expected/observed semantic pairs and\n+overall product verdict remain separate. The product independently checks\n+subject/artifact/authority identity, policy/version, premises and evidence basis\n+that native v0 string fields do not fully represent. Wrong subject/authority,\n+scope expansion, policy/version, missing/contradicted dependencies and same-hash\n+incompatible claims match detached expectations. Native valid linking does not\n+override product incompatibility. No private Vertice dependency was found.\n+\n+The canonical JSON embedding in native v0 string fields is not native manifest\n+interchange conformance or arbitrary semantic entailment.\n+\n+## E. Trustless/recompute-kit audit\n+\n+The candidate executes pinned historical main\n+`1a37bcaf91918fd8a98f164d97d0fddbc28c6755`: real scan_subject_binding.v0 checker\n+and canonical runner, not a package-presence stub. Native check/case identity,\n+verdict, evidence grade, source/corpus pin, execution and replay remain visible.\n+Contract mode is null where the historical artifact lacks it; the wrapper's\n+MAIN_SELF_GRADING interpretation is explicit and is not invented reporter\n+metadata. Product wrapper maturity is EXPERIMENTAL.\n+\n+Fresh positive/negative signed one-document USD cases, divergent saved output,\n+empty corpus, unsupported pin/profile, absent executable evidence and opaque\n+grade controls were exercised. Exit0/package/runner presence do not imply\n+semantic success. REPRODUCED negative stays negative; DRIFT/unavailable source\n+does not become semantic contradiction. Opaque authenticated reports do not\n+satisfy LOCAL_RECOMPUTATION.\n+\n+Read-only audit observation found current main\n+`3c3923956200d01ab74c2dcbb49b268739943bda`: PR57 head\n+`197c6d26e68f85a117dd12a94924a7f959edaef4` merged at\n+`2026-10-11T22:35:33Z`. The earlier source observation remains historical; no\n+runtime repin was made. The candidate does not claim the newly merged reporter\n+protocol. All12 current public scan vectors were executed separately; checker\n+bytes match the selected checker. Explicit removal of an unused toy_scan.rule\n+annotation and selection of the supported historical pin are recorded input\n+adaptations, not current-main reporter support. The current runner's Windows\n+python3 command was unavailable; original RUNNER failure and a separately\n+recorded interpreter adaptation remain distinct observations.\n+\n+## F. Interpoll audit\n+\n+Public master pin `559e47f2cd2ffcbd8ad38293da89448d8ec3152d` and\n+`shared-validation/engagement.js` are exact and Unlicense-covered. Actual native\n+Schnorr verification is combined with original exact supplied retry/observation\n+relations. Pavlo attribution is scoped to signed engagement\n+`2cfde5efc3d10b56c73e74723d3f328b77f2fc1f` and retry\n+`a1eb47653aa7b8f0484ab977d75a5db41d226d02`, not the entire application.\n+\n+Independent I01-I10 controls cover signed intent, target/type/material change,\n+identical retry, mutated retry, duplicate without new execution, absent or wrong\n+observation/attempt, unsupported authority and replay under a different claim.\n+Valid signatures do not authorize a different executed action. Native admission\n+remains NOT_EVALUATED and execution remains OBSERVATION_SUPPLIED: no live\n+Interpoll server, relay, SQL or human observation provenance is established.\n+\n+REQ-01 exposed ignored fresh/server requirements and null outcome defaulting.\n+Closed typed requirements/direct guards repair those failures without adding\n+fresh admission/authentication capabilities. The later I03/I08 correction keeps\n+typed different action-kind requests contradictory and typed unsupported\n+authority namespaces explicitly unsupported; producer validators stay intact.\n+\n+## G. PRF guarantee audit\n+\n+Merged main pin `fac26d2e8346aeab08194343b78c345d235c6935` executes\n+`tools/award_actual_settlement.py` under retained MIT terms. PR14 remains OPEN at\n+`f525737069dc4cef7741f805d08a988912f4454f`; the product transfer rule is an\n+EXPERIMENTAL REIMPLEMENTED_FROM_SPEC relation, not execution of PR14's consumer.\n+\n+P01-P06 independently exercise positive preserved transfer, changed downstream\n+dependency, reproduced native negative with preserved transfer, missing basis,\n+conflicting tuples/results and unsupported policy/evidence demands. Native\n+outcome, REPRODUCED/DIVERGED and PRESERVED/VIOLATED/UNVERIFIABLE are separate.\n+G30 preserves native VIOLATED and transfer PRESERVED while overall remains\n+CONTRADICTED. No chain authenticity or universal economic truth is inferred.\n+Unknown caller policy/evidence keys now reject rather than being ignored.\n+\n+## H. Complete product projection rules\n+\n+[Product table](profiles/product-projection-v2.json) has46 literal cases.\n+[Independent table](reports/release-audit-v0.2/core/results/projection-decision-table.json)\n+contains3238 independently-oracled substitutions, all matching. Ordered rules:\n+\n+| Priority | Condition | Verdict |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| 1 | Malformed representation/inventory/status vocabulary/obligations/support flag | REJECTED_MALFORMED |\n+| 2 | Any supplied layer or nested PRF product is malformed | REJECTED_MALFORMED |\n+| 3 | Any supplied contradiction/violation or separate recomputation semanticOutcome REFUTED | CONTRADICTED |\n+| 4 | Unsupported profile/required layer/required nested PRF projection | UNSUPPORTED_PROFILE |\n+| 5 | Required inability/divergence or required PRF inability | CANNOT_RECOMPUTE |\n+| 6 | Required positive premise unestablished | INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE |\n+| 7 | All guards clear and all required positives established | VERIFIED |\n+\n+Positive admission prerequisites: INPUT=ADMITTED and CANONICALIZATION=VERIFIED.\n+Mandatory: integrity/authenticity/subject VERIFIED, replay REPRODUCED **and**\n+native semantic outcome VERIFIED, evidence SUFFICIENT, compatibility COMPATIBLE.\n+Selected guarantees need PRESERVED, continuity PRESERVED/VERIFIED and domain\n+VERIFIED/PRESERVED. Integrity/authenticity/native PASS never override negative\n+compatibility. A selected nested PRF product must independently succeed.\n+There is no Boolean-truthiness fallback. Tests cover single/pair status axes,\n+optional obligations, native polarity/support combinations, nested six-value\n+PRF products and malformed reports; this is **not** an exhaustive Cartesian\n+product of all fourteen layers or a formal proof of adapter soundness.\n+\n+## I. All 68 vector witnesses\n+\n+[V0_2_VECTOR_WITNESS_MATRIX.md](V0_2_VECTOR_WITNESS_MATRIX.md) and its machine\n+matrix cover every vector, claim, relation, native/product expectations, reason,\n+independent oracle, measured mutant and positive control. Classification:\n+**63 LOAD_BEARING;5 REDUNDANT;0 SELF_REFERENTIAL;0 DECORATIVE;0 UNCLEAR**.\n+68 stored controls do not mean68 independent semantic branches.\n+\n+The five aliases are G09/G01, G10/G05, G19/G04, I01/G13 and I05/G14. V08 shares\n+V01 receipt bytes but adds a deliberate crash setup, so is not redundant.\n+Both generators author literal product expectations rather than calling verify\n+or project to derive them.140 detached literal corpus checks passed. Shared\n+native fixture/verifier construction does not independently prove native\n+canonicalization/crypto; negative substitutions remain product witnesses.\n+Comparators require stated reasons, not an exact closed reason set; native\n+payload expectations are selected constraints, not exhaustive report equality.\n+\n+## J. Both mutation families\n+\n+An independent observer applied all 14 legacy +14 v2 substitutions, verified\n+intended source locations/hashes and exact witness IDs, and preserved positive\n+semantics. All 28 catalogue witnesses were semantic disagreements.26 positives\n+were fully identical excluding execution.argv; two retained identical semantics\n+with disclosed diagnostic differences. Broad mutants removing combined\n+policy/version or multiple scope barriers are not isolated subfield coverage.\n+\n+Zero inventory, unapplied/no-op, outer crash/null and damaged positive controls\n+never counted as successful coverage. Frozen v2 correctly rejects inner-native\n+crash/null. **Frozen v1 incorrectly reported both as KILLED, exit0**, despite\n+unavailable computation rather than semantic refutation. MUT-01 records exact\n+before evidence and independent reproduction. The repair inspects nested\n+execution/output failure and retains the legitimate fixed-fault V08 witness:\n+the same crash is held constant while only false semantic refutation changes.\n+Final rerun receipts: [16 final negative controls](reports/release-audit-v0.2/repair/independent-final/mutations/negative-control-results.json): zero/no-op/unapplied/outer crash/outer null/damaged positive/inner crash/inner null for each family; all KILLED=0, no successful coverage. Function-driver exit0 is not treated as a successful returned gate.\n+\n+## K. Provenance and authorship\n+\n+All 43 historical repositories retain truthful roles in sources.json,\n+PROVENANCE.md and FULL_WORK_REUSE_MAP.md;74 historical capability records remain\n+unchanged. Eight additive integrations across six repositories keep native\n+source, product wrapper and experimental transfer identities separate.\n+51/51 selected unique SHAs resolve;396/396 declared paths/groups exist at pins;\n+18/18 new contribution declarations match changed paths and author metadata.\n+\n+Historical ledger108 entries includes68 ORIGINAL_CODE declarations with commit\n+proof:170 references across161 unique commit endpoints resolve without explicit\n+login mismatch. These prove scoped contributions, not exclusive authorship or\n+per-line ownership. Repository ownership is not authorship. Shared Semantic ABI\n+and Trustless implementation/review roles, Interpoll scoped contributions and\n+PRF native versus open-transfer attribution are distinguished. No revenue\n+percentage is calculated.\n+\n+Public upstream observations are time-scoped to `2026-10-11T23:09:39.173Z`.\n+Current PR57 merged state and selected older-main behavior are both retained;\n+PR14 stays open/experimental. No experimental source is represented as current\n+production main. Exact public observations are in domains/public-source-identities.json\n+and corpus source/path/attribution reports.\n+\n+## L. License and third-party audit\n+\n+Root Apache-2.0 matches official text byte-for-byte, SHA-256\n+`cfc7749b96f63bd31c3c42b5c471bf756814053e847c10f3eb003417bc523d30`.\n+LICENSE/NOTICE/LICENSING/THIRD_PARTY notices preserve selected grants and product\n+glue distinction.91 copied upstream files (77 retained+14new, including four\n+new licenses) match Git blobs/SHA-256 and independently fetched exact-ref bytes.\n+Seven npm packages retain seven legal files. Selected runtime/vendor grants are\n+Apache-2.0,CC0-1.0,Unlicense,MIT and existing BSD-3-Clause; no selected runtime\n+source had absent/pending/conflicting grant. Reimplementations are separately\n+identified; provider captures/vendor material are not silently relicensed.\n+\n+**Audit-capture finding LICENSE-01:** a newly added historical-ledger audit JSON\n+embedded upstream commit patches/source excerpts, some without a clear\n+redistribution grant. This is new audit evidence, not frozen4888 runtime/vendor\n+material; it contradicts an unqualified claim that every newly present source\n+byte is covered. Only the five agent-created post4888 audit commits were curated to retain\n+metadata/path/hash/authorship evidence instead of ambiguous copied patches.\n+Original raw evidence remains in private local audit scratch/bundle. Frozen\n+candidate bytes/commits remain unchanged. Clearance is established by\n+[curation mapping](reports/release-audit-v0.2/capture-license/local-history-curation.json) and [independent curation check](reports/release-audit-v0.2/capture-license/audit02-curation-independent-review.json) plus final tracked-byte/license/source-lock revalidation. A later deletion commit alone would have retained the raw bytes in pushed ancestry; the curation explicitly addresses that history. 1082 patch strings, 4 API body captures and 86 API contents were replaced with metadata/hash records. The exact raw bundle stays unpublished under work/, SHA256 `bdcda1d52ff39859be852c110c32fc010649a24e54268fad1d608ea9669aff3b`. Original raw execution receipts retain their original commit IDs; the old/new mapping does not relabel an execution. All non-report blobs per mapped commit are identical, frozen4888 remains the ancestor, and all raw audit commits/capture blobs are unreachable from the curated branch. No license clearance is inferred solely from the earlier runtime-vendor audit.\n+\n+## M. Determinism\n+\n+Frozen determinism gate passed42 product runs in seven groups plus12 native\n+runs in four groups: normal/repeat/jitless, environment variation, two distinct\n+filesystem paths and native Python optimized execution. Only exact\n+execution.argv paths are excluded from product semantic identity; native\n+results, evidence, policy, grade, reasons, statuses and pins remain included.\n+Operational receipts intentionally retain absolute command paths and timing.\n+\n+Python -I ignores PYTHONHASHSEED; setting that variable is recorded without\n+claiming it changes isolated Python hashing. A separate direct native CLI -O\n+group covers Trustless optimization; bridge -O alone does not optimize its\n+child checker. JSON ordering/whitespace/CRLF document equivalence is separately\n+probed. Artifact byte line endings remain meaningful. Full --jitless HTTP\n+testing is unsupported on Node22 Undici/WebAssembly; full no-opt is the supported\n+alternate. No exhaustive environment/platform portability claim is made.\n+Final repaired determinism evidence: [final determinism](reports/release-audit-v0.2/repair/final/determinism.json): 42 product + 12 native runs, all declared comparisons pass.\n+\n+## N. Malformed/adversarial inputs\n+\n+Fresh probes reject null/{}/[]/wrong roots/empty document, duplicate JSON keys,\n+extra/missing members, malformed/uppercase hashes, oversized bounded identity,\n+document >4MiB, unpaired Unicode, invalid UTF-8, traversal/unsupported URI paths,\n+unsafe integers, exponent underflow, NaN/Infinity, duplicate/conflicting evidence,\n+unknown adapters/profiles/semantic versions/canonicalization. None verifies.\n+Numbers are exact safe integers; hashes are lowercase canonical hex; legal\n+Unicode IDs compare exactly, without NFC/NFD/case aliases.\n+\n+The extra requirement probes found five active domain and six continuity\n+fail-open cases outside those57 passing checks. Closed typed context schemas\n+and direct guards now reject unknown/mistyped fields. Boolean continuity true\n+without envelope proof remains insufficient; false preserves limited continuity;\n+true with independently hashed envelope proves only that supplied envelope.\n+Missing contexts retain safe insufficiency. Valid unselected contexts remain\n+inactive by contract, not counted as a separate authorization claim.\n+\n+## O. UI/CLI claim audit\n+\n+Actual browser observations cover all six product verdicts, with screenshot,\n+text/class/color and selected layer state records:\n+\n+| Scenario | Overall / visual result |\n+| --- | --- |\n+| Exact V01 | VERIFIED; good/green |\n+| G10 intact/authentic but incompatible scope | CONTRADICTED; bad/red; integrity/authenticity remain visibly VERIFIED |\n+| V17 QEV packaging/replay valid, provider unknown | INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE; neutral; provider reason visible |\n+| Isolated D13 checker crash | CANNOT_RECOMPUTE; neutral; no semantic refutation |\n+| Empty-object request | REJECTED_MALFORMED; bad/red |\n+| G17 unsupported profile | UNSUPPORTED_PROFILE; neutral |\n+\n+Editing input invalidates stale verdict and disables saving until verification\n+runs. Request and bundle attachment inputs are visible. Overall verdict\n+dominates separate layer successes. QEV does not display global verified quantum\n+execution when provider authentication is NOT_ESTABLISHED. This static Node UI\n+has no separate framework build; its actual server/start/browser smoke is\n+recorded. These are finite visual checks, not exhaustive accessibility/browser\n+certification. CLI exact outputs preserve component/native statuses and reasons.\n+\n+## P. Fourteen fresh end-to-end demos\n+\n+Full machine-readable input/output index:\n+[demos/index.json](reports/release-audit-v0.2/demos/index.json).\n+\n+| Demo | Fresh scenario | Actual bounded outcome |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| D1 | Independently signed commit A, request A | VERIFIED |\n+| D2 | Same receipt, request B | CONTRADICTED |\n+| D3 | Semantic ABI scope mismatch | CONTRADICTED |\n+| D4 | Semantic ABI authority mismatch | CONTRADICTED |\n+| D5 | Real pinned Trustless checker, compatible request | Native positive retained; VERIFIED |\n+| D6 | Same native result, incompatible request | Native result unchanged; CONTRADICTED |\n+| D7 | Exact native-signed Interpoll action | Supplied exact execution relation VERIFIED |\n+| D8 | Mutated retry under same signed intent | CONTRADICTED |\n+| D9 | Native PRF positive and retained downstream relation | PRESERVED / VERIFIED |\n+| D10 | Changed downstream dependency | VIOLATED / CONTRADICTED |\n+| D11 | Valid packaging and reproduced native negative | REPRODUCED negative; CONTRADICTED |\n+| D12 | Empty evidence | INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE |\n+| D13 | Actual isolated checker crash | CANNOT_RECOMPUTE |\n+| D14 | Unsupported profile | UNSUPPORTED_PROFILE |\n+\n+D13 intentionally faults only a disposable copy. Initial controller failures\n+are retained and not counted as product outcomes. Fresh domain construction's\n+initial EUR grammar error and current-main runner-controller mistake are also\n+retained separately, not semantic kills or successful verifier observations.\n+Final repaired demo rerun: [14 final fresh demos](reports/release-audit-v0.2/repair/independent-final/demos/index.json), all at exact eb942 source; D13 records its explicit disposable bridge fault.\n+\n+## Q. v0.1 regression comparison\n+\n+All 30 original vectors were run at public v0.1.0 `62cd3e59...` and frozen v0.2.\n+30/30 complete semantic reports match after excluding only execution.argv host\n+paths; native results, grades, reasons and statuses remain included. The\n+original vector inputs and expectations remain unchanged. Exact per-vector\n+reports/hashes are in [regression summary](reports/release-audit-v0.2/regression/summary.json).\n+Repairs do not alter v1 verifier/schema semantics; the legacy mutation harness\n+correction is assurance infrastructure, not changed product verdicts. Final canonical vector gate passes all 30 original plus38 v2 controls; [final full semantic comparison](reports/release-audit-v0.2/repair/independent-final/regression-final.json) again matches all 30 fresh v0.1 reports.\n+\n+## R. Ranked findings\n+\n+| ID | Severity | Demonstrated defect/issue | Disposition |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| MUT-01 | HIGH | Legacy v1 harness counted newly introduced inner checker crash/null output as successful semantic kill | Nested failure classification repaired; fixed-fault V08 preserved; 16 final controls reject false coverage |\n+| REQ-01 | HIGH | Five active Interpoll/PRF unknown or mistyped consumer requirements were dropped while overall VERIFIED | Typed closed contexts and direct guards; exact before/after evidence retained |\n+| CONT-01 | MEDIUM | Six malformed/unknown continuity requirements yielded VERIFIED with whole envelope NOT_ESTABLISHED | Typed closed continuity admission; Boolean controls retained |\n+| REG-01 | MEDIUM | First repair narrowed I03/I08 into malformed instead of contradicted/unsupported | Separate pre-correction checkpoint; minimally restored typed semantic classifications, four new regressions |\n+| LICENSE-01 | HIGH | New audit JSON embedded ambiguous-grant upstream patches/source excerpts | Metadata-only curation limited to own post4888 audit commits; closed; raw commits/blobs excluded from curated reachable ancestry |\n+| DOC-01 | LOW | files-not-reused.md kept stale no-copy/no-execution wording for now-vendored native files | Scoped documentation correction after discovery |\n+| DOC-02 | INFO | PR57 merged after original source snapshot; selected old main is not current-main reporter behavior | Current observation documented; selected source pin preserved |\n+| SCOPE-01 | INFO | Valid unselected adapter/guarantee context is inactive under documented activation rules | Earlier orphan suspicion corrected; no activation feature added |\n+\n+No BLOCKER-level runtime bypass or ten-dimension compatibility promotion was\n+independently demonstrated. This does not mean no untested defect exists. Green\n+tests never override the explicit HIGH/MEDIUM reproductions.\n+\n+## S. Fix chronology and before/after evidence\n+\n+1. Frozen identity and fresh624/68/14+14 gate were captured first.\n+2. Discovery checkpoint `dde5419f453969ae33b9e88b3151dba3e370f196` records exact\n+   before findings and inputs before technical repair.\n+3. Repair `1fecfc2587c5d89d350017a2a7a98ca78e933b9f` adds closed typed optional\n+   requirements, direct guards, nested v1 mutation failure checks and meaningful\n+   regressions; no native source repin, v1 schema change or vector rewrite.\n+4. Independent41 exact before-input replays pass after repair; original57 and\n+   independent3238 projection checks pass on its fresh exact clone. New composed\n+   requirement tests are **43**, direct-context tests28 and mutation controls8;\n+   earlier prose saying44 requirement tests was an arithmetic error, not an\n+   observed TAP count. Canonical actual703/703 was correct.\n+5. The66/68 vector regression was committed at `40fcaa7` before correcting it.\n+   `3df769c4d873d6f354d1627a97967eec645bd727` restores typed Interpoll mismatch\n+   classifications with four additional tests. Final fresh gate passes707/707 in all three modes and68/68 vectors.\n+6. Metadata-only audit-evidence curation preserves frozen4888 and raw private\n+   before evidence. Exact final tested identity, curation mapping and source-lock fields above come from actual command/blob receipts.\n+\n+The local raw audit commits above remain in the unpublished evidence bundle. Their sanitized equivalents are a9800bbb... (discovery), 2c602f64... (technical repair), e719f2dd... (regression checkpoint), b97201fe... (schema correction), and eb942148... (independent evidence). Exact full mappings and raw/sanitized byte hashes are in the curation receipt. Only audit capture metadata differs for each pair.\n+\n+No meaningless feature/style cleanup or upstream modification was performed.\n+Any final report/evidence-only closure must identify the exact tested runtime\n+commit and disclose that its own child SHA is not self-embedded.\n+\n+## T. Final verdict and release boundary\n+\n+**Frozen4888 candidate: NEEDS_TECHNICAL_FIXES.**\n+\n+Final repaired recommendation: **READY_TO_PUBLISH_V0_2**. All demonstrated technical defects, the repair regression, false release wording and audit-capture publication defect are closed in separate documented steps. No unresolved demonstrated HIGH/MEDIUM defect remains within the tested contract. The frozen4888 candidate itself must not be published as if cleared.\n+\n+Readiness is for the bounded experimental v0.2 product and its\n+declared interfaces, not production security certification, independent human\n+operator reproduction, full upstream conformance, real provider/hardware or\n+server/chain authenticity, arbitrary entailment, live ledger finality or actual\n+PQ cryptographic conformance. XRPL remains an interface boundary only. No push\n+or publication is authorized or performed by this audit.\n+\n+Final verdict: READY_TO_PUBLISH_V0_2"},{"sha":"3d52527a7b071005cb3aa3c0926927bba7ad3e6e","filename":"THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md","status":"added","additions":68,"deletions":0,"changes":68,"blob_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/blob/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/raw/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/contents/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md?ref=396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,68 @@\n+# Third-party notices and source boundaries\n+\n+The root Apache-2.0 grant covers new product-authored material. The selected\n+upstream components below retain their own grants, notices and attribution.\n+Copied license files are distributed as source bytes; this document supplements\n+them rather than replacing their terms. Git ownership does not establish sole\n+authorship.\n+\n+## v0.2 selected native files\n+\n+| Source | Exact source pin | Copied paths | Grant / retained file |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| `trustless-ai/semantic-abi` | `d15c666dfccff17f7350fe97d2fc7b71cb2cbaee` | `runner/src/{classes,evaluate,linker,manifest}.mjs` and license | Apache-2.0; `vendor/semantic-abi-v02/LICENSE` |\n+| `trustless-ai/recompute-kit` | `1a37bcaf91918fd8a98f164d97d0fddbc28c6755` | `tools/run_conformance.py`, `conformance/scan-subject-binding-v0/{scan_check.py,README.md,suite.json}` and license | CC0-1.0; `vendor/recompute-kit-v02/LICENSE` |\n+| `Interpoll1/decentralised` | `559e47f2cd2ffcbd8ad38293da89448d8ec3152d` | `shared-validation/engagement.js` and license | Unlicense; `vendor/interpoll-v02/LICENSE` |\n+| `pipavlo82/protected-relation-fixtures` | `fac26d2e8346aeab08194343b78c345d235c6935` | `tools/award_actual_settlement.py` and license | MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Pavlo Tvardovskyi; `vendor/prf-v02/LICENSE` |\n+\n+These are fourteen files in total, including four license files. Raw SHA256,\n+Git blob identities and exact source/product paths are preserved in\n+`provenance/v02-semantic-abi.json`, `provenance/v02-trustless.json` and\n+`provenance/v02-actions-prf.json`, and consolidated in `provenance/sources.json`.\n+The selected source trees contained no additional root or nested NOTICE/COPYING\n+file applicable to these selected v0.2 files at inspection time. Original file\n+headers and the full copied licenses remain unchanged.\n+\n+Semantic ABI's neutral runner has shared implementation history including\n+Echo-Merlini, with Pavlo's merged semantic-model fixes separately evidenced.\n+Recompute-kit's checker/runner retain babyblueviper1, Pavlo, Merlini/Echo and\n+zexoverz contribution boundaries. Public review/witness evidence is not converted\n+into sole checker authorship. Interpoll's selected signed-action implementation\n+and PRF's award relation have path-level Pavlo-authored commit evidence in the\n+action/PRF fragment; no attribution to the entire Interpoll application is made.\n+\n+## Experimental specification reuse\n+\n+PRF PR14 at `f525737069dc4cef7741f805d08a988912f4454f` remained open and unmerged\n+when inspected. Its public MIT specification informed the original bounded\n+product guarantee-transfer relation. Its Python consumer, adapters, schema and\n+source-derived fixture expectations are not copied or executed here. That\n+relationship is `REIMPLEMENTED_FROM_SPEC`, not a native dependency or main\n+behavior claim.\n+\n+Interpoll's application outbox and database/relay implementation are public\n+read-only specification/behavior inputs. Their code and user data are not copied.\n+RSI/SEG provide public relation and consumer-context methodology only. These\n+relationships establish no runtime, deployment or standards conformance claim.\n+\n+## Existing v0.1 retained components\n+\n+Crystal, generic RVR, QEV and Moth nested source licenses and notices remain\n+unchanged in `vendor/crystal`, `vendor/rvr`, `vendor/qev` and `vendor/qev_moth`.\n+Exact selected byte/grant records remain in `provenance/native-sources.json`,\n+`provenance/qev-sources.json` and `provenance/qev-moth-sources.json`.\n+QEV's nested neutral Semantic ABI code is Apache-2.0 and its selected schema\n+dedication is CC0-1.0. Nested source pins differ where documented; no historical\n+component is silently upgraded by the v0.2 source selection.\n+\n+Installed npm dependencies retain exact notices under `vendor/licenses` and\n+`provenance/npm-licenses.json`: noble curves/hashes, AJV, fast-deep-equal,\n+json-schema-traverse and require-from-string use MIT; fast-uri uses BSD-3-Clause.\n+The product does not relicense those packages or infer conformance from their\n+presence. No new npm dependency was added for the four v0.2 native slices.\n+\n+No private/commercial Vértice implementation, external production capture,\n+provider/user dataset, credentials or unpublished operational key was imported\n+for v0.2. Fresh synthetic fixtures and deliberately public test keys are identified\n+as such. The source catalog and full reuse map retain all 43 historical audit\n+repository accounts without inventing additional transferred capability."},{"sha":"0109bda36dab95856ba603c7025f090aa2a2c98e","filename":"V0_2_REVIEW_REPORT.md","status":"added","additions":227,"deletions":0,"changes":227,"blob_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/blob/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/V0_2_REVIEW_REPORT.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/raw/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/V0_2_REVIEW_REPORT.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/contents/V0_2_REVIEW_REPORT.md?ref=396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,227 @@\n+# ReceiptOS Verify v0.2 review report\n+\n+Recommendation: **READY_FOR_V0_2_RELEASE_AUDIT**.\n+\n+This is a local review build, version `0.2.0-dev.0`, not a published v0.2 release or an independent security certification. The original v0.1 verification path remains the regression baseline. All upstream repositories were used read-only. No push, PR, merge, release, tag modification, private Vértice implementation or live provider/ledger job was performed.\n+\n+## A. Exact public base\n+\n+| Identity | Mechanically observed value |\n+| --- | --- |\n+| Public repository | `pipavlo82/receiptos-verify` |\n+| Main and peeled v0.1.0 | `62cd3e59c8f568496ed087d55f0aec3d63363b0a` |\n+| Public tree | `8a5de5a3735e04f3f45cf164b59da17289693bc2` |\n+| Annotated tag object | `d2226e56a935fc68e1571fa805468d8e1cadb69f` |\n+| Original worktree | Clean before changes |\n+| Original source lock | 222 files; `bd6ad5d4640823ab55458777f93aa5f7999107415fe4550c3d99cbe9b0eb54f6` |\n+| Original package lock | `34c5ead1add79a374494eba5d51966d5557f2109373d1a0ab9bc01ebbb5e307c` |\n+\n+The historical `750a9b...` and rejected `33d8ee...` candidates were not substituted for the public tag. A fresh exact-base worktree reproduced **275/275 tests, 30/30 vectors and 14/14 applied semantic kills**. Its 627 tracked regular files were inventoried and hashed. See [base gate](reports/v0.2/base/summary.json), [base file inventory](reports/v0.2/base/tracked-files.json) and [current public reference observation](reports/v0.2/public-base-identity.json).\n+\n+The v0.1 bare checkout requires an initially empty `reports/tmp` parent before its original Git tests register. The external controllers create only that empty scratch directory. Four historical local stdout files retain CRLF while their public Git blobs have LF, as already recorded in the publication closure. This work leaves those frozen files untouched; it does not claim original-working-byte equality with every public blob. [The preservation inventory](reports/v0.2/unchanged-v01-artifacts.json) discloses all 4 such differences and verifies the original tracked Git identities. All original tests, schemas and vectors remain byte-identical.\n+\n+## B. Branch and tested implementation\n+\n+| Identity | Value |\n+| --- | --- |\n+| Local branch | `feat/v0.2-generic-trustless-boundary` |\n+| Freshly tested implementation commit | `57067b18dd2e5c1aae9ad47476bece6e0aa51cf7` |\n+| Tested tree | `8ae49a0381339e87062e724f50e5d98197bd8a94` |\n+| Fresh checkout | `C:\\Users\\msi\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-10-11\\files-pasted-by-the-user-mission\\work\\v02-final` |\n+| Initial fresh status | `CLEAN` |\n+| Fresh tracked regular files | 974 |\n+| Implementation source lock | `49ec1e4e79a40844013fe8180a7f1b8cd2a03ffadf6c0c2c821f34d206f66200` |\n+| v0.2 dependency lock | `699f2fc389c8d95ad0e5c7f2ef1b3566152b1f9e5123e2ab49cb5c9d59285023` |\n+\n+This report and fresh evidence are added in a documentation/evidence-only child commit. That closure's own SHA is intentionally not embedded in its contents, which would be self-referential; the final chat response identifies the actual closure HEAD. No runtime, test, schema, profile, vector, native/vendor or dependency bytes change after the exact implementation above was reproduced. Final source-lock refresh accounts for this report. [Fresh gate](reports/v0.2/fresh/summary.json) records the independently checked commit/tree and every exact command.\n+\n+## C. Files changed\n+\n+The implementation changes 367 tracked paths, including retained raw evidence. [Complete path inventory and numstat](reports/v0.2/implementation-files-changed.json) give every addition/change relative to the public tag.\n+\n+| Area | Concrete change |\n+| --- | --- |\n+| Core and schemas | Separate request/bundle/report v2 admission; generic surface relation; signing domain; evidence sufficiency; finite projection |\n+| Adapters | Native Semantic ABI, Trustless scan, Interpoll signature/trace and PRF main relation plus bounded transfer |\n+| Profiles/corpus | 46 literal projection cases, G01–G30 and I01–I08; M01–M14 |\n+| Tests/tools | Additive tests, strict mutation output controls, unique isolation copies, demos and determinism receipts |\n+| CLI/server/UI | Version dispatch, v2 demos and G/I controls; visible request/bundle JSON file inputs; established branding retained |\n+| Provenance/legal | Additive pins, attribution, fourteen exact selected vendor/legal files, third-party notices; no dependency added |\n+| Documentation | Generic boundary, adapters, architecture, projection, guarantee and complete witness matrix |\n+\n+Original v1 test/schema/vector/report Git blobs and root LICENSE are unchanged. The v1 verifier has additive schema dispatch; corpus isolation gains unique scratch names without changing relation expectations. Historical generated reports were not overwritten.\n+\n+## D. New schema and compatibility relation\n+\n+Request v2 explicitly carries `claim`, `subject`, `scope`, `authority`, `policy`, `version`, `time`, `assumptions`, `dependencies`, `requested_guarantees`, `evidence`, `evidence_requirements`, `verification_profile` and adapter selection. The signed evidence has a separately declared surface. Neither is replaced by the other or by a digest.\n+\n+Claim identity/kind/parameters; subject identity/version; artifact digest and optional Git identities; authority ID/class; exact structured scope; policy ID/version; claim version; safe half-open time applicability; assumptions; dependencies and evidence basis are checked separately. The four compatibility outcomes are `COMPATIBLE`, `CONTRADICTED`, `INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE`, `UNSUPPORTED`. All eleven required reason families are implemented, including missing versus contradicted dependencies.\n+\n+The current relation is exact structured compatibility plus explicit independently caller-accepted premises, not arbitrary logical entailment. Unicode IDs compare exactly; absent is not null. Native input/scope binding prevents a producer from adding an unsupported guarantee to a digest or scanner declaration. Only actually committed supported attachment roles and completed native execution supply accepted evidence basis. A matched hash cannot establish authority, broaden scope or override an incompatible declaration.\n+\n+Current executable positive v2 paths require a trusted Ed25519 producer key, authority ID/key binding and the accepted `INDEPENDENT_RECOMPUTATION` class. This is local consumer authority acceptance, not provider authentication or an external trust registry. Assumptions and dependency status are caller premises whose external truth this verifier does not establish.\n+\n+See [contract](docs/generic-claim-boundary.md), [schema](schemas/request-v2.schema.json), [surface schema](schemas/claim-surface.schema.json) and [architecture](docs/v0.2-architecture.md). Original v1 inputs/signatures retain their own schema/domain; v1 capsules are not silently relabeled v2.\n+\n+## E. Executable adapter inventory\n+\n+The v2 registry contains **8 versioned surfaces: 7 bounded executable/admission relations and 1 interface**. Its capability maturity is 2 STABLE, 5 EXPERIMENTAL and 1 INTERFACE_ONLY. The preserved v1 registry's 12 overlapping surfaces are not added to this as twenty independent verifiers.\n+\n+| Surface | Actual executed relation | Product maturity / boundary |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| Crystal | Pinned native Bun receipt-root verifier | STABLE narrow root relation; excludes top-level anchor metadata |\n+| RVR | Pinned Python digest predicate and saved-artifact replay | STABLE bounded SHA256_EQUALS; replay distinct from native polarity |\n+| Semantic ABI | Unchanged neutral manifest validator, linker and optional pair evaluator | EXPERIMENTAL product embedding; expected pair caller-selected, observed pair independent |\n+| Trustless | Main scan_subject_binding.v0 native checker and canonical conformance runner | Main source STABLE; product wrapper EXPERIMENTAL; deterministic toy scan, not a production scanner |\n+| Interpoll | Unchanged native Schnorr engagement verifier plus exact supplied retry/observation relation | EXPERIMENTAL; supplied trace, not proof of live server/SQL execution |\n+| PRF | Unchanged main award/settlement Python relation plus original downstream rule | EXPERIMENTAL composition; main tuple relation and PR14-inspired transfer labeled separately |\n+| Chronicle | Preserved bounded supplied-entry/reference continuity relation | EXPERIMENTAL; no Artifact/Collection/Portfolio aggregate-root computation |\n+| Ledger | Off-chain/Ethereum/XRPL boundary | INTERFACE_ONLY; no live chain/finality implementation |\n+\n+Full pins, vocabularies, required evidence and limits are in [adapter inventory](reports/v0.2/adapter-inventory.json) and the adapter documentation. QEV/PQ/stochastic remain optional v1 capabilities; they are not falsely claimed as generic-v2 ports. No package presence or runner declaration is called executed semantic success.\n+\n+## F. Complete test gate\n+\n+| Run | Actual tests | Pass | Fail / skip / cancel / todo |\n+| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |\n+| Fresh public v0.1 baseline | 275 | 275 | 0 / 0 / 0 / 0 |\n+| v0.2 normal | 624 | 624 | 0 / 0 / 0 / 0 |\n+| v0.2 repeat | 624 | 624 | 0 / 0 / 0 / 0 |\n+| v0.2 Node --no-opt | 624 | 624 | 0 / 0 / 0 / 0 |\n+| Exact implementation fresh clone, own dependencies/cache | 624 | 624 | 0 / 0 / 0 / 0 |\n+\n+The 275 baseline tests remain included in the 624 total; repeated observations are not added as coverage. New test count is 349. Runtime observations: Node 22.15.0, Python 3.12.10, npm 10.9.2, Bun 1.3.14. The fresh clone used its own seven locked npm packages, `npm ci --ignore-scripts`, an initially absent install cache and no parent dependency resolution. Commands, raw byte hashes and inventories are retained in [local gate](reports/v0.2/local-gate.json), [normal](reports/v0.2/normal-tests.json), [repeat](reports/v0.2/repeat-tests.json), [no-opt](reports/v0.2/no-opt-tests.json) and [fresh gate](reports/v0.2/fresh/summary.json).\n+\n+Full `--jitless` is unsupported for these HTTP tests on this Node build because it disables the WebAssembly required by Undici's parser. The earlier actual partial run (534 registered, 531 passed, three module failures) remains retained; it is not reported green. Full `--no-opt` passes, selected product CLI jitless paths pass, and the native Python relations are separately compared under `-O`.\n+\n+Two earlier complete modes were incorrectly launched in the same checkout concurrently and collided on original fixed test scratch paths. Actual failure logs are retained. Sequential final normal/no-opt/repeat runs pass; the recommended orchestration uses sequential modes or different checkouts. No original test was weakened to hide the collision. See [assessment](reports/v0.2/parallel-gate-failures/assessment.json).\n+\n+## G. Vector corpus and independent expectation discipline\n+\n+**68/68 vectors pass: unchanged V01–V30 plus 38 new vectors (G01–G30, I01–I08).** Inputs, layer expectations, exact reason witnesses, native assertions, paired positives and source hashes are committed. Expected product/layer outcomes are literal declarations, never `expected := verify(actual)`.\n+\n+The [complete witness matrix](docs/v0.2-vector-mutation-witnesses.md) accounts for every new vector, oracle boundary, semantic overlap and exact input hash. G13/I01 and G14/I05 are deliberate domain/cross-domain aliases, not independent coverage. G10 includes a deliberately narrower declared scope and therefore also has the independently checked primitive-scope constraint; it is not overstated as an isolated M02 witness. Fixture construction/signing/canonical helpers are shared with the product, so this is detached semantic expectation discipline, not a wholly independent implementation of every byte primitive.\n+\n+G29 prevents an authenticated opaque scanner report from being graded as local recomputation. G30 demonstrates RVR positive plus PRF native negative/reproduced and transfer PRESERVED: overall remains CONTRADICTED. [Observed corpus](reports/v0.2/vectors.json) includes full reports and all comparisons.\n+\n+## H. Mutation and explicit negative controls\n+\n+**Original catalogue: 14/14 applied semantic kills. New catalogue: 14/14 applied semantic kills.** Each has zero survived, crashed, invalid-output, not-applied, broken-positive or invalid-baseline outcomes. These are two versioned inventories, not a claim of 28 independent defect classes. [v1 regression](reports/v0.2/regression-mutations.json) and [v2 mutations](reports/v0.2/mutations.json) record exact before/after source hashes, intended substitutions, native/process results, witnesses and preserved positives.\n+\n+| New mutant | Semantic defect | Witness / positive |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| M01 | Ignore authority | G04 / G01 |\n+| M02 | Ignore scope | G05 / G01 |\n+| M03 | Ignore policy version | G06 / G01 |\n+| M04 | Ignore dependency presence | G07 / G23 |\n+| M05 | Ignore dependency contradiction | G08 / G23 |\n+| M06 | Compare evidence subject to itself | G03 / G01 |\n+| M07 | Let native PASS bypass compatibility | G11 / G24 |\n+| M08 | Promote reproduced negative | G12 / G24 |\n+| M09 | Accept material retry mutation | G14 / G13; I05/I04 additional domain controls |\n+| M10 | Promote PRF UNVERIFIABLE to PRESERVED | G21 / G15 |\n+| M11 | Ignore requested claim version | G22 / G01 |\n+| M12 | Let integrity override contradiction | G18 / G01 |\n+| M13 | Upgrade opaque authenticated grade | G29 / G24 |\n+| M14 | Hide negative nested PRF projection | G30 / G15 |\n+\n+The harness refuses zero inventory; unapplied and no-op substitutions become NOT_APPLIED, actual process/native crashes become CRASHED, invalid host/native output becomes INVALID_OUTPUT, and damaged positive controls become CONTROL_BROKEN. None counts as semantic coverage. A well-formed host CANNOT_RECOMPUTE wrapping invalid native JSON is also not a kill. Eight explicit mutation control tests pass, alongside original v1 hostile inventories. [Named control evidence](reports/v0.2/negative-control-test-evidence.json) links actual TAP assertions.\n+\n+Empty evidence, unsupported adapter/profile, wrong claim/authority/scope/policy, missing/contradicted dependencies, absent/null/extra/duplicate fields, invalid UTF-8/JSON, unsafe numbers, accessors, sparse arrays and malformed projection/report boundaries are exercised in the canonical suite and corpus. They cannot establish VERIFIED. File/URI/executable paths are fixed product operations, never evidence-selected network or command execution.\n+\n+## I. Product projection decision table\n+\n+[Machine-readable projection table](profiles/product-projection-v2.json) contains 46 literal cases. [Projection documentation](docs/product-projection.md) defines finite status vocabularies and exact required successes. Order:\n+\n+| Priority | Guard | Result |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| 1 | Malformed layer/obligation representation, inventory or support flag | REJECTED_MALFORMED |\n+| 2 | Any admitted layer or nested PRF product is malformed | REJECTED_MALFORMED |\n+| 3 | Any supplied contradiction/violation or refuted native semantics | CONTRADICTED |\n+| 4 | Unsupported required profile/surface | UNSUPPORTED_PROFILE |\n+| 5 | Required computation unavailable/diverged | CANNOT_RECOMPUTE |\n+| 6 | Any required positive premise unestablished | INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE |\n+| 7 | Every required success established and all guards clear | VERIFIED |\n+\n+Integrity, authenticity, subject binding, replay with separate positive native polarity, evidence sufficiency and semantic compatibility are mandatory even for an empty consumer-required-layer list. Guarantee, continuity and Interpoll domain requirements are added when applicable. A supplied contradiction is not ignored just because its layer was optional. Nested PRF product projection is validated separately from transfer PRESERVED/VIOLATED/UNVERIFIABLE. No Boolean truthiness, native PASS, signature, hash, exit zero or REPRODUCED fallback exists.\n+\n+## J. Five end-to-end demos\n+\n+Fresh synthetic inputs are built without taking expected verdicts from the implementation. Demo C executes the real pinned main recompute-kit checker/runner over fresh synthetic scanner input; it is not a captured external scan. Native runner PASS and scanner NO_FINDING remain distinct.\n+\n+| Demo | Integrity | Authenticity | Subject | Replay | Compatibility | Guarantee | Product |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| A / matching | VERIFIED | VERIFIED | VERIFIED | REPRODUCED | COMPATIBLE | NOT_REQUESTED | **VERIFIED** |\n+| A / wrong_commit | VERIFIED | VERIFIED | CONTRADICTED | REPRODUCED | CONTRADICTED | NOT_REQUESTED | **CONTRADICTED** |\n+| B / wrong_scope | VERIFIED | VERIFIED | VERIFIED | REPRODUCED | CONTRADICTED | NOT_REQUESTED | **CONTRADICTED** |\n+| C / compatible | VERIFIED | VERIFIED | VERIFIED | REPRODUCED | COMPATIBLE | NOT_REQUESTED | **VERIFIED** |\n+| C / incompatible | VERIFIED | VERIFIED | VERIFIED | REPRODUCED | CONTRADICTED | NOT_REQUESTED | **CONTRADICTED** |\n+| D / matching | VERIFIED | VERIFIED | VERIFIED | REPRODUCED | COMPATIBLE | NOT_REQUESTED | **VERIFIED** |\n+| D / mutated_retry | VERIFIED | VERIFIED | VERIFIED | REPRODUCED | COMPATIBLE | NOT_REQUESTED | **CONTRADICTED** |\n+| E / preserved | VERIFIED | VERIFIED | VERIFIED | REPRODUCED | COMPATIBLE | PRESERVED | **VERIFIED** |\n+| E / violated | VERIFIED | VERIFIED | VERIFIED | REPRODUCED | COMPATIBLE | VIOLATED | **CONTRADICTED** |\n+\n+Full inputs/outputs: [demo source](tools/demos-v2.mjs), [complete reports](reports/v0.2/demos.json), [fresh CLI output](reports/v0.2/fresh/cli-v2.stdout). Demo A's identical receipt cannot establish commit B. Demo B's scope mismatch remains negative despite integrity/authenticity. Demo C preserves native output across compatible/incompatible caller surfaces. Demo D's second retry materially changes signed intent. Demo E checks a separately caller-selected PRF tuple/dependency relation.\n+\n+Additional G30 control preserves native `VIOLATED / amount_mismatch`, replay REPRODUCED and transfer PRESERVED while overall is CONTRADICTED. No negative result is promoted to success.\n+\n+## K. Provenance and attribution changes\n+\n+All **43 repository accounts and 74 historical source entries** are preserved by fingerprint and additive mapping. Eight new integration records cover six source repositories; three source fragments retain source paths, trees, licenses, product dependencies and exact path-level contribution evidence. Ownership is not treated as authorship, and shared Semantic ABI work is not attributed solely to Pavlo.\n+\n+| Integration | Exact source SHA | Mode / maturity |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| Semantic ABI neutral native | d15c666dfccff17f7350fe97d2fc7b71cb2cbaee | PINNED_SOURCE / EXPERIMENTAL product embedding |\n+| recompute-kit main scan | 1a37bcaf91918fd8a98f164d97d0fddbc28c6755 | PINNED_SOURCE / EXPERIMENTAL wrapper, STABLE main source |\n+| Interpoll native signature | 559e47f2cd2ffcbd8ad38293da89448d8ec3152d | PINNED_SOURCE / EXPERIMENTAL |\n+| Interpoll exact retry trace | 559e47f2cd2ffcbd8ad38293da89448d8ec3152d | REIMPLEMENTED_FROM_SPEC / EXPERIMENTAL |\n+| PRF main award/settlement | fac26d2e8346aeab08194343b78c345d235c6935 | PINNED_SOURCE / STABLE bounded relation |\n+| PRF downstream transfer | f525737069dc4cef7741f805d08a988912f4454f | REIMPLEMENTED_FROM_SPEC / EXPERIMENTAL open PR14 |\n+| RSI detached testing | 3d3038f90c3dd98e79f948398167c5cc3ef2fdd8 | METHODOLOGY_ONLY / STABLE source |\n+| SEG caller-context discipline | 18f595b537017e5ff7b9074366c3065e877488f9 | METHODOLOGY_ONLY / STABLE source |\n+\n+Interpoll's path-level Pavlo implementation/retry evidence includes commits `2cfde5efc3d10b56c73e74723d3f328b77f2fc1f` and `a1eb47653aa7b8f0484ab977d75a5db41d226d02`, rather than repository ownership. See [machine provenance](provenance/sources.json), [human provenance](PROVENANCE.md), [all-work map](FULL_WORK_REUSE_MAP.md) and [validation](reports/v0.2/provenance-license-validation.stdout). These records do not assign revenue or adjudicate exclusive authorship.\n+\n+## L. License and third-party changes\n+\n+Root Apache-2.0 LICENSE remains byte-identical. New authored material remains Copyright 2026 Pavlo Tvardovskyi. Fourteen selected new vendored files include eight executable source files, two native profile/documentation files and four original grants: Semantic ABI Apache-2.0, recompute-kit CC0-1.0, Interpoll Unlicense and PRF MIT. Each copied file has exact upstream Git blob, SHA-256 and byte length; no unlicensed/pending source, private code, vendor capture or third-party dataset was imported.\n+\n+NOTICE, LICENSING.md and [THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md](THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md) distinguish copied pinned code, public-spec product reimplementations and methodology. Existing seven npm package notices and versions remain accounted for; only product version metadata changes in package lock. The offline provenance/license validator passes and does not purport to be a legal opinion.\n+\n+## M. Known limitations and repaired findings\n+\n+| Severity | Finding observed before correction | Current status / evidence |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| HIGH | Opaque AUTHENTICATED_REPORT incorrectly satisfied local recomputation grade | Fixed; G29/M13; grade-finding-before/after.json |\n+| HIGH | Unsupported requested-guarantee fields were ignored | Fixed; exact supported declaration required; eleven boundary tests; guarantee-finding-before/after.json |\n+| HIGH | Malformed native output inside a well-formed host report counted as a mutation kill | Fixed; INVALID_OUTPUT, zero kills; mutation-invalid-native-before.json and native controls |\n+| HIGH | PRF negative native result hidden by PRESERVED transfer in composed product | Fixed; retained exact before/after input hashes; G30/M14 and seven composition tests |\n+| MEDIUM | PRF unsupported/malformed/crash classification collapsed into generic insufficiency | Fixed with nested finite product projection; retained six before/after probes |\n+| LOW | Direct projection obligation sparse/accessor/duplicate arrays lacked admission | Fixed; three explicit tests; projection-obligations-before/after.json |\n+| LOW | Trustless wrapper maturity wording could imply complete stable product integration | Corrected: STABLE main source, EXPERIMENTAL bounded wrapper |\n+\n+The first grade and unsupported-guarantee observations retain actual tool output but lack full pre-fix input/source/time capture; they are explicitly labeled with those limits. Their after probes and static regressions do not fabricate exact before-input byte identity. PRF composition and invalid-native mutation findings retain full actual before evidence. Diagnostic recordings are not backdated or regenerated as pretend historical evidence.\n+\n+Remaining bounded limitations: no arbitrary claim entailment; no independent truth of caller premises; no real scanner-origin/provider/hardware provenance; no server/SQL execution authentication from Interpoll traces; no PR14 wire conformance; no full upstream suites or production security proof; no generic-v2 QEV/PQ/stochastic/capsule port; no live Ethereum/XRPL, ML-DSA implementation or ledger finality. The retained low v1 internal null-context helper limitation is not expanded into a public verification claim. All controls run on this operator's machine; a fresh checkout is not a second independent operator.\n+\n+Determinism passes **42 product runs across 7 semantic groups**, plus **12 native runs across 4 groups**. Product normal/repeat/jitless/environment/two-path outputs differ only in exact diagnostic `execution.argv`; every native result, reason, policy, grade, evidence identity and pin is retained in semantic identity. Native normal/repeat/Python -O stdout bytes are identical. Python -I ignores PYTHONHASHSEED, which is disclosed rather than claimed as a changed isolated seed. See [full determinism receipt](reports/v0.2/determinism.json).\n+\n+The UI uses the existing white angular R/cyan-violet crystal identity. Twenty new API/actual application-rendering tests pass, plus unchanged v1 UI tests. Actual browser smoke displays G10 CONTRADICTED, G29 INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE, and G30 CONTRADICTED with PRESERVED transfer; visible local JSON attachment inputs are outside collapsed details. Overall verdict dominates. [Rendered UI proof](reports/v0.2/ui-prf-preserved-negative.png) is a visual observation, not additional semantic coverage. Preview at `http://127.0.0.1:8810/` is a local process and must be checked before later reuse; default start port remains 8808. There is no bundler build step for this static local UI.\n+\n+## N. Open experimental dependencies\n+\n+Reporter-contract recompute-kit PR57 is **OPEN**, pinned head `197c6d26e68f85a117dd12a94924a7f959edaef4`. It was inspected but not copied or implemented. Main artifacts retain native `contractMode: null`; product self-grading interpretation is separately labeled. PRF PR14 is **OPEN**, head `f525737069dc4cef7741f805d08a988912f4454f`; only its neutral public transfer specification informs original experimental product code. Neither open head is called merged main. States are frozen observations, not promises of future upstream state.\n+\n+## O. Exact supported claims\n+\n+Within the declared bounded profiles and independently accepted caller premises, the product checks the exact caller/evidence surface, committed input and native relation. Authentic/intact evidence for A cannot establish incompatible B; native PASS/REPRODUCED cannot bypass compatibility; an opaque grade cannot impersonate local recomputation; a signed action cannot authorize a materially changed supplied retry; a preserved negative PRF transfer remains negative overall. These claims have literal paired controls, executable native relations, load-bearing semantic witnesses and applied mutation checks.\n+\n+## P. Claims not established\n+\n+This work does not establish universal semantic correctness, arbitrary upstream conformance, absence of vulnerabilities, external execution truth, authentic quantum hardware, real ML-DSA, live ledger finality, soundness/completeness of caller premises, exclusive authorship or production readiness. Integrity is not authenticity; authenticity is not correctness; replay is not a positive verdict; package presence/exit zero is not verification. No historical artifact receives new semantics merely because the product can parse it.\n+\n+## Q. Release recommendation\n+\n+**READY_FOR_V0_2_RELEASE_AUDIT**\n+\n+The local implementation, regression, corpus, semantic mutations, malformed controls, native execution, determinism, fresh checkout, provenance/license and presentation gates pass within their documented boundaries. Proceed next to a separately scoped independent v0.2 release-candidate audit. No push or release action is authorized or performed by this closure."},{"sha":"924d452f3148385aba793dce6e76b8dba1bc942d","filename":"V0_2_VECTOR_WITNESS_MATRIX.md","status":"added","additions":90,"deletions":0,"changes":90,"blob_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/blob/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/V0_2_VECTOR_WITNESS_MATRIX.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/raw/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/V0_2_VECTOR_WITNESS_MATRIX.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/contents/V0_2_VECTOR_WITNESS_MATRIX.md?ref=396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,90 @@\n+# v0.2 independent vector witness matrix\n+\n+Frozen candidate `4888a0584369a91075eb2bdbd9a2ff6b99c46588`. Reviewed all 68 inputs, both generators, fixture constructors, comparators and mutation catalogs without deriving expectations from the verifier. Classifications: **63 LOAD_BEARING,5 REDUNDANT,0 SELF_REFERENTIAL,0 DECORATIVE,0 UNCLEAR**. Count 68 is stored controls, not68 distinct semantic branches.\n+\n+`LOAD_BEARING` means a finite input independently witnesses its stated product relation. It does not certify the entire upstream implementation. Positive controls count as required non-vacuity checks. The30 original vectors exercise the v1 compatibility path; they are retained even when v2 covers the same principle.\n+\n+Exact full expected layer/native fields, vector SHA256, canonical input identity and original/declarative mutant metadata are in `vector-witness-matrix.json`. Matrix reasons are required codes, not an exact closed set: current comparators permit additional reasons. A dash for mutant means no measured catalog mutant selects it; it is not counted as a kill.\n+\n+## Independence limits\n+\n+- `tools/build-vectors.mjs` and `tools/generate-v02-vectors.mjs` construct literal expected statuses/reasons; neither calls verify/project to obtain expected product verdicts. Native constructors execute native code only to create saved evidence. The Trustless helper separately fixes literal positive/negative one-document expectations before running native code. PRF tuple outcomes are literal with independently inspectable amounts.\n+- RVR/Crystal/QEV fixture builders and verifier share upstream implementations. Their successful round trip alone is not independent verification of native cryptographic/canonicalization correctness. Literal subject/authority/scope/replay/absence substitutions remain independent product-boundary witnesses.\n+- Interpoll fixture uses product actionMaterial/commitActionTrace helpers. Negative material substitutions independently test equality, but cannot independently establish the commitment wire algorithm.\n+- Original v1 vector comparator checks layer status/product/required reason codes and not full native payload. v2 adds selected literal native-field constraints; these are not exhaustive native-report equality.\n+- G09/G01 and G10/G05 use advertised semantic-abi/rvr routing aliases but execute the same RVR/native-binding and Semantic ABI positive/scope branches. G19 repeats G04 authority-ID branch. I01 is byte-identical to G13 and I05 is byte-identical to G14 apart from metadata/positive-control declaration. V08 shares V01 request/bundle bytes but has an explicit crash setup, so is not redundant.\n+\n+| Vector | Claim | Relation | Native result | Product result | Reason | Independent oracle | Mutant killed | Positive control | Assessment |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| V01 | Caller exact commit and SHA256 predicate | Artifact bytes, Git commit/tree/path and caller surface agree | original_rvr.outcome=VERIFIED; replay=REPRODUCED | VERIFIED | (none required) | SHA256 of decoded 36-byte artifact equals caller digest; baseline supplies the positive control for substitutions | РІР‚вЂќ | V01 | LOAD_BEARING |\n+| V02 | Caller-selected commit B | requested.commit != receipt.commit | original_rvr.outcome=VERIFIED; replay=REPRODUCED | CONTRADICTED | REQUESTED_SUBJECT_NOT_BOUND, COMMIT_MISMATCH | Literal string inequality; the receipt and native result retain commit A | ignore-commit | V01 | LOAD_BEARING |\n+| V03 | Crystal root integrity | stored anchor root != recomputed receipt root | original_rvr.outcome=VERIFIED; replay=REPRODUCED | REJECTED_MALFORMED | RECEIPT_ROOT_MISMATCH | One signed payload root is replaced by 64 zeroes; valid outer re-signing cannot repair the native Crystal relation | РІР‚вЂќ | V01 | LOAD_BEARING |\n+| V04 | Caller-selected subject identity | requested.subject.id != receipt.subject.id | original_rvr.outcome=VERIFIED; replay=REPRODUCED | CONTRADICTED | ID_MISMATCH | Literal subject-ID inequality with unchanged valid signed evidence | ignore-requested-subject, compare-receipt-to-itself | V01 | LOAD_BEARING |\n+| V05 | Evidence completeness | Required native-result role absent | original_rvr.outcome=VERIFIED; replay=REPRODUCED | INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE | EVIDENCE_MISSING | Count/role inspection independently finds missing native-result manifest member | РІР‚вЂќ | V01 | LOAD_BEARING |\n+| V06 | Nonempty evidence sufficiency | Zero manifest members cannot establish required roles | original_rvr.outcome=VERIFIED; replay=REPRODUCED | INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE | EVIDENCE_MISSING | Literal empty list; replay payload presence is distinct from committed attachment sufficiency | accept-empty-evidence | V01 | LOAD_BEARING |\n+| V07 | Negative digest predicate | artifact SHA256 != selected expected digest | original_rvr.outcome=REFUTED; replay=REPRODUCED | CONTRADICTED | NATIVE_NEGATIVE_RESULT | Independent hashlib yields nonzero artifact digest versus all-zero required digest | promote-reproduced-to-verified | V01 | LOAD_BEARING |\n+| V08 | Unavailable checker | Process crash != semantic refutation | original_rvr.outcome=VERIFIED; replay=CANNOT_RECOMPUTE; fresh_native_output=UNAVAILABLE (saved original exists but is not fresh execution) | CANNOT_RECOMPUTE | NATIVE_RVR_EXECUTION_UNAVAILABLE | Explicit execution_setup crash-rvr is part of the vector; identical input bytes to V01 alone are not the complete witness | count-crash-as-semantic-refutation | V01 | LOAD_BEARING |\n+| V09 | Signed execution declaration completeness | package_present && runner_declared && !executed is insufficient | original_rvr.outcome=VERIFIED; replay=REPRODUCED | INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE | EXECUTION_REPORT_INCOMPLETE | Literal executed=false; this vector does not prove that no host native process ran | package-presence-as-pass | V01 | LOAD_BEARING |\n+| V10 | Consumer semantic scope | requested scope path != declared scope path | original_rvr.outcome=VERIFIED; replay=REPRODUCED | CONTRADICTED | SEMANTIC_SCOPE_MISMATCH | Literal different.txt vs result.txt mismatch; SHA256 identity remains equal | РІР‚вЂќ | V01 | LOAD_BEARING |\n+| V11 | Guarantee dependency retention | Downstream guarantee drops required dependency and relation | original_rvr.outcome=VERIFIED; replay=REPRODUCED | CONTRADICTED | GUARANTEE_DEPENDENCY_DROPPED | Independent set membership: source-binding required upstream and caller, absent downstream | ignore-guarantee-dependency | V12 | LOAD_BEARING |\n+| V12 | Positive guarantee transfer | Exact obligations and dependency survive transfer | original_rvr.outcome=VERIFIED; replay=REPRODUCED | VERIFIED | (none required) | Independent equality of guarantee, dependency and accepted caller obligation premises | РІР‚вЂќ | V01 | LOAD_BEARING |\n+| V13 | Authorized action/retries | Signed material equals accepted/duplicate action | original_rvr.outcome=VERIFIED; replay=REPRODUCED; domain_profile=interpoll | VERIFIED | (none required) | Independent canonical-field comparison; no server execution provenance is claimed | РІР‚вЂќ | V01 | LOAD_BEARING |\n+| V14 | Retry material binding | Retry down differs from authorized up | original_rvr.outcome=VERIFIED; replay=REPRODUCED; domain_profile=interpoll | CONTRADICTED | RETRY_AUTHORIZED_ACTION_CHANGED | Literal action value inequality; both original and substituted action can have valid signatures | ignore-retry-action-change | V13 | LOAD_BEARING |\n+| V15 | Current-state continuity | Later entry state B supersedes current claim A | original_rvr.outcome=VERIFIED; replay=REPRODUCED | CONTRADICTED | LATER_STATE_SUPERSEDES_CURRENT_CLAIM | Independent ordered entry inspection; historical observation A remains present | РІР‚вЂќ | V21 | LOAD_BEARING |\n+| V16 | Known profile admission | Unsupported product profile cannot certify | original_rvr.outcome=VERIFIED; replay=REPRODUCED | UNSUPPORTED_PROFILE | UNSUPPORTED_PROFILE | Literal unsupported.v9 is absent from finite declared profile inventory | РІР‚вЂќ | V01 | LOAD_BEARING |\n+| V17 | QEV provider authority | Valid packaging/replay does not establish provider authentication | original_rvr.outcome=VERIFIED; replay=REPRODUCED; domain_profile=qev | INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE | PROVIDER_AUTHENTICATION_NOT_ESTABLISHED | Native synthetic evidence lacks accepted provider authentication; outer signer is not the provider | РІР‚вЂќ | V01 | LOAD_BEARING |\n+| V18 | Producer vs native semantic result | Producer PASS contradicts replayed REFUTED | original_rvr.outcome=REFUTED; replay=REPRODUCED | CONTRADICTED | ASSERTED_NATIVE_RESULT_CONTRADICTION, NATIVE_NEGATIVE_RESULT | Independent SHA256 mismatch plus producer PASS literal; negative result is not replaced by replay success | РІР‚вЂќ | V01 | LOAD_BEARING |\n+| V19 | Authority class applicability | Historical capture cannot satisfy current recomputation requirement | original_rvr.outcome=VERIFIED; replay=REPRODUCED | CONTRADICTED | SEMANTIC_AUTHORITY_CLASS_MISMATCH | Literal authority-class inequality; positive signature is a separate fact | ignore-authority | V01 | LOAD_BEARING |\n+| V20 | Stochastic provenance boundary | Deterministic stream replay does not authenticate origin | original_rvr.outcome=VERIFIED; replay=REPRODUCED; domain_profile=stochastic | INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE | STOCHASTIC_PROVENANCE_NOT_ESTABLISHED | Independently decoded stream [1,2,3] can reproduce a selection; no provenance evidence exists | РІР‚вЂќ | V01 | LOAD_BEARING |\n+| V21 | Historical continuity | Later divergence does not negate exact earlier observation | original_rvr.outcome=VERIFIED; replay=REPRODUCED | VERIFIED | LATER_STATE_NONBLOCKING_FOR_HISTORICAL_CLAIM | Same A/B entry sequence as V15 with separately requested historical mode | РІР‚вЂќ | V01 | LOAD_BEARING |\n+| V22 | Caller policy version | Caller policy version 2 != committed version 1 | original_rvr.outcome=VERIFIED; replay=REPRODUCED | CONTRADICTED | POLICY_MISMATCH | Literal policy version inequality; old schema binds complete policy digest too | ignore-policy-version | V01 | LOAD_BEARING |\n+| V23 | Canonicalization profile admission | Unknown canonicalization profile cannot be assumed | original_rvr.outcome=VERIFIED; replay=NOT_RUN | REJECTED_MALFORMED | CANONICALIZATION_PROFILE_UNSUPPORTED | Literal unknown-canon is outside finite supported canonicalization vocabulary | ignore-canonicalization-profile | V01 | LOAD_BEARING |\n+| V24 | Evidence grade | Producer assertion cannot satisfy local recomputation grade | original_rvr.outcome=VERIFIED; replay=REPRODUCED | INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE | EVIDENCE_GRADE_NOT_ESTABLISHED | Literal PRODUCER_ASSERTION vs LOCAL_RECOMPUTATION requirement | ignore-evidence-grade | V01 | LOAD_BEARING |\n+| V25 | Expected actor authority | Valid signed actor differs from caller-authorized actor | original_rvr.outcome=VERIFIED; replay=REPRODUCED; domain_profile=interpoll | CONTRADICTED | ACTION_AUTHORITY_MISMATCH | Literal expected zero actor differs from signed actor; signature validity alone is insufficient | accept-any-valid-signature | V13 | LOAD_BEARING |\n+| V26 | Committed bytes availability | Null artifact bytes cannot be replayed | original_rvr.outcome=VERIFIED; replay=CANNOT_RECOMPUTE; fresh_native_output=UNAVAILABLE (saved original exists but is not fresh execution) | CANNOT_RECOMPUTE | COMMITTED_EVIDENCE_UNAVAILABLE | Literal committed attachment bytes=null; saved original native payload does not fill missing committed bytes | РІР‚вЂќ | V01 | LOAD_BEARING |\n+| V27 | Trust failure plus checker crash | Missing signer trust is not hidden by unavailable replay | original_rvr.outcome=VERIFIED; replay=CANNOT_RECOMPUTE; fresh_native_output=UNAVAILABLE (saved original exists but is not fresh execution) | INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE | SIGNER_NOT_TRUSTED, NATIVE_RVR_EXECUTION_UNAVAILABLE | Independent empty trusted_keys plus explicit crash setup; checks projection precedence, not another pure crash witness | РІР‚вЂќ | V01 | LOAD_BEARING |\n+| V28 | Moth counts packaging vs authority | Requested32/delivered0 is preserved without provider proof | original_rvr.outcome=VERIFIED; replay=REPRODUCED; domain_profile=qev | INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE | PROVIDER_AUTHENTICATION_NOT_ESTABLISHED | Explicit synthetic native requested/delivered fields and absent provider authentication; no real QPU proof | РІР‚вЂќ | V01 | LOAD_BEARING |\n+| V29 | Independent domain claim selection | Caller job differs from captured native claim job | original_rvr.outcome=VERIFIED; replay=REPRODUCED; domain_profile=qev | CONTRADICTED | INDEPENDENT_CLAIM_MISMATCH | Literal jobId substitution; preserved native capture cannot choose the caller claim | РІР‚вЂќ | V28 | LOAD_BEARING |\n+| V30 | Domain reproduced negative | Replayed refuted counts remain negative | original_rvr.outcome=VERIFIED; replay=REPRODUCED; domain_profile=qev | CONTRADICTED | PROVIDER_AUTHENTICATION_NOT_ESTABLISHED | Fresh synthetic refuted-counts constructor, literal negative product expectation; not independent general QEV conformance | РІР‚вЂќ | V28 | LOAD_BEARING |\n+| G01 | Exact generic SHA256 claim | All separately typed requested and evidence dimensions agree | RECOMPUTATION.semanticOutcome=VERIFIED; SEMANTIC_COMPATIBILITY.observedSemanticPair=PRESERVED | VERIFIED | (none required) | Independent surface equality and hashlib artifact predicate; native constructions are evidence, not expected product output | РІР‚вЂќ | G01 | LOAD_BEARING |\n+| G02 | Commit applicability