level companion to [the full reuse map](../FULL_WORK_REUSE_MAP.\n \n Existing sources were read only. Public neutral Semantic ABI work is allowed; private/commercial Vértice code and captures were not read or imported. No captured user/provider data, credentials or real trust keys become synthetic demo evidence. Optional, historical, fixture and methodology roles remain visible even when no source code is copied.\n \n+Audit snapshot and Fresh default labels below refer to the original source audit observation, not continuously current branch heads. V0.2 selected native additions are explicitly stated in the affected entries; all other exclusions and third-party rights remain in force.\n+\n ## All 20 owned public repositories\n \n ### pipavlo82/-crystal-artifact\n@@ -138,7 +140,7 @@ Retained role: **adapter**. Neutral guarantee preservation and oracle-blind rela\n \n Representative source references: `tools/relation_discrimination.py`, `adapters/v0/run_adapter.py`, `adapters/v0/score_results.py`, `spec/external-adapter-contract-v0.md`, `tools/award_actual_settlement.py`.\n \n-Not copied as runtime/data: `fixtures/`, `corpus/`, `evidence/`, `adapters/v0/score_results.py`, `tools/guarantee_preservation.py`. No upstream Python evaluator, scoring oracle, fixture corpus or captured settlement evidence is copied or executed. Neutral relation/guarantee ideas are independently reimplemented on product objects. PR14 remains OPEN, unmerged and EXPERIMENTAL; accepted basis/completeness are caller premises.\n+Not copied into product runtime/data: `fixtures/`, `corpus/`, `evidence/`, `adapters/v0/score_results.py`, `tools/guarantee_preservation.py`. V0.2 copies and executes only the merged-main `tools/award_actual_settlement.py` with its MIT license at `fac26d2e8346aeab08194343b78c345d235c6935`. PR14 consumer/scoring/captures are not copied or executed; the downstream relation is an original bounded reimplementation. PR14 remains OPEN and EXPERIMENTAL, with accepted basis/completeness caller premises.\n \n ### pipavlo82/quantum-execution-evidence\n \n@@ -292,7 +294,7 @@ Retained role: **adapter**. Signed public engagement, immutable retry and bounde\n \n Representative source references: `shared-validation/engagement.js`, `shared-validation/engagement-store.js`, `src/services/publicEngagementService.ts`, `src/services/reactionOutboxService.ts`, `docs/security/PUBLIC_ENGAGEMENT_V1.md`.\n \n-Not copied as runtime/data: `shared-validation/engagement.js`, `shared-validation/engagement-store.js`, `src/services/publicEngagementService.ts`, `src/services/reactionOutboxService.ts`, `tools/coordination-impact-v2/`. No upstream service/store/UI/SQL deployment or coordination receipt corpus is copied. Public signed-action/retry semantics are independently reimplemented. Exact signed retries do not establish live admission atomicity, target existence, viewing, human uniqueness or independent coordination judgments.\n+V0.1 did not copy the native action implementation. V0.2 copies and executes only `shared-validation/engagement.js` from `559e47f2cd2ffcbd8ad38293da89448d8ec3152d` under its retained Unlicense grant, through the bounded native signed-action adapter. Not copied as runtime/data: `shared-validation/engagement-store.js`, `src/services/publicEngagementService.ts`, `src/services/reactionOutboxService.ts`, `tools/coordination-impact-v2/`. No upstream service/store/UI/SQL deployment or coordination receipt corpus is copied. Supplied retry relation checks are product code around that native signature primitive. Exact signed retries do not establish live admission atomicity, target existence, viewing, human uniqueness or independent coordination judgments.\n \n ### jdleo/provably-fair-dice\n \n@@ -434,7 +436,7 @@ Retained role: **adapter**. Pinned scan/time/consumption/permission profiles and\n \n Representative source references: `conformance/scan-subject-binding-v0/scan_check.py`, `conformance/scan-subject-binding-v0/mutation_check.py`, `conformance/scan-subject-binding-v0/vectors.json`, `conformance/scan-subject-binding-v0/suite.json`, `conformance/encode-json-utf8-lf-v0/encode-json-utf8-lf-v0.spec.md`.\n \n-Not copied as runtime/data: `conformance/scan-subject-binding-v0/scan_check.py`, `conformance/scan-subject-binding-v0/mutation_check.py`, `conformance/scan-subject-binding-v0/vectors.json`, `conformance/scan-subject-binding-v0/suite.json`, `conformance/encode-json-utf8-lf-v0/encode-json-utf8-lf-v0.spec.md`. No complete upstream scanner/runner/conformance/runtime is copied or invoked. Selected subject/report-only/self-grading/nonempty/control ideas inform original host checks. Open PR57/65 proposals remain separately pinned; process exit/package presence is not semantic execution.\n+Not copied into product runtime: `conformance/scan-subject-binding-v0/mutation_check.py`, upstream `vectors.json`, or `conformance/encode-json-utf8-lf-v0/encode-json-utf8-lf-v0.spec.md`. V0.2 copies the selected scan checker, canonical `tools/run_conformance.py`, suite/README and CC0 license from historical main `1a37bcaf91918fd8a98f164d97d0fddbc28c6755`, and actually invokes that bounded checker/runner. It does not import the whole toolkit or newly merged PR57 reporter behavior. Release-audit-only public CC0 vectors/artifacts are separately identified in audit evidence, not used as product runtime or independently authored synthetic fixtures. Package presence/exit zero remains insufficient.\n \n ### trustless-ai/semantic-abi\n \n@@ -444,7 +446,7 @@ Retained role: **adapter**. Neutral manifest/linker claim, authority, scope and\n \n Representative source references: `schema/manifest.schema.json`, `schema/manifest-v0.md`, `runner/src/manifest.mjs`, `runner/src/linker.mjs`, `runner/src/evaluate.mjs`.\n \n-Not copied as runtime/data: `adapters/`, `runner/src/evaluate.mjs`, `runner/src/manifest.mjs`. Public neutral schema/linker specifications are allowed. The product relation adapter is an original reimplementation; a byte-pinned neutral linker subset is separately copied inside generic QEV. Public system-specific adapter code and all private/commercial Vértice implementations/captures are excluded by scope, not read. No producer authority label becomes a verified premise.\n+Not copied as runtime/data: public system-specific `adapters/` or private/commercial Vértice implementations/captures. V0.2 copies four unchanged neutral public runtime files (`classes.mjs`, `manifest.mjs`, `linker.mjs`, `evaluate.mjs`) and their Apache-2.0 license from `d15c666dfccff17f7350fe97d2fc7b71cb2cbaee`; the adapter actually executes validation/linking and optional pair evaluation. Generic-QEV neutral copies remain separately manifested. New product encoding/projection is original glue, not complete upstream wire conformance. No producer authority label becomes an independently established premise.\n \n ## New npm runtime dependencies\n \n@@ -454,4 +456,4 @@ Node/Bun/Python runtimes and optional real PQ/ledger/provider systems are enviro\n \n The copied npm license paths and byte hashes are finalized in `provenance/npm-licenses.json` and linked from `provenance/dependencies.json`. Public snapshot preservation is limited to the saved 43 repositories / 21,119 files with zero mismatches, without a global live-worktree cleanliness claim.\n \n-Working bounded product slices also include original Interpoll action/retry, PQ provider/vector/temporal-authority interfaces and `tools/reproduce.mjs` local conduct reproduction. Their cited upstream implementation files remain uncopied. Kit/RSI/SEG source methods are applied without native whole-tool/domain execution; the machine catalog carries both `used` and implementation boundaries. `.gitmodules` references identify uninitialized external dependencies whose payload files are not present in the frozen source archives.\n+Working bounded product slices also include original Interpoll action/retry, PQ provider/vector/temporal-authority interfaces and `tools/reproduce.mjs` local conduct reproduction. Selected native Interpoll, Semantic ABI, recompute-kit and PRF files are explicitly copied/executed as listed above and in the v0.2 manifests; remaining application/queue/provider implementations are uncopied. RSI/SEG methods are applied without their native tool/onchain execution; the machine catalog carries both `used` and implementation boundaries. `.gitmodules` references identify uninitialized external dependencies whose payload files are not present in the frozen source archives."},{"sha":"e970c073232368c0fbc85fb6f31a2aa790f089c0","filename":"docs/generic-claim-boundary.md","status":"added","additions":39,"deletions":0,"changes":39,"blob_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/blob/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/docs%2Fgeneric-claim-boundary.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/raw/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/docs%2Fgeneric-claim-boundary.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/contents/docs%2Fgeneric-claim-boundary.md?ref=396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@\n+# Generic caller-selected claim boundary\n+\n+ReceiptOS Verify does not answer only whether a receipt is intact. It evaluates what supplied evidence establishes for a caller-selected claim, within the selected profile's bounded relation.\n+\n+Request v2 requires `claim`, `subject`, `scope`, `authority`, `policy`, `version`, `time`, `assumptions`, `dependencies`, `requested_guarantees`, `evidence`, `evidence_requirements`, `verification_profile` and an adapter ID. The authenticated statement carries a separate `surface` with the same ten semantic dimensions. Consumer policy configuration is caller-owned; the evidence surface carries only policy ID/version. Neither object is substituted for the other.\n+\n+`claim` has an opaque ID, a supported primitive kind and exact parameters. Subject has a generic kind, opaque ID and version, with artifact and Git identities when represented. Artifact digest, Git commit/tree/path, top-level claim version and subject version remain distinct dimensions. Optional absence is not null. IDs compare exactly as Unicode scalar sequences under the existing canonical JSON profile: NFC/NFD or case transformations are not silently equivalent.\n+\n+Authority has ID and class. Current executable v2 profiles require `INDEPENDENT_RECOMPUTATION`, a producer key ID matching the signed authority ID, caller-trusted Ed25519 key material and an explicitly accepted authority declaration. That is bounded local authority acceptance, not an external trust registry or proof of provider identity.\n+\n+Scope is an exact canonical object. A broader or narrower object is incompatible unless a future versioned profile defines and tests an entailment relation. Native adapters also bind the evidence declaration to their permitted scope and actual input, preventing a signer from expanding a primitive into an unsupported guarantee.\n+\n+Policy ID/version and the independent top-level claim version compare exactly. Time is an exact nonempty safe-integer half-open interval `[not_before, not_after)` and the independently selected verification instant must lie within it. No live clock, revocation service or historical-key discovery is implied.\n+\n+All assumptions used by either surface must appear in caller policy's established assumptions. All dependencies used by either surface need an independently accepted exact ID/version result. Required dependencies must also be declared by the evidence. A contradicted dependency dominates missing information. Duplicate dependency IDs, including conflicting result statuses or differing versions, are rejected instead of last-wins resolution. These caller premises are inputs, not independently verified external truth.\n+\n+Evidence basis comes from attachment roles whose actual bytes pass the manifest/payload commitment checks and from an actually completed pinned execution. Receipt-provided booleans such as package-present or exit-zero cannot establish that basis.\n+\n+The compatibility result is `COMPATIBLE`, `CONTRADICTED`, `INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE` or `UNSUPPORTED`, with dimension results and exact reasons. Reasons include CLAIM_MISMATCH, SUBJECT_MISMATCH, ARTIFACT_MISMATCH, AUTHORITY_MISMATCH, SCOPE_MISMATCH, POLICY_MISMATCH, VERSION_MISMATCH, TIME_MISMATCH, ASSUMPTION_UNESTABLISHED, DEPENDENCY_MISSING and DEPENDENCY_CONTRADICTED. The public native Semantic ABI vocabulary is retained separately.\n+\n+A matching digest, valid signature, native PASS or REPRODUCED result cannot override incompatibility. REPRODUCED negative evidence stays negative. Contradiction means supplied evidence does not establish the selected positive claim; it does not prove that some other subject executed or failed.\n+\n+## Compatibility with v0.1\n+\n+No v1 vector is migrated or regenerated. V1 callers retain the original schemas and projection. V2 inputs require an explicitly different statement signing domain (`receiptos.verify.statement.v2`); an old signature cannot be relabeled as v2. The original commit A/B witness remains a special case of the broader identity boundary.\n+\n+## Optional requirement contexts\n+\n+Supplied Interpoll, PRF and continuity context objects have closed, typed field\n+contracts. Unknown semantic requirements and mistyped known fields are rejected,\n+including null used as a defaulted outcome or non-Boolean envelope obligation.\n+This admission does not add fresh-server authentication or chain evidence.\n+\n+Context presence alone does not activate a capability. Adapter selection and\n+`requested_guarantees` remain authoritative: a valid PRF context with an empty\n+requested-guarantee list stays inactive and establishes no transfer claim.\n+Missing/partial supported context safely withholds the relevant result. Git\n+object closure is specific to subject kind `git-artifact`; opaque generic kinds\n+can carry matching labels without establishing Git repository membership."},{"sha":"a0aa61e6d7c4b347ae208668e4e156876e569d27","filename":"docs/guarantee-preservation.md","status":"added","additions":117,"deletions":0,"changes":117,"blob_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/blob/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/docs%2Fguarantee-preservation.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/raw/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/docs%2Fguarantee-preservation.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/contents/docs%2Fguarantee-preservation.md?ref=396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,117 @@\n+# Native PRF relation and downstream guarantee preservation\n+\n+`receiptos.verify.guarantee-preservation.v2` has two explicit source boundaries.\n+\n+1. The **merged-main native relation** is\n+   `pipavlo82/protected-relation-fixtures` at\n+   `fac26d2e8346aeab08194343b78c345d235c6935`,\n+   `tools/award_actual_settlement.py`. It is copied unchanged with its MIT\n+   license and actually executed with isolated Python over fresh synthetic\n+   tuples. This source-main relation is classified `STABLE` within its stated\n+   bounded synthetic contract.\n+2. The **product downstream transfer relation** is original code informed by\n+   the public PR14 guarantee-preservation specification at\n+   `f525737069dc4cef7741f805d08a988912f4454f`. Live PR14 inspection found it\n+   `OPEN` and unmerged. This product projection is `EXPERIMENTAL` and\n+   `REIMPLEMENTED_FROM_SPEC`; it neither executes PR14's Python consumer nor\n+   claims its wire-format conformance.\n+\n+The complete adapter remains `EXPERIMENTAL`. No PR-only behavior is called\n+current-main behavior. Source identities, licenses and path-level contribution\n+records are in `provenance/v02-actions-prf.json`.\n+\n+## Separate caller premises\n+\n+`evaluatePrfV2(input, context)` accepts:\n+\n+```text\n+input.profile = award-actual-settlement-v0\n+input.upstream = {award, settlements, native_result}\n+input.downstream = {native_result, dependencies:[{id,version}]}\n+\n+context.accepted_basis = {id, dependencies:[{id,version}]}\n+context.required_native_result = {outcome, reason}\n+context.required_relation_input_digest = SHA256(canonical({award,settlements}))\n+context.required_guarantee = native-result-and-dependencies-preserved\n+```\n+\n+The caller independently selects the exact award/settlement input digest,\n+selects the required native result and separately accepts the exact\n+dependency identities and versions. Neither field is manufactured from a\n+producer's success flag. A nonempty, unambiguous basis is required. Dependency\n+ordering is irrelevant; identity and version equality are exact.\n+The selector is mandatory: an unrelated award tuple with the same native result\n+cannot establish the caller's requested PRF relation. This is a separately scoped\n+PRF award/settlement obligation, not proof that the surrounding RVR or Trustless\n+claim's native result was transferred.\n+\n+The v2 product request supports exactly this guarantee declaration:\n+`requested_guarantees: [{\"id\":\"native-result-and-dependencies-preserved\"}]`.\n+Additional declaration fields, including version, parameters, scope or authority,\n+are unsupported rather than silently ignored. They produce guarantee\n+`UNVERIFIABLE` with `GUARANTEE_UNSUPPORTED` and an otherwise positive product\n+result of `INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE`. Unknown IDs and multiple obligations have the\n+same semantics. An empty declaration list makes no guarantee-preservation claim.\n+The independently selected native result, tuple digest and dependencies belong\n+in `guarantee_requirement` using the bounded context contract above.\n+\n+The native main `relation(award, settlements)` checks one supplied finalized\n+award against one observed settlement: target, tender, fulfiller, acceptance and\n+actual amount must preserve the award tuple. Native `PRESERVED`, `VIOLATED` or\n+`UNVERIFIABLE` and its exact reason remain available. A completed Python process\n+with exit 0 establishes no positive native verdict by itself.\n+\n+The copied module's fixture validation and expected case table are not invoked\n+by this adapter. It calls `relation` directly on supplied tuples and compares\n+the observed native output with separately declared native evidence. Changed\n+payment can therefore yield `VIOLATED` even when the producer declared a\n+positive result. No upstream fixture expectation is an oracle for product tests.\n+\n+## Projection relation\n+\n+The product preserves `recomputation`, `nativeResult` and\n+`guaranteeProjection` separately.\n+\n+| Evidence | Replay | Transfer | Product |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| Native positive reproduced; exact caller result/dependencies preserved downstream | `REPRODUCED` | `PRESERVED` | `VERIFIED` |\n+| Native negative reproduced; that exact negative and dependencies retained | `REPRODUCED` | `PRESERVED` | `CONTRADICTED` |\n+| Native output differs from supplied native evidence | `DIVERGED` | `UNVERIFIABLE` | `CONTRADICTED` |\n+| Exact upstream result reproduced; downstream changes result or a dependency | `REPRODUCED` | `VIOLATED` | `CONTRADICTED` |\n+| Missing caller-accepted premise or native `UNVERIFIABLE` | `REPRODUCED` when possible | `UNVERIFIABLE` | `INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE` |\n+| Native process unavailable, crashes or output contract fails | `CANNOT_RECOMPUTE` | `UNVERIFIABLE` | `CANNOT_RECOMPUTE` |\n+| Unsupported profile/guarantee | As available | `UNVERIFIABLE` | `UNSUPPORTED_PROFILE` |\n+\n+A preserved transfer is not necessarily a positive upstream result. Correctly\n+reproducing and faithfully retaining `VIOLATED / amount_mismatch` preserves the\n+declared transfer relation while the product remains negative. Conversely,\n+positive upstream evidence does not establish a consumer guarantee when that\n+consumer drops or changes a required dependency.\n+\n+Composition preserves the adapter's separate `productProjection` as an explicit\n+product obligation alongside the transfer status. A positive surrounding RVR\n+claim cannot turn a faithfully transferred negative PRF tuple into global\n+`VERIFIED`: the transfer stays `PRESERVED`, the PRF product projection stays\n+`CONTRADICTED` and overall is `CONTRADICTED`. Unsupported PRF profiles, malformed\n+PRF input and unavailable native checks retain their respective product failure\n+classification rather than being reduced to generic insufficient evidence.\n+\n+## Scope and limitations\n+\n+The caller's accepted basis remains a bounded premise. This adapter does not\n+prove that the basis is complete, sound or authorized by an outside institution.\n+It does not establish authenticated chain execution, award authority, universal\n+mechanism truthfulness or arbitrary downstream program behavior. Exact\n+downstream declarations are supplied artifacts, not execution proof.\n+\n+Fresh product tests independently declare expected tuple outcomes, exercise\n+payment substitution, native divergence, faithfully preserved negatives,\n+downstream native substitution, dropped/versioned dependencies, missing/empty\n+premises and malformed/unsupported inputs. RSI's detached relation expectations\n+and SEG's separately selected consumer context inform this discipline; neither\n+upstream's runtime is executed here.\n+\n+Only the merged-main award module and MIT license were copied. PR14 Python\n+consumer, adapters, schema, suite and source-derived recompute-kit expectation\n+fixtures were not copied: the product uses its own bounded input contract, and\n+its Trustless adapter independently handles native recompute-kit execution."},{"sha":"42d9a9175f1ad85295c8f8b9777f30353d9f55a6","filename":"docs/interpoll-adapter.md","status":"added","additions":81,"deletions":0,"changes":81,"blob_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/blob/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/docs%2Finterpoll-adapter.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/raw/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/docs%2Finterpoll-adapter.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/contents/docs%2Finterpoll-adapter.md?ref=396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,81 @@\n+# Interpoll signed actions and supplied retry evidence\n+\n+`receiptos.verify.interpoll-action.v2` executes the unchanged public Interpoll\n+`verifyAction` implementation from `Interpoll1/decentralised` default branch\n+`master`, pinned to `559e47f2cd2ffcbd8ad38293da89448d8ec3152d`. The source file is\n+`shared-validation/engagement.js`; its Unlicense is retained beside the copied\n+file. No Interpoll repository, server, browser, database or deployment is changed.\n+\n+Pavlo's signed-action implementation is evidenced by commit\n+`2cfde5efc3d10b56c73e74723d3f328b77f2fc1f`; the durable exact retry implementation\n+is evidenced by `a1eb47653aa7b8f0484ab977d75a5db41d226d02`. Both are ancestors of\n+the inspected current default branch. These path-level commit records establish\n+identified contributions; they do not attribute the entire shared repository to\n+Pavlo. Exact file identities and contribution links are recorded in\n+`provenance/v02-actions-prf.json`.\n+\n+## Caller and producer boundary\n+\n+The product adapter is original glue around the native Schnorr action relation.\n+`evaluateInterpollV2(input, context)` accepts the producer trace separately from\n+the caller's selected `context.requested_action` and `context.authority`.\n+\n+The requested action is the exact native material tuple: `version`, `namespace`,\n+`kind`, `actor`, `targetType`, `targetId`, `value`, `createdAt` and `nonce`.\n+The caller authority contains `actor` and `namespace`. The receipt cannot select\n+either premise on the caller's behalf. A signature over A cannot authorize B,\n+even when B retains A's signature or action ID. Equality covers the complete\n+native signed envelope for accepted actions and every retry, including material\n+parameters, nonce, timestamp, ID and signature.\n+\n+The trace models these fields separately:\n+\n+| Field | Evidence meaning |\n+| --- | --- |\n+| `signed_intent` | Native signed action; key control over exact intent |\n+| `accepted_action` | Supplied `accepted` or `duplicate` relay response and action |\n+| `attempts` | Distinct attempt IDs, exact signed envelopes, delivery status and declared execution attempt |\n+| `observation` | Supplied action/attempt-bound `APPLIED` or `REJECTED` observation |\n+| `final_committed_result` | Exact action ID, ordered attempt IDs and digests of supplied trace and observation |\n+\n+`commitActionTrace` computes a product trace digest. That digest binds supplied\n+artifacts; it does not establish an actual database transaction or relay origin.\n+The adapter's `EXPERIMENTAL` maturity covers this bounded supplied-trace relation.\n+\n+## Native result and product result\n+\n+Native signature evaluation uses `fresh: false` for historical evidence.\n+`signature = VALID` therefore does not establish fresh admission, revocation\n+status, target existence, successful relay delivery or actual viewing. Native\n+authorization, acceptance status, retry relation, supplied observation and trace\n+commitment remain separate in `nativeResult`.\n+\n+| Condition | Product result |\n+| --- | --- |\n+| Exact caller-selected signed action and complete matching supplied execution trace | `VERIFIED` for this bounded relation |\n+| Changed caller action, accepted action or material retry | `CONTRADICTED` |\n+| Invalid native signature | `CONTRADICTED` |\n+| Unsupported caller authority | `UNSUPPORTED_PROFILE` |\n+| Duplicate acceptance with no new execution | `INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE` for a new execution claim |\n+| Missing execution observation or trace commitment | `INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE` |\n+| Supplied execution rejection | `CONTRADICTED` |\n+| Extra or conflicting semantic fields | `REJECTED_MALFORMED` |\n+\n+`AUTHORIZATION_ONLY` is a separately selected narrower outcome. It can establish\n+the exact signed-action relation while leaving execution `NOT_ESTABLISHED`.\n+`EXECUTION_OBSERVED` is the default and requires supplied observation evidence.\n+Neither mode independently authenticates an Interpoll server or execution.\n+\n+## Controls and reuse limits\n+\n+`tests/interpoll-v2.test.mjs` includes I01-I08 plus missing caller intent,\n+wrong caller target, native signature tampering, trace tampering, supplied\n+rejection, duplicate execution inflation and observation binding controls.\n+Positive fixtures use a public synthetic key and deterministic Schnorr auxiliary\n+bytes; they contain no real Interpoll identity or captured user data.\n+\n+Only `engagement.js` and its license were copied. The application, relay, SQL\n+store, Gun integration, durable TypeScript outbox and captured production data\n+were not copied. Exact-retry and observation composition are recorded as\n+`REIMPLEMENTED_FROM_SPEC`. In particular, the adapter does not execute the\n+application's durable queue or prove its SQL atomicity."},{"sha":"021245fa7daa8861356534ae161598dab919c76b","filename":"docs/product-projection.md","status":"added","additions":52,"deletions":0,"changes":52,"blob_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/blob/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/docs%2Fproduct-projection.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/raw/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/docs%2Fproduct-projection.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/contents/docs%2Fproduct-projection.md?ref=396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@\n+# Product projection v0.2\n+\n+The product verdict is a finite, ordered decision over fourteen separate layer results. Native replay, native semantic outcome and native adapter vocabularies remain visible. They are not Boolean aliases for the product result.\n+\n+`profiles/product-projection-v2.json` is the machine-readable decision table. Its forty-six literal cases were specified independently of `projectV2`; expected outcomes are not generated by the function under test. `tests/projection-v2.test.mjs` checks the table and malformed boundaries, while `tests/generic-boundary-v2.test.mjs` and `tests/prf-composition-v2.test.mjs` exercise actual composed receipts and native execution.\n+\n+| Priority | Condition | Product verdict |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| 1 | Invalid layer inventory, field representation, status vocabulary, obligations or support flag | `REJECTED_MALFORMED` |\n+| 2 | Any admitted layer is `REJECTED_MALFORMED` | `REJECTED_MALFORMED` |\n+| 3 | Any layer contradicts/violates its relation, or native recomputation semantic outcome is `REFUTED` | `CONTRADICTED` |\n+| 4 | Unsupported profile or required adapter/semantic surface | `UNSUPPORTED_PROFILE` |\n+| 5 | Required computation cannot run/recompute or replay is `DIVERGED` | `CANNOT_RECOMPUTE` |\n+| 6 | Any required positive premise is unestablished | `INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE` |\n+| 7 | All preceding guards clear and all required successes are established | `VERIFIED` |\n+\n+The six mandatory obligations always apply, even if `policy.required_layers` is empty:\n+\n+| Layer | Required success |\n+| --- | --- |\n+| Integrity | `VERIFIED` |\n+| Authenticity | `VERIFIED` |\n+| Subject Binding | `VERIFIED` |\n+| Recomputation | `REPRODUCED`, with separate semantic outcome `VERIFIED` |\n+| Evidence Sufficiency | `SUFFICIENT` |\n+| Semantic Compatibility | `COMPATIBLE` |\n+\n+Consumers can also require Guarantee Preservation (`PRESERVED`), Continuity (`PRESERVED` or `VERIFIED`) and Domain Adapter (`VERIFIED` or `PRESERVED`). Requested guarantees, continuity requests and the Interpoll trace adapter add their applicable obligation automatically. Omitted optional layers do not establish those guarantees. A supplied contradiction is never ignored merely because its layer was optional.\n+\n+Integrity and authenticity success cannot override a subject, authority, scope, policy, version or dependency contradiction. `REPRODUCED` negative native evidence remains negative. An upstream native negative result can have a separately `PRESERVED` transfer relation; preserving that transfer does not make the original claim positive.\n+\n+A PRF result retains its native tuple outcome, transfer status and separate\n+`productProjection`. When supplied, the nested product projection must contain\n+exactly `status` from the six-value product vocabulary and a `reasonCodes` array\n+of nonempty strings. Malformed or contradicted nested results take the same\n+precedence as other supplied layer results. For a requested PRF obligation,\n+unsupported, unavailable or insufficient nested product results also block\n+overall verification at their corresponding precedence. A successful transfer\n+status cannot hide these failures.\n+\n+The surrounding RVR digest predicate and the separately caller-selected PRF\n+award/settlement obligation remain distinct relations. RVR may remain positive\n+while the PRF native tuple is negative and faithfully transferred. The report\n+then keeps RVR `VERIFIED`/`REPRODUCED`, PRF transfer `PRESERVED` and overall\n+`CONTRADICTED`; it does not relabel the transfer as `VIOLATED`. A PRF checker\n+crash or malformed native output yields overall `CANNOT_RECOMPUTE`, never a\n+semantic contradiction. Malformed PRF input is `REJECTED_MALFORMED` and an\n+unsupported PRF profile is `UNSUPPORTED_PROFILE`.\n+\n+Package presence, a runner declaration, process exit zero, native runner `PASS`, backend-conformance `PASS`, and truthy JSON values are not positive semantic outcomes. An empty evidence collection cannot establish the mandatory evidence obligation. A crashed checker gives unavailable computation; it is not semantic refutation or mutation coverage. `DRIFT` is unavailable source reproduction rather than a semantic claim failure.\n+\n+The projection proves only the declared composition of these input layers. It does not independently establish the soundness of caller-accepted dependencies, the real-world truth of signed declarations, scanner-origin execution, provider/hardware authenticity, general scope entailment, production security or ledger finality. Every `VERIFIED` result remains bounded by its displayed claim surface, accepted policy and adapter limitations."},{"sha":"5eebf60678c53a9d1742446a6b05bcdf64359972","filename":"docs/semantic-abi-adapter.md","status":"added","additions":29,"deletions":0,"changes":29,"blob_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/blob/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/docs%2Fsemantic-abi-adapter.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/raw/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/docs%2Fsemantic-abi-adapter.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/contents/docs%2Fsemantic-abi-adapter.md?ref=396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@\n+# Semantic ABI adapter for v0.2\n+\n+`evaluateSemanticAbi({expected, observed, context})` executes the unchanged public neutral Semantic ABI manifest validator, semantic linker and optional two-level pair evaluator. The source is `trustless-ai/semantic-abi` main at `d15c666dfccff17f7350fe97d2fc7b71cb2cbaee` (tree `63b5075bffb3027ab63c2a7f25de06502b0ed861`). It is an **EXPERIMENTAL**, bounded adapter over the draft native v0 relation. It imports no Vértice adapter, commercial behavior, capture or private implementation.\n+\n+The generic request is the caller-selected `expected` surface. The signed/packaged evidence declares the separate `observed` surface. The product's `compareClaimSurfaces` checks claim, subject, artifact, authority identity/class, exact scope, policy/version, claim version, time applicability, assumptions, dependencies and accepted evidence basis. These dimensions remain separately visible. Matching artifact bytes cannot override an incompatible authority or scope.\n+\n+## Native execution and encoding\n+\n+The vendored `runner/src/classes.mjs`, `linker.mjs`, `manifest.mjs` and `evaluate.mjs` retain their exact upstream bytes and Apache-2.0 license. Each adapter call validates the producer and consumer declarations and executes `linkEdge(producer, requirement)` when the declarations are supported.\n+\n+Native v0 accepts string `claim_type`, `authority_class`, `scope` and exactly one of `issued_at` or `verification_time`. The wrapper encodes complete generic claim and scope objects as canonical JSON strings and the generic time interval as a tagged canonical JSON string in `verification_time`. This is an explicit product embedding of the native equality relation. It is not a claim of standard upstream manifest wire conformance or an assertion that an interval string is a wall-clock timestamp. Actual half-open interval applicability is independently checked by the product relation.\n+\n+The native authority classes are `INDEPENDENT_JUDGMENT`, `CRYPTOGRAPHIC_VERIFICATION`, `EX_POST_VALIDATION`, `INFRASTRUCTURE_ATTESTATION`, `ONCHAIN_COMMITMENT`, `INDEPENDENT_RECOMPUTATION`, `KEY_BINDING_AUTHORITY` and `SEMANTIC_VERIFICATION`. Unknown classes remain unsupported. Native exact recomputation-to-semantic-verification coercion is preserved in the native result. The product conservatively requires the exact caller-selected authority identity/class and can therefore contradict that native edge.\n+\n+## Preserved results\n+\n+The response contains `nativeResult.manifest_validation`, `nativeResult.link`, `expectedSemanticPair`, `observedSemanticPair`, optional `nativeResult.pair_evaluation`, the complete product `compatibility`, and separate adapter `status`/`reasonCodes`.\n+\n+`observedSemanticPair` comes from the executed native linker: valid edge gives `PRESERVED`; native `TYPE_ERROR` gives `VIOLATED`; unavailable or unsupported declarations give `UNVERIFIABLE`. The optional `context.expected_pair` is a detached caller-selected test oracle. The receipt cannot supply this oracle; it never changes the observation or product compatibility. If absent, `expectedSemanticPair` and pair evaluation remain null. No implementation-derived expectation is fabricated.\n+\n+A negative native observation with detached expected `VIOLATED` yields backend-conformance `PASS` while the product remains `CONTRADICTED`. A native edge can be `PRESERVED` while the product reports `SUBJECT_MISMATCH`, `AUTHORITY_MISMATCH`, `POLICY_MISMATCH`, `VERSION_MISMATCH` or `DEPENDENCY_CONTRADICTED`; those fields are outside the native v0 manifest. Native vocabulary is preserved rather than rewritten as the product verdict.\n+\n+Dependencies, assumptions and evidence basis come from independently selected context/policy premises. A producer declaration is not proof that a dependency or authority was established. This adapter does not authenticate a declaration by itself and never establishes real-world truth merely by linking it.\n+\n+## Provenance and limits\n+\n+`provenance/v02-semantic-abi.json` records exact copied-file Git blob IDs/SHA-256 digests and public contribution evidence. Pavlo Tvardovskyi authored semantic-model repair commit `8fb67bd43140a1cc7aab5c272796da0417d3ceaf`, merged through PR #1 at `474b474132a64d139972ebf2c06c18a174ce39bb`. The retained neutral runtime also contains Echo-Merlini implementation history; it is not attributed solely to Pavlo or inferred from repository ownership.\n+\n+The product tests use fresh synthetic generic surfaces and detached literal outcomes. They cover exact compatibility, subject/artifact/authority/scope/policy/version/time mismatches, absent or contradicted dependencies, absent evidence basis, and equal artifact hashes with incompatible semantics. Their positive controls retain the exact matching surface. They demonstrate the bounded adapter and product relation, not complete upstream or cross-system conformance."},{"sha":"7ee77b2f4540fc2721521919ab207bef9dfe81fe","filename":"docs/trustless-adapter.md","status":"added","additions":147,"deletions":0,"changes":147,"blob_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/blob/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/docs%2Ftrustless-adapter.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/raw/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/docs%2Ftrustless-adapter.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/contents/docs%2Ftrustless-adapter.md?ref=396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,147 @@\n+# Trustless native integration in v0.2\n+\n+The executable profile `receiptos.verify.trustless-scan.v2` wraps selected,\n+unchanged public recompute-kit code. It runs the real native\n+`scan_subject_binding.v0` relation and the real pinned-main conformance runner\n+against fresh caller-supplied evidence. It does not run the complete\n+recompute-kit suite inventory.\n+\n+## Exact public source\n+\n+The public main observed when this adapter was pinned was\n+`1a37bcaf91918fd8a98f164d97d0fddbc28c6755`, tree\n+`7b64f2b3f51a3df93ab74d6ea717f74635799845`. PR65 is merged into this main.\n+The selected scan checker and canonical runner are vendored byte-for-byte;\n+runtime SHA-256 checks pin all executed upstream files and the selected spec.\n+The CC0-1.0 source grant remains in `vendor/recompute-kit-v02/LICENSE`.\n+\n+PR57 was OPEN at `197c6d26e68f85a117dd12a94924a7f959edaef4`, with\n+base `1a37bcaf91918fd8a98f164d97d0fddbc28c6755`, at the source observation.\n+Release audit independently found it merged at `2026-10-11T22:35:33Z`;\n+current main is `3c3923956200d01ab74c2dcbb49b268739943bda`. The adapter\n+retains its historical-main pin and does not import newly merged reporter\n+behavior. It rejects source pins other than its exact selected pin. That pinned suite\n+does not declare `adapter.contract`: the preserved native `contractMode` is\n+therefore `null`. `runnerContractInterpretation: MAIN_SELF_GRADING` describes\n+the observed main runner behavior separately. PR52 was also open at the source observation at\n+`7eaf8995748ec4a00cb313463d2555da8fea25b4`; its changes are not imported.\n+\n+`sourceMaturity: STABLE` identifies the merged source relation and\n+`sourceState: PUBLIC_MAIN` excludes open-PR behavior. Adapter `maturity:\n+EXPERIMENTAL` identifies the new bounded product integration. Neither establishes\n+production security, complete upstream conformance, or a real-world poisoning detector.\n+\n+## Input and execution\n+\n+`evaluateTrustless(input, context)` accepts:\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"profile\": \"scan_subject_binding.v0\",\n+  \"source_pin\": \"1a37bcaf91918fd8a98f164d97d0fddbc28c6755\",\n+  \"case_id\": \"receiptos_positive\",\n+  \"input\": {\n+    \"public_key_ed25519\": \"<64 lowercase hex digits>\",\n+    \"toy_scan\": {\"scanner_version\": \"declared/version\", \"pattern\": \"declared-pattern\"},\n+    \"corpus\": [{\"id\": \"document-id\", \"content\": \"document content\"}],\n+    \"manifest\": {\"body\": {\"rag_corpus\": {}}, \"sig\": \"<128 lowercase hex digits>\"},\n+    \"decision\": {}\n+  },\n+  \"artifact\": {\"profile\": \"scan_subject_binding.v0\", \"results\": [], \"total\": 1, \"reproduced\": 1}\n+}\n+```\n+\n+The abbreviated manifest, decision and artifact above illustrate field\n+placement and are not a valid fixture. `buildTrustlessEvidence()` in the test\n+helper constructs complete fresh synthetic inputs and captures genuine native\n+CLI JSON. Its positive and negative expectations are independent literals.\n+No upstream captured datasets or upstream test signing credentials are copied.\n+The helper uses an explicitly public RFC8032 test seed; it is not a secret or\n+an accepted production authority.\n+\n+The supplied artifact is the actual `scan_check.py` JSON format: `profile`,\n+`results[{case_id,reproduced,result}]`, `total`, `reproduced`. A selected row must\n+contain `replay_bindings`, `result_only_check`, `subject_bound_check` and\n+`evidence_grade`; native refused-binding controls may also contain\n+`replay_failures`. Multi-row artifacts are admitted, but only the explicitly\n+selected case is replayed. Empty, duplicate or inconsistent inventories fail\n+admission. The `c0` answer-flip demonstration has a different result contract\n+and is unsupported by this bounded scan-result adapter.\n+\n+Execution first calls native `check_decision`, `sig_ok`, `subject_bound`, and\n+`result_only` without reading the saved artifact's expectations. It independently\n+recomputes signature validity, Merkle/root and retrieval/answer bindings, the\n+bound scan subject, and the declared deterministic scanner's outcome.\n+\n+The bridge then creates a fresh one-case conformance capsule. It copies the\n+unchanged native checker/spec, supplies freshly pinned vector bytes, and makes\n+an ephemeral suite declaration whose only command is that checker under the\n+current Python interpreter. It executes the unchanged native CLI and\n+`run_conformance.run_suite`. Original main's reference `suite.json` is retained\n+as source evidence; the entire original conformance-plus-mutation suite is not\n+claimed executed. No caller-supplied command, path, interpreter or URL executes.\n+Temporary paths are excluded from canonical result identity and removed after\n+the run. Python standard library is the only additional runtime dependency.\n+\n+## Separate native and product meanings\n+\n+| Preserved item | Meaning |\n+| --- | --- |\n+| suite/check/case IDs | Exactly the bounded native profile and selected case |\n+| runner `PASS` | Native program reproduced its saved target |\n+| `NO_FINDING` | Declared scanner found nothing in its bound subject |\n+| `CONTRADICTED` | Native deterministic scan disagrees with the signed clean assertion |\n+| `CANNOT_ESTABLISH` / `NOT_VALID` | Native refusal, with no evidence grade |\n+| `REPRODUCED` evidence grade | Native deterministic scanner was rerun |\n+| `AUTHENTICATED_REPORT` grade | Signed bound assertion; scanner-origin execution is not established |\n+| product `REPRODUCED` / `DIVERGED` | Saved native result equality / disagreement |\n+| `CANNOT_RECOMPUTE` | Native source/runtime/parser/runner unavailable or invalid output |\n+\n+The layer status is a replay state; it is never an overall `VERIFIED` label.\n+`semanticOutcome` separately maps bounded native `NO_FINDING` to `VERIFIED`,\n+contradiction or invalid binding to `REFUTED`, and unresolved evidence to\n+`UNVERIFIABLE`. This is a result for the named bounded scan relation, not\n+`POISONING_ABSENT` or proof of arbitrary correctness. The generic product\n+compatibility and evidence-sufficiency layers must still authorize the\n+caller-selected claim and accepted evidence grade.\n+\n+A real native runner `PASS` can accompany a correctly reproduced\n+`CONTRADICTED` result. It remains negative. A fabricated saved positive result\n+cannot change the raw native computation; it produces `DIVERGED`. Canonical\n+runner exit 0 by itself is never a semantic result. Runner `DRIFT` is unavailable\n+source identity, not semantic failure. Exceptions/crashes and malformed or empty\n+output are `CANNOT_RECOMPUTE`, not contradiction.\n+\n+## Claim and subject binding\n+\n+The product binds `claim.kind = TRUSTLESS_CHECK` and claim parameters\n+`profile`, `case_id`, `input_digest` to the adapter's independently observed\n+`nativeBinding`. The bound `input_digest` is SHA-256 of the exact canonical\n+`input` object, including manifest, public key, scanner declaration, decision\n+and corpus; it is also `observedArtifactDigest`. The product-selected subject\n+can name this native case and those exact bytes. The digest does not replace\n+the generic authority/scope/policy/time/dependency relation.\n+\n+The distinct native subject remains inspectable as `observedSubject` and\n+`nativeBinding.subject`: the effective-dataset Merkle digest and declared\n+scanner version. `binding` also preserves corpus root, signed scan subject,\n+signature validity, scanner declaration, query and k. A signed scan of one\n+dataset cannot establish another dataset; the native profile remains frozen\n+to k=1 and its explicit recordwise transfer rule.\n+\n+## Contribution and limitations\n+\n+The scan checker is authored by babyblueviper1, with its README documenting\n+Pavlo's effective-dataset witness/review contribution. Commit\n+`a05099ee5674f40148ee88ddf5105fdcf2fda607` explicitly credits Zexo and Pavlo's\n+evidence-grade refusal finding. Pavlo's exact authored runner failure-classifier\n+implementation is commit `ce28d6888b224dd8551d0d1a1196a6cd706420cd`; the overall\n+runner also contains babyblueviper1, Merlini/Echo and Zexo contributions. No\n+sole authorship is inferred from repository ownership or review.\n+\n+This adapter does not execute arbitrary recompute-kit suites, scanner binaries,\n+live services, PR57 reporters, private Vértice code, or full main mutation\n+inventory. `AUTHENTICATED_REPORT` does not prove scanner-origin execution.\n+The public supplied key's signature validity does not establish an external\n+authority identity. A caller's broader authority, scope, version, policy,\n+dependencies and evidence basis remain independently checked product premises."},{"sha":"4d7a13df126802a8f5b57cd6d0419711d2ba7ceb","filename":"docs/v0.2-architecture.md","status":"added","additions":31,"deletions":0,"changes":31,"blob_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/blob/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/docs%2Fv0.2-architecture.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/raw/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/docs%2Fv0.2-architecture.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/contents/docs%2Fv0.2-architecture.md?ref=396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@\n+# v0.2 architecture\n+\n+This is an additive versioned boundary over the public v0.1.0 implementation. The public tag peels to `62cd3e59c8f568496ed087d55f0aec3d63363b0a`, tree `8a5de5a3735e04f3f45cf164b59da17289693bc2`. The historical pre-publication candidate is not the public base. Original request/bundle/report v1 schemas, thirty vectors and fourteen mutation definitions remain regression inputs.\n+\n+`verify()` dispatches request v2 to `verifyV2()`; otherwise the audited v1 admission and verification path remains in place. V2 has separate schemas, admission, signing domain and projection. V1 capsules continue to use their explicit v1 interchange contract; no compatibility is inferred for v2 capsules.\n+\n+The pipeline is strict admission, canonicalization, committed-attachment/payload integrity, native Crystal root verification, product Ed25519 authentication, requested/evidence surface comparison, pinned native recomputation, evidence sufficiency, optional PRF transfer and Chronicle continuity, then a finite product projection. Computations may be performed before all gates are established so a report can preserve each observation. This does not authorize a gate bypass.\n+\n+All fourteen layers remain visible. Native outcomes and replay are independent fields. The Semantic ABI compatibility layer executes the public neutral manifest validator and linker; optional detached pair evaluation never invents an expected pair from evidence. Crystal/RVR keep their public pins. The Trustless integration executes the main `scan_subject_binding.v0` checker and canonical conformance runner, preserving the actual artifact and its self-grading runner interpretation separately. Interpoll executes the unchanged public Schnorr verifier and a bounded product retry relation. PRF executes the unchanged main award/actual-settlement relation and a separately labeled experimental transfer rule derived from open PR14.\n+\n+The generic core contains no Ethereum or XRPL semantics. The existing ledger boundary reserves off-chain/unanchored, Ethereum and XRPL. There is no live chain implementation or finality claim.\n+\n+Evidence cannot select executable paths, commands, network destinations or source pins. No upstream worktree is changed. Only selected neutral public source files are vendored, with byte hashes, original grants and contributor evidence. See the provenance and third-party notices.\n+\n+## Bounded claims\n+\n+V2 does not implement arbitrary logical entailment. It supports exact structured claim-surface identity plus independently supplied premise checks. Primitive claim kinds have explicit native bindings:\n+\n+| Kind | Actual relation | Permitted evidence-declared scope |\n+|---|---|---|\n+| SHA256_EQUALS | Native RVR digest predicate and saved-artifact replay | `{\"evidence_member\":\"artifact\"}` |\n+| TRUSTLESS_CHECK | Pinned scan-subject-binding case over the exact committed input | Exact case ID and `scan-subject-binding` relation |\n+| SIGNED_ACTION_TRACE | Signed intent, supplied accepted/attempt/observation trace and trace commitment | Native namespace and `supplied-trace-only` observation |\n+\n+Other signed declarations cannot expand these capabilities. In particular a clean toy scan is not poisoning absence, supplied action observations are not authenticated server execution, and receipt publisher authority is not provider/hardware authority.\n+\n+PRF is a separately selected award/settlement obligation. Its caller-owned input digest and expected native result bind that tuple. It does not transfer the current RVR/Trustless result automatically. A reproduced negative PRF tuple can retain a PRESERVED transfer relation while its native result remains negative.\n+\n+## Deterministic identity\n+\n+Canonical inputs and semantic/native result identities are deterministic. Execution command receipts include the actual host paths, runtime versions and captured stdout/stderr; those operational fields are outside semantic identity. The v0.2 determinism gate compares complete semantic reports after removing only execution `argv` fields, and retains exact raw command receipts separately. No native verdict, reason, source pin, evidence digest or claim field is excluded."},{"sha":"bd8d2e72b1a2fc8404b76a56e468155d4b101977","filename":"docs/v0.2-vector-mutation-witnesses.md","status":"added","additions":204,"deletions":0,"changes":204,"blob_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/blob/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/docs%2Fv0.2-vector-mutation-witnesses.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/raw/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/docs%2Fv0.2-vector-mutation-witnesses.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/contents/docs%2Fv0.2-vector-mutation-witnesses.md?ref=396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,204 @@\n+# ReceiptOS Verify v0.2 vector and mutation witnesses\n+\n+This review accounts for all **38 new static vectors** (`G01`-`G30`, `I01`-`I08`) and all **14 semantic mutants** (`M01`-`M14`). The original 30 v0.1 vectors remain a separate regression corpus, giving 68 combined vectors. Counts describe cases and catalog entries; they do not imply 38 independent relations or exhaustive security coverage.\n+\n+The inputs are the checked-in `vectors/v0.2/<ID>.json` files, not dynamically generated expected outputs. `tools/generate-v02-vectors.mjs` records literal expected projections, 14 layer statuses, selected native values and required reason codes. It never calls `verifyV2`, `projectV2` or an adapter to calculate the expected product verdict. This document reads those literal expectations and the recorded results; it is not a second implementation of the verifier.\n+\n+## Oracle origins and limits\n+\n+| Oracle family | Origin of the literal expectation | Independence and evidence boundary |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| O-GEN/RVR | Human-selected equality/inequality, dependency, applicability and evidence-presence premises in `tools/generate-v02-vectors.mjs`, plus the literal SHA256 predicate of a fresh synthetic artifact. | Product expectations are detached from verifier output. Fixture construction still shares canonicalization, signing and surface-extraction utilities with production; this is not an independently implemented canonicalizer, signer or schema oracle. RVR's saved artifact is generated native evidence, not the product expectation. |\n+| O-GEN/SABI | Literal compatible/incompatible semantic declaration and literal native pair expectation; unchanged public neutral linker executes at its pinned source. | Product JSON strings encode native v0 claim/scope/time fields. Subject, artifact, authority ID, policy, version and dependency checks remain product relations. `observedSemanticPair=PRESERVED` does not mean the full generic surface is compatible. Native pair grading uses no expected pair invented from its own observed result. |\n+| O-KIT | `tests/helpers/trustless-v02-fixture.mjs` contains independent literal positive, poison-negative and opaque-scanner outcomes; one-leaf Merkle construction is independent of the native checker. Actual unchanged checker CLI generates saved artifacts. | The adapter reruns the checker and main runner; saved expectations serve only as replay targets. Runner PASS can reproduce a negative result. The deliberately narrow toy scanner is not a poisoning-absence proof or full recompute-kit conformance. Opaque scanner authentication is not scanner execution. |\n+| O-ACTION | Explicit synthetic up intent and separate caller-selected action; exact material identity, attempt, observation and duplicate premises are selected literally. Native upstream Schnorr verification executes. | Fixture construction uses product `actionMaterial` and `commitActionTrace`; therefore correct construction of the trace commitment is not independently proved by this corpus. Fresh synthetic key control and a supplied trace do not establish real Interpoll admission, server execution, freshness or a deployed actor identity. |\n+| O-PRF | Literal finalized award/accepted matching settlement, amount 50, native PRESERVED result, missing-settlement UNVERIFIABLE result and two independently caller-accepted dependency identities. Unchanged native main relation executes on the selected tuple. | The dependency basis is caller-accepted, not discovered or proven complete by this adapter. The guarantee concerns the separately selected award/settlement tuple and transfer relation; it does not silently become a guarantee about the surrounding RVR claim. Open PR14 informs the experimental product transfer relation, not main-source behavior or wire compatibility. |\n+\n+All fixtures are synthetic. The same project authors selected the relations and literals; there is no claim of organizationally independent audit authorship. Native source execution supplies an additional executable comparison where described, not an independent proof of every wrapper decision.\n+\n+## Literal expectation convention\n+\n+Every vector explicitly stores all 14 expected layer statuses. The common base is:\n+\n+| Layer | Literal base status |\n+| --- | --- |\n+| INPUT | `ADMITTED` |\n+| CANONICALIZATION | `VERIFIED` |\n+| INTEGRITY | `VERIFIED` |\n+| AUTHENTICITY | `VERIFIED` |\n+| SUBJECT_BINDING | `VERIFIED` |\n+| RECOMPUTATION | `REPRODUCED` |\n+| EVIDENCE_SUFFICIENCY | `SUFFICIENT` |\n+| SEMANTIC_COMPATIBILITY | `COMPATIBLE` |\n+| GUARANTEE_PRESERVATION | `NOT_REQUESTED` |\n+| CONTINUITY | `NOT_REQUESTED` |\n+| DOMAIN_ADAPTERS | `NOT_REQUESTED` |\n+| PRODUCT_PROJECTION | `VERIFIED` |\n+| EXPLAINABLE_REPORT | `GENERATED` |\n+| PROVENANCE | `RECORDED` |\n+\n+The following matrix lists every deviation from that base and every required reason. `PRODUCT_PROJECTION` always equals the literal overall result. Unlisted layer statuses retain the table above. `R` means `RECOMPUTATION.semanticOutcome`; `Pair` means `SEMANTIC_COMPATIBILITY.observedSemanticPair`. `runner`, `scan`, `signature`, `grade` and `PRF upstream` are the selected literal native keys, not Boolean aliases for overall verification.\n+\n+Reason checks require the listed codes to be present. They do **not** lock the complete reason array or forbid additional diagnostic reasons. Native-key checks likewise select explicit paths rather than independently validating every byte of the complete native report; strict report admission and adapter-specific tests provide separate controls.\n+\n+## Complete new-vector witness matrix\n+\n+| Vector | Exact input change / relation and oracle family | Literal native expectation | Literal product, layer changes and required reasons | Positive control | Defect / coverage assessment |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| [G01](../vectors/v0.2/G01.json) | RVR SHA256_EQUALS positive: the caller-selected digest, native predicate, supplied artifact, subject and signed declaration agree. **O-GEN/RVR** | R=`VERIFIED`; Pair=`PRESERVED` | Overall **VERIFIED**; base layers. Reasons: none required. | G01 (base); negatives below | **POSITIVE_CONTROL**. Positive control for generic failures; no measured mutant witness. |\n+| [G02](../vectors/v0.2/G02.json) | Only caller subject.commit becomes 40 b characters; receipt commit and identical artifact stay A. Commit identity must remain caller-selected. **O-GEN/RVR** | R=`VERIFIED`; Pair=`PRESERVED` | Overall **CONTRADICTED**; SUBJECT_BINDING=`CONTRADICTED`; SEMANTIC_COMPATIBILITY=`CONTRADICTED`; PRODUCT_PROJECTION=`CONTRADICTED`. Reasons: `SUBJECT_MISMATCH`. | G01 | **DISTINCT_FIELD_WITNESS**. Detects ignoring commit; no v0.2 catalog mutant measured here. |\n+| [G03](../vectors/v0.2/G03.json) | Only caller subject.id becomes synthetic:other; artifact and commit remain equal. Evidence subject cannot be compared to itself. **O-GEN/RVR** | R=`VERIFIED`; Pair=`PRESERVED` | Overall **CONTRADICTED**; SUBJECT_BINDING=`CONTRADICTED`; SEMANTIC_COMPATIBILITY=`CONTRADICTED`; PRODUCT_PROJECTION=`CONTRADICTED`. Reasons: `SUBJECT_MISMATCH`. | G01 | **MEASURED_WITNESS**. M06 measured witness. |\n+| [G04](../vectors/v0.2/G04.json) | Only call