ot invent another execution. |\n+| [I05](../vectors/v0.2/I05.json) | Keep first accepted/executed signed up attempt; append pending, non-executed retry-attempt with changed down value. Same request/bundle as G14. **O-ACTION** | R=`REFUTED`; Pair=`PRESERVED`; signature=`VALID` | Overall **CONTRADICTED**; DOMAIN_ADAPTERS=`CONTRADICTED`; PRODUCT_PROJECTION=`CONTRADICTED`. Reasons: `RETRY_AUTHORIZED_ACTION_CHANGED`. | I04 | **REDUNDANT_ALIAS**. M09-associated domain alias; the measured catalog witness is G14. I04 is the matching multi-attempt positive. |\n+| [I06](../vectors/v0.2/I06.json) | Acceptance and sole attempt become duplicate, with execution_attempted false; a supplied APPLIED observation still points to that duplicate attempt. Duplicate acceptance alone cannot establish new execution. **O-ACTION** | R=`UNVERIFIABLE`; Pair=`PRESERVED`; signature=`VALID` | Overall **INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE**; DOMAIN_ADAPTERS=`INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE`; PRODUCT_PROJECTION=`INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE`. Reasons: `ACTION_NEW_EXECUTION_NOT_ESTABLISHED`. | I01 | **DISTINCT_FAILURE_WITNESS**. Distinct execution-sufficiency branch; no catalog mutant measured. |\n+| [I07](../vectors/v0.2/I07.json) | Set observation to null and refresh trace commitment, digest and signature. Intact authorized intent cannot replace an execution observation. **O-ACTION** | R=`UNVERIFIABLE`; Pair=`PRESERVED`; signature=`VALID` | Overall **INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE**; DOMAIN_ADAPTERS=`INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE`; PRODUCT_PROJECTION=`INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE`. Reasons: `ACTION_EXECUTION_OBSERVATION_MISSING`. | I01 | **DISTINCT_FAILURE_WITNESS**. Distinct missing-observation branch; no catalog mutant measured. |\n+| [I08](../vectors/v0.2/I08.json) | Caller action-authority namespace becomes unsupported while the valid signed action retains namespace v1. **O-ACTION** | R=`UNVERIFIABLE`; Pair=`PRESERVED`; signature=`VALID` | Overall **UNSUPPORTED_PROFILE**; DOMAIN_ADAPTERS=`UNSUPPORTED_PROFILE`; PRODUCT_PROJECTION=`UNSUPPORTED_PROFILE`. Reasons: `ACTION_AUTHORITY_UNSUPPORTED`. | I01 | **DISTINCT_FAILURE_WITNESS**. Domain authority support control; differs from generic authority-ID mismatch G04/G19. |\n+\n+## Overlap, control selection and metadata corrections\n+\n+- `G13`/`I01` are exact request/bundle aliases, and `G14`/`I05` are exact request/bundle aliases. They preserve the requested general/domain listings, but contribute two positive/negative scenarios, not four independent scenarios.\n+- `G04`/`G19` differ only in the mismatching authority ID value and exercise the same authority branch. The measured M01 witness is G04.\n+- `G01`/`G09` share the artifact replay relation and global Semantic ABI evaluation. G09 additionally exercises the semantic-abi selector route; it is not another independently implemented content verifier.\n+- `G05`/`G10` share exact-scope rejection and neutral linker failure, using different literal scopes and adapter selector labels. Only G05 is the measured M02 witness.\n+- `G11`/`G18` both exercise claim mismatch. Their mutation controls differ: native Trustless positive bypass (M07) versus integrity/signature bypass (M12). This is overlapping defense coverage against distinct projection defects.\n+- `G02`, `G03`, `G22` and `G25` change different identity dimensions; they are not four independent native verifiers. `I02`/`I03` likewise exercise different material action fields through the same equality branch.\n+- `G07`/`G08` now name G23, the satisfied dependency premise, as their positive control in both static metadata and the generator. This corrected metadata only; request, bundle and literal expectations were unchanged. G10's misleading M02 annotation was removed; the relation remains covered. Metadata associating G19 with M01 and I05 with M09 is a defect association, not an additional recorded mutation execution.\n+- G14/I05 were strengthened from changing the sole attempt to changing a real **second** pending retry after an unchanged accepted/executed first attempt. The exact trace commitment, native-input digest, signed surface and outer signature were refreshed; expected statuses/reasons stayed literal and unchanged. I04 preserves matching repeated intent. The strengthened G14 still kills M09 with the positive preserved.\n+\n+`G23` establishes only that an explicit caller-accepted SATISFIED premise permits continuation. It does not prove dependency discovery, independent remote premise verification or the truth of a caller-supplied assertion. This boundary applies equally to the PRF accepted dependency basis.\n+\n+## Complete new-mutant matrix\n+\n+The canonical catalog is `mutations/catalog-v2.mjs`; the detailed receipt is `reports/v0.2/mutations.json`. A kill requires exactly applied changed source, valid literal baseline expectations, a preserved positive control, complete valid host output, usable native execution/output and a changed semantic product projection. Every source patch records original/mutant SHA-256 plus exactly-one occurrence and changed replacement hashes. A well-formed but wrong semantic verdict remains admissible as a witness; the harness does not recompute the implementation's projection to decide its expected answer.\n+\n+| Mutant | Exact defect / modified relation | Preserved positive | Measured witness | Recorded baseline -> mutant | Assessment |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| M01 | ignore authority identity; `src/core/claim-surface.mjs` | G01 | G04 | `CONTRADICTED` -> `VERIFIED` | `KILLED`; applied=true, positive preserved=true, both processes `COMPLETED`/`COMPLETED`. |\n+| M02 | ignore scope at both product and native semantic link; `src/core/claim-surface.mjs`, `src/adapters/semantic-abi-v2.mjs` | G01 | G05 | `CONTRADICTED` -> `VERIFIED` | `KILLED`; applied=true, positive preserved=true, both processes `COMPLETED`/`COMPLETED`. Combined mutation changes both product scope comparison and native scope encoding; it does not claim separately measured kills for each single weakening. |\n+| M03 | ignore policy version; `src/core/claim-surface.mjs` | G01 | G06 | `CONTRADICTED` -> `VERIFIED` | `KILLED`; applied=true, positive preserved=true, both processes `COMPLETED`/`COMPLETED`. |\n+| M04 | ignore dependency premise presence; `src/core/claim-surface.mjs` | G23 | G07 | `INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE` -> `VERIFIED` | `KILLED`; applied=true, positive preserved=true, both processes `COMPLETED`/`COMPLETED`. |\n+| M05 | ignore dependency contradiction; `src/core/claim-surface.mjs` | G23 | G08 | `CONTRADICTED` -> `VERIFIED` | `KILLED`; applied=true, positive preserved=true, both processes `COMPLETED`/`COMPLETED`. |\n+| M06 | compare evidence subject to itself; `src/core/claim-surface.mjs` | G01 | G03 | `CONTRADICTED` -> `VERIFIED` | `KILLED`; applied=true, positive preserved=true, both processes `COMPLETED`/`COMPLETED`. |\n+| M07 | native positive bypasses semantic compatibility; `src/projection/project-v2.mjs` | G24 | G11 | `CONTRADICTED` -> `VERIFIED` | `KILLED`; applied=true, positive preserved=true, both processes `COMPLETED`/`COMPLETED`. |\n+| M08 | promote reproduced negative to verified; `src/projection/project-v2.mjs` | G24 | G12 | `CONTRADICTED` -> `VERIFIED` | `KILLED`; applied=true, positive preserved=true, both processes `COMPLETED`/`COMPLETED`. Two replacements remove the explicit negative rejection and permit REFUTED at the final positivity gate. |\n+| M09 | allow retry to mutate signed material action; `src/adapters/interpoll-v2.mjs` | G13 | G14 | `CONTRADICTED` -> `VERIFIED` | `KILLED`; applied=true, positive preserved=true, both processes `COMPLETED`/`COMPLETED`. Witness now changes a second pending retry; signature and first matching execution remain intact. |\n+| M10 | collapse native PRF UNVERIFIABLE to preserved; `src/adapters/prf-v2.mjs` | G15 | G21 | `INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE` -> `VERIFIED` | `KILLED`; applied=true, positive preserved=true, both processes `COMPLETED`/`COMPLETED`. |\n+| M11 | ignore requested claim version; `src/core/claim-surface.mjs` | G01 | G22 | `CONTRADICTED` -> `VERIFIED` | `KILLED`; applied=true, positive preserved=true, both processes `COMPLETED`/`COMPLETED`. The witness changes top-level claim version only; it does not separately measure subject-version mutation. |\n+| M12 | integrity and signature override contradiction; `src/projection/project-v2.mjs` | G01 | G18 | `CONTRADICTED` -> `VERIFIED` | `KILLED`; applied=true, positive preserved=true, both processes `COMPLETED`/`COMPLETED`. |\n+| M13 | promote authenticated scan report grade to local scanner recomputation; `src/core/evidence-v2.mjs` | G24 | G29 | `INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE` -> `VERIFIED` | `KILLED`; applied=true, positive preserved=true, both processes `COMPLETED`/`COMPLETED`. The authenticated native assertion remains preserved while the strict local-scanner grade requirement is incorrectly removed. |\n+\n+| M14 | hide requested PRF native negative behind preserved transfer; `src/projection/project-v2.mjs`: replace extraction of guarantee.productProjection at the exact prf-product marker with null | G15 | G30 | `CONTRADICTED` -> `VERIFIED` | `KILLED`; applied=true, positive preserved=true, both processes `COMPLETED`/`COMPLETED`. This measures requested-guarantee composition, not the native PRF relation or the correctness of the caller-accepted dependency basis. |\n+\n+The 14 catalog entries are a selected fault model. The kill ratio is not a percentage of all possible implementation defects, proof of full native conformance, or a count of all vector branches. Defects without a measured catalog mutant are explicitly identified in the vector matrix. The original 14 v0.1 mutants are a separate retained regression run, not relabeled as new v0.2 coverage.\n+\n+## Mutation negative controls and before/after evidence\n+\n+`tests/mutation-v2.test.mjs` now contains **8 focused tests**, all observed passing in `node --test tests/mutation-v2.test.mjs` after the harness fix. Canonical test command receipts and complete TAP output are retained by the overall review gate. A passing negative-control test means the harness correctly refused successful mutation coverage, not that the deliberately broken mutant was killed.\n+\n+| Control | Exact intervention | Required/observed classification and evidence |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| Empty inventory | Call `auditMutants([])` | Throws `ZERO_MUTANTS`; cannot produce a passing zero-denominator report. |\n+| Unapplied mutation | Required source text does not exist | `NOT_APPLIED`, applied=false, KILLED=0, passed=false. |\n+| No-op mutation | Replacement is identical to original | `NOT_APPLIED`, applied=false, KILLED=0, passed=false; separate from unapplied text in the same test. |\n+| Host crash | Inject `process.exit(7)` immediately inside verifyV2 | Actual process `CRASH`; classification `CRASHED`, KILLED=0, passed=false. |\n+| Invalid host output | Inject `return null` inside verifyV2 | `INVALID_OUTPUT`, KILLED=0, passed=false; no malformed report becomes a semantic witness. |\n+| Broken positive | Change final positive projection to well-formed CONTRADICTED/BROKEN_POSITIVE_CONTROL | Positive process still COMPLETED, positive_preserved=false; `CONTROL_BROKEN`, KILLED=0, passed=false. |\n+| Inner checker crash | Bridge exits 7 only when the corpus contains poison; G24 positive remains normal, G12 is the witness | Host witness report is valid/COMPLETED with product CANNOT_RECOMPUTE; recursive execution evidence detects failed native checker. `CRASHED`, checker_execution_failed=true, KILLED=0, positive preserved. |\n+| Invalid inner native output with exit 0 | Bridge emits literal JSON null and exits 0 only on poison; G24 positive remains normal | Host witness report remains valid/COMPLETED, exit 0, product CANNOT_RECOMPUTE. `INVALID_OUTPUT`, checker_output_invalid=true, checker_execution_failed=false, KILLED=0, positive preserved. |\n+| Legitimate native semantic refusal | Direct classifier control with TRUSTLESS_NATIVE_NOT_VALID / semanticVerdict NOT_VALID | Not classified as malformed output. Native NOT_VALID is a valid negative vocabulary item; existing adapter tests independently exercise native refusal behavior. This classifier test is not counted as an executed semantic mutant. |\n+\n+During this review, the inner-null control exposed a real harness defect: the original harness counted a well-formed host CANNOT_RECOMPUTE result as KILLED merely because it differed from baseline CONTRADICTED. `reports/v0.2/mutation-invalid-native-before.json` records an actual fresh pre-fix probe, exact UTC start/end, source and input SHA-256 identities, full reproduction source, G24/G12 IDs and the false successful kill receipt. This was recorded before changing the harness, not reconstructed afterward.\n+\n+The correction is confined to the mutation harness. It rejects known checker transport/output failure codes and non-semantic CANNOT_RECOMPUTE/REJECTED_MALFORMED outcomes, while preserving actual nested crashes as CRASHED and native NOT_VALID as semantic. The focused post-fix inner-null control records INVALID_OUTPUT and zero kills through executable assertions. A malformed-output testing contract would need a separately explicit fault model; this semantic catalog has none.\n+\n+A separate product finding is covered by G29/M13: native authenticated opaque scanner assertions previously satisfied LOCAL_RECOMPUTATION policy. `reports/v0.2/grade-finding-before.json` truthfully retains the actual earlier stdout and explicitly identifies absent full input/report files, source snapshot hash and timestamp. The product guard and `tests/trustless-grade-v2.test.mjs` preserve the native AUTHENTICATED_REPORT result but require product INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE. Wrapper replay must not upgrade scanner execution grade.\n+\n+\n+A **HIGH composition finding** is covered by G30/M14. The pre-fix core replaced the top-level guarantee status with its transfer status, so a correctly reproduced native PRF VIOLATED result with a PRESERVED transfer was presented as overall VERIFIED. Correct transfer of a negative conclusion preserves that negative conclusion; it does not certify a positive relation. The same composition path also weakened unsupported, malformed and unavailable checker outcomes into mere insufficiency.\n+\n+`reports/v0.2/prf-composition-finding-before.json` retains actual read-only pre-fix probes with full inputs/reports, UTC times, runtime, source SHA-256 values, input digests and explicitly recorded fault injection. Its reproduced-negative-preserved case records native VIOLATED / amount_mismatch, native replay REPRODUCED, transfer PRESERVED and the incorrect overall VERIFIED. G30's oracle is a fresh independently selected literal 50-versus-100 mismatch, not an expected answer generated from the projection. The fixed projection separately validates and consumes guarantee.productProjection without erasing PRESERVED transfer; G30 requires overall CONTRADICTED while G15 still permits VERIFIED. M14 removes only this product projection consumption and is killed by the changed semantic result with G15 preserved.\n+\n+G30 adds a distinct composition witness to G16's changed-dependency transfer failure and G21's UNVERIFIABLE native relation. It remains one bounded supplied award/settlement tuple. It proves neither real settlement provenance, completeness of the caller's accepted basis, nor a semantic link between that tuple and the surrounding positive RVR artifact predicate. The surrounding RVR result intentionally remains VERIFIED to expose the independent requested-guarantee obligation.\n+\n+## Receipt interpretation and remaining limits\n+\n+`reports/v0.2/vectors.json` records the original 30 plus these 38 cases; `reports/v0.2/mutations.json` records the 14 selected new mutants and patch identities. The final review report owns the canonical rerun after the fixture and harness corrections above. Earlier full-suite receipts with failures remain evidence of those earlier runs; a successful vector/mutation subset is not a claim that an unrelated whole-suite command passed.\n+\n+This document establishes no universal semantic entailment, real-world scanner accuracy, independent server execution provenance, general retry-state-machine proof, production cryptographic certification, completeness of a caller-accepted dependency basis or all-profile conformance. Exact scope compatibility is conservative equality. G27 covers one explicit exclusive interval boundary. No new continuity/ledger relation is claimed by these 38 cases; those boundaries rely on the separately retained v0.1 suite and documented interface limits.\n+\n+No circular product oracle was found in the literal expectation generator. Shared fixture construction utilities and the duplicated/overlapping cases above remain material limits on independence; literal expectations are not automatically correct because they are detached. The native-key subset and reason-subset assertions do not prove all unasserted fields. No unresolved implementation defect is claimed here after the explicitly recorded fixes; the final release recommendation remains conditional on the root canonical gate and independent release audit.\n+\n+## Exact static input inventory\n+\n+These SHA-256 values identify the complete JSON vector files, including input and literal oracle metadata, after the G07/G08/G10 metadata correction, strengthened G14/I05 retry inputs and new G30 preserved-negative composition witness. They are file identity evidence, not semantic correctness evidence.\n+\n+| Vector | SHA-256 of static vector file |\n+| --- | --- |\n+| G01 | `5727fe2a9ade58c90ca76101d0bae92936f060ab89dd8c43d8f8e580d2729c21` |\n+| G02 | `c2c816c1c4fd606f54648cc6ebcca213d5c60ad61af1f27f8debdfafdc478982` |\n+| G03 | `e6144cb1d92147f2af3361ff407fb16d79e2f156e40321606041dbe0a9e2d522` |\n+| G04 | `203ac24477f36bf7c7639565a033f1e15e8ebcbc90bba7aad745e80e12e30632` |\n+| G05 | `8601d66716fe17b8359e3517ca59be88a0863fe5956a0823e5eed68c7806dfd5` |\n+| G06 | `ded90f38ab4acf098da849d8ce3ee29e03ece2fc216a2652dbb6bef0160ec146` |\n+| G07 | `965908533d3450b9c73be753c0a3dc5412fd2a94945db77c13c145e458e372d6` |\n+| G08 | `73cb0e5de47bcc25e7e5a98f1efd93ba30214121244d2de7397cb7ebdb40333d` |\n+| G09 | `b8d0ffa04c2842a6a6c621cde87308abc7e0fcca32f02c972e9a5e6a7b5a4878` |\n+| G10 | `da439f4ae911a6cc7f031adff628319d55a10c3bd6e0e95590eaf6c2fd5f4254` |\n+| G11 | `3c373bd478ea1746cad1478b7705d314038b46929904d380dee93bb4ab9b9eaf` |\n+| G12 | `fafd048e8e716ac2cd51d9a2095f1bfd49d52b3b1e99986e405968f8fc88708a` |\n+| G13 | `e6dd3a7828f707384694d5c44585eacc9b90ef64d7aa12e6df220c3c306d5a59` |\n+| G14 | `a3e2a4518b9b3f8d39225a73e17cc6b767a1ef8ca3f8a9487c925a48733e97d2` |\n+| G15 | `8cd47ee20e89a87e58c5f0d2238abfad07a25e9780360e3774f833ee66ea0bd7` |\n+| G16 | `cf2cf3b8baeb5648acb167ad8249550dc8d76f990a752cb105423662e6a39cc3` |\n+| G17 | `74c5317210ae934b45c0f8462cb949017920400e661fe754e096501beb70199e` |\n+| G18 | `abe86e0d1dfd22e4cf57bd401c99e56abea9b6b8f9e8c23c3ac748ce8bb0338d` |\n+| G19 | `fdb7dcd29fb8018b553d7f6892e408ce945ec9a539b0348dd20ec67dabab3028` |\n+| G20 | `3137f3955e8a5e3a1cf50ba032e8c0d89bd0915861aa1fd21d78471356bd9dca` |\n+| G21 | `0fd57affe79447474ea36d433498c1607d306cd9f5ccc3ff3a2db59319f7c4de` |\n+| G22 | `1a3904d76db8f7deddc9d82a9aabf0ddee64c4d76be318cc5c389990a435164d` |\n+| G23 | `7d507244777be5a838b7fa2aa0855f03d5a0137466a629170630c7c38a977799` |\n+| G24 | `d6cc30a3175d30044dd0b622be7318e6d244741f5f0205ab9862b9248ed0d2be` |\n+| G25 | `bcc29da9cb257a71c7c0fe38d4a0304550ed1f22b183425efc924570a1ae5519` |\n+| G26 | `6790ee7fc9901f161faa553817926cf5d833a40da64f1ffc5f249aa8485b7244` |\n+| G27 | `64ff3d037378f229fb3588451a5b0937dffee3f4be76c9d9c36ce37ed170d754` |\n+| G28 | `5ec2e9bbafedd09eb1de20ed84031d40c9d27d92bb0dfd047b6fd8ce471791d2` |\n+| G29 | `dedf24e7ec6b840fc395739afdf2e14e023db798b79bdc62d684ce1aad54590c` |\n+| G30 | `9e02177e42366795827ca4e719563eca367e019966c8a72796f49eb3f5d3b17e` |\n+| I01 | `3e13b8673486ec45be40405d9ea4c0d89f7c40afa256fbe92b3bf03d07246b59` |\n+| I02 | `2f8317f6c032c0a63b0316640f014979fbf17be5358bc03e385e52f2f8460a8c` |\n+| I03 | `548ff15fb09e50d39b92c032f9a5c467c9f3fae6c0e04e0f9508d25c67bfbdef` |\n+| I04 | `c9545b4a5e3d48b63b359a351a0fce85c28226636ad415d67dbc365f58959aae` |\n+| I05 | `ad416e47e9902aea87a379646f345a1eb2b0c44bec63a32b82dcb8af248e2bf7` |\n+| I06 | `ef28c92e2886b70c5e8b65d298c677287f6692364131b2f061da0b7f680604b7` |\n+| I07 | `56c480cea456fe160db7c493979b965925421b326f6dbee701e0abd6863bd98f` |\n+| I08 | `429eb6e7260c51e73ccbd81cd4587250f33461fe3edeaa72a63c4f74d0fcfcf5` |"},{"sha":"cee41e42116f8d690249e9e0fe0f977292de307f","filename":"mutations/catalog-v2.mjs","status":"added","additions":23,"deletions":0,"changes":23,"blob_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/blob/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/mutations%2Fcatalog-v2.mjs","raw_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/raw/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/mutations%2Fcatalog-v2.mjs","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/contents/mutations%2Fcatalog-v2.mjs?ref=396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@\n+const boundary='src/core/claim-surface.mjs', projection='src/projection/project-v2.mjs';\n+const patch=(file,from,to)=>({file,changes:[[from,to]]});\n+const compare=(field,code)=>`compare('${field}',requested.${field},evidence.${field},'${code}');`;\n+const ignored=field=>`add('${field}','COMPATIBLE',[]);`;\n+const inject=\"  const obligations = [...new Set([...REQUIRED_V2,...required])];\";\n+export const mutationsV2=[\n+  {id:'M01',defect:'ignore authority identity',positive:'G01',witness:'G04',patches:[patch(boundary,compare('authority','AUTHORITY_MISMATCH'),ignored('authority'))]},\n+  {id:'M02',defect:'ignore scope at both product and native semantic link',positive:'G01',witness:'G05',patches:[patch(boundary,compare('scope','SCOPE_MISMATCH'),ignored('scope')),patch('src/adapters/semantic-abi-v2.mjs','scope: encoded(surface.scope),','scope: encoded({}),')]},\n+  {id:'M03',defect:'ignore policy version',positive:'G01',witness:'G06',patches:[patch(boundary,compare('policy','POLICY_MISMATCH'),ignored('policy'))]},\n+  {id:'M04',defect:'ignore dependency premise presence',positive:'G23',witness:'G07',patches:[patch(boundary,\"if (!observed || observed.status !== 'SATISFIED' && observed.status !== 'CONTRADICTED') dependencyReasons.push('DEPENDENCY_MISSING');\",\"if (false) dependencyReasons.push('DEPENDENCY_MISSING');\")]},\n+  {id:'M05',defect:'ignore dependency contradiction',positive:'G23',witness:'G08',patches:[patch(boundary,\"if (observed?.status === 'CONTRADICTED') dependencyReasons.push('DEPENDENCY_CONTRADICTED');\",\"if (false) dependencyReasons.push('DEPENDENCY_CONTRADICTED');\")]},\n+  {id:'M06',defect:'compare evidence subject to itself',positive:'G01',witness:'G03',patches:[patch(boundary,\"compare('subject',identity(requested.subject),identity(evidence.subject),'SUBJECT_MISMATCH');\",\"compare('subject',identity(evidence.subject),identity(evidence.subject),'SUBJECT_MISMATCH');\")]},\n+  {id:'M07',defect:'native positive bypasses semantic compatibility',positive:'G24',witness:'G11',patches:[patch(projection,inject,inject+\"\\n  if (layers.RECOMPUTATION?.semanticOutcome==='VERIFIED') return result('VERIFIED',reasons);\")]},\n+  {id:'M08',defect:'promote reproduced negative to verified',positive:'G24',witness:'G12',patches:[{file:projection,changes:[\n+    [\"if (layers.RECOMPUTATION?.semanticOutcome==='REFUTED') return result('CONTRADICTED',[...reasons,'NATIVE_NEGATIVE_RESULT']);\",\"if (false) return result('CONTRADICTED',[...reasons,'NATIVE_NEGATIVE_RESULT']);\"],\n+    [\"layers.RECOMPUTATION?.semanticOutcome!=='VERIFIED'\",\"!['VERIFIED','REFUTED'].includes(layers.RECOMPUTATION?.semanticOutcome)\"]]}]},\n+  {id:'M09',defect:'allow retry to mutate signed material action',positive:'G13',witness:'G14',patches:[patch('src/adapters/interpol