 and Pavlo evidence-grade refusal finding.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"role\": \"PUBLIC_SPEC_WITNESS_AND_REVIEW\",\n+      \"actor\": \"pipavlo82\",\n+      \"sourcePath\": \"conformance/scan-subject-binding-v0/README.md\",\n+      \"url\": \"https://github.com/trustless-ai/recompute-kit/blob/1a37bcaf91918fd8a98f164d97d0fddbc28c6755/conformance/scan-subject-binding-v0/README.md\",\n+      \"boundary\": \"README credits built-with Pavlo first effective-dataset executable witness and reshaping after his review; does not establish authorship of every checker line.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"role\": \"AUTHORED_RUNNER_FAILURE_CLASSIFIER_IMPLEMENTATION\",\n+      \"actor\": \"pipavlo82\",\n+      \"commit\": \"ce28d6888b224dd8551d0d1a1196a6cd706420cd\",\n+      \"sourcePath\": \"tools/run_conformance.py\",\n+      \"url\": \"https://github.com/trustless-ai/recompute-kit/commit/ce28d6888b224dd8551d0d1a1196a6cd706420cd\",\n+      \"boundary\": \"GitHub author pipavlo82; commit author Pavlo Tvardovskyi. Selected runner also contains babyblueviper1, Merlini/Echo and zexoverz contributions.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"role\": \"POST_MERGE_REVIEW_COMMENT\",\n+      \"actor\": \"pipavlo82\",\n+      \"url\": \"https://github.com/trustless-ai/recompute-kit/pull/59#issuecomment-6072721352\",\n+      \"boundary\": \"Review/ordering/documentation findings, not original implementation attribution.\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"upstreamPullRequests\": [\n+    {\n+      \"number\": 59,\n+      \"state\": \"MERGED\",\n+      \"head\": \"a05099ee5674f40148ee88ddf5105fdcf2fda607\",\n+      \"mergeCommit\": \"afd69037b3ef0cae7019eaa7328f3459954e116a\",\n+      \"author\": \"babyblueviper1\",\n+      \"mergedAt\": \"2026-10-09T01:46:39Z\",\n+      \"used\": true\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"number\": 65,\n+      \"state\": \"MERGED\",\n+      \"head\": \"4ed3a65fb44324239cb67fd807f51881af1b8bb3\",\n+      \"mergeCommit\": \"1a37bcaf91918fd8a98f164d97d0fddbc28c6755\",\n+      \"author\": \"pipavlo82\",\n+      \"mergedAt\": \"2026-10-11T20:26:34Z\",\n+      \"used\": \"source main includes merged guard history; PR65 profile mutation files are not vendored\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"number\": 57,\n+      \"state\": \"OPEN\",\n+      \"head\": \"197c6d26e68f85a117dd12a94924a7f959edaef4\",\n+      \"base\": \"1a37bcaf91918fd8a98f164d97d0fddbc28c6755\",\n+      \"author\": \"babyblueviper1\",\n+      \"maturity\": \"EXPERIMENTAL\",\n+      \"used\": false,\n+      \"reason\": \"Unmerged reporter-contract migration kept distinct from executable main adapter.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"number\": 52,\n+      \"state\": \"OPEN\",\n+      \"head\": \"7eaf8995748ec4a00cb313463d2555da8fea25b4\",\n+      \"author\": \"babyblueviper1\",\n+      \"maturity\": \"EXPERIMENTAL\",\n+      \"used\": false,\n+      \"reason\": \"Unmerged uncovered-entry behavior not imported.\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"boundaries\": [\n+    \"STABLE identifies merged source, not production security certification.\",\n+    \"Five selected upstream text files copied byte-for-byte from Git blobs; no captured datasets copied.\",\n+    \"Only native scan_subject_binding.v0 raw relation and one-case conformance runner are executed, not all upstream suites or mutation coverage.\",\n+    \"Main does not declare adapter.contract for the selected suite; native contractMode is null, product runnerContractInterpretation is MAIN_SELF_GRADING.\",\n+    \"Saved native expected result is only replay target; native raw functions compute semantic outcome independently.\",\n+    \"No private or commercial Vertice material used.\"\n+  ]\n+}"},{"sha":"bd2de00cda30e433943ceb23971ade38d5a3fc86","filename":"reports/release-audit-v0.2/.gitattributes","status":"added","additions":1,"deletions":0,"changes":1,"blob_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/blob/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/reports%2Frelease-audit-v0.2%2F.gitattributes","raw_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/raw/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/reports%2Frelease-audit-v0.2%2F.gitattributes","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/contents/reports%2Frelease-audit-v0.2%2F.gitattributes?ref=396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1 @@\n+* -text -whitespace"},{"sha":"29269c58f32122b8c6d9e915da7aa49b11c19415","filename":"reports/release-audit-v0.2/ASSESSMENT_CORRECTION.md","status":"added","additions":11,"deletions":0,"changes":11,"blob_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/blob/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/reports%2Frelease-audit-v0.2%2FASSESSMENT_CORRECTION.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/raw/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/reports%2Frelease-audit-v0.2%2FASSESSMENT_CORRECTION.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/contents/reports%2Frelease-audit-v0.2%2FASSESSMENT_CORRECTION.md?ref=396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@\n+# Assessment correction after contract review\n+\n+The before-checkpoint accurately preserves seven observed extension successes,\n+but its initial classification included two cases that are not established\n+technical defects. Valid inactive PRF/adapter contexts are explicitly selected\n+by `requested_guarantees`/adapter ID; presence alone activates no obligation.\n+An empty requested-guarantee list expressly establishes no transfer claim.\n+Those two cases are INFO and remain unchanged after repair. Five active unknown\n+or mistyped semantic requirements remain the HIGH REQ-01 defect. Exact before\n+receipts and initial findings are not rewritten. No broader activation feature\n+or behavioral change is introduced by this correction."},{"sha":"8f65b17740b15b6133c33ccefcf7180faee24789","filename":"reports/release-audit-v0.2/FINDINGS_BEFORE_FIX.md","status":"added","additions":23,"deletions":0,"changes":23,"blob_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/blob/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/reports%2Frelease-audit-v0.2%2FFINDINGS_BEFORE_FIX.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/raw/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/reports%2Frelease-audit-v0.2%2FFINDINGS_BEFORE_FIX.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/contents/reports%2Frelease-audit-v0.2%2FFINDINGS_BEFORE_FIX.md?ref=396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@\n+# Frozen v0.2 audit findings — BEFORE REPAIR\n+\n+Frozen candidate: `4888a0584369a91075eb2bdbd9a2ff6b99c46588`.\n+Tree: `d5a6fb8e47db373e59b6ce5ed021f3e1240a09fc`.\n+Initial worktree and fresh checkout clean; exact tracked inventories and diff against v0.1.0 are in `freeze/`.\n+\n+The fresh canonical suite passes 624/624 normal and no-opt, all68 vectors and both14-mutant inventories. These observations do not override the independently demonstrated defects below. This checkpoint records discovery before changing any implementation, schema or test source. Frozen-candidate verdict: **NEEDS_TECHNICAL_FIXES**.\n+\n+| ID | Severity | Exact defect | Before evidence |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| MUT-01 | HIGH | The legacy v1 mutation runner labels an inner-native crash and an exit-zero native JSON null as KILLED, returns process exit0, and reports successful mutation coverage. Positive V01 remains VERIFIED; negative V07 changes only to unavailable computation, not a semantic witness. | mutation-inner-failure/native-crash-before.json; native-null-before.json; controller.py |\n+| REQ-01 | HIGH | Unsupported/mistyped Interpoll and PRF caller requirements are silently dropped; orphan adapter/guarantee contexts are not evaluated. Seven exact requests become globally VERIFIED despite requesting unestablished fresh admission, server authentication, chain evidence or policy. | domains/FINDINGS.md; domains/requirement-admission/*.json |\n+| CONT-01 | MEDIUM | Non-Boolean whole-envelope requirement and unknown continuity options are ignored. Six malformed requests yield VERIFIED / continuity PRESERVED / whole-envelope NOT_ESTABLISHED. | core/FINDINGS.md; core/results/extension-summary.json and exact per-input reports |\n+| DOC-01 | LOW | docs/files-not-reused.md retains unqualified old no-copy/no-execution claims for native files now included/executed in v0.2. | corpus source/path audit and frozen document |\n+| DOC-02 | INFO | PR57 merged after the pinned-main observation: current recompute-kit main is3c3923956200d01ab74c2dcbb49b268739943bda, merge22:35:33Z. Candidate correctly uses historical-main1a37bcaf...; release wording must distinguish that observation from current state. No runtime repin is required. | domains/public-source-identities.json; current-main-replay.json; corpus/public-source-observations.json |\n+\n+MUT-01 is a coverage-integrity failure, not a demonstrated positive core verdict bypass. The original declared v1 crash-refutation mutant is a different legitimate semantic test: the same deliberately induced crash is present in baseline and mutant, and the mutation incorrectly labels unavailable computation CONTRADICTED. A repair must retain that witness while refusing newly introduced checker failures.\n+\n+REQ-01 and CONT-01 must be repaired by rejecting unknown, mistyped or nonapplicable consumer requirements, without implementing fresh server admission, chain authentication or new continuity features. Preserve supported positive contexts and all original v1 vector semantics. Direct adapter APIs and composed request admission both need the same fail-closed boundary.\n+\n+Independent passing checks remain separately scoped:57 generic/adversarial inputs,3238 finite projection substitutions,51 supported domain probes,140 literal corpus-oracle checks. The extension failures are additional cases and are not hidden inside those passing totals. All68 vectors remain;63 are assessed load-bearing and5 redundant semantic aliases, not68 independent branches. See the independent matrix and detailed reports.\n+\n+No upstream source or frozen candidate artifact was edited. No push, tag, release, PR or merge was performed. Implementation repairs follow in a separate commit; this discovery checkpoint must not be rewritten to pretend repaired outcomes occurred on the frozen SHA."},{"sha":"35f00becd96ec6b52594deab3d69c9c0e1255a61","filename":"reports/release-audit-v0.2/REPAIR_REGRESSION_BEFORE_FIX.md","status":"added","additions":7,"deletions":0,"changes":7,"blob_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/blob/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/reports%2Frelease-audit-v0.2%2FREPAIR_REGRESSION_BEFORE_FIX.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/raw/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/reports%2Frelease-audit-v0.2%2FREPAIR_REGRESSION_BEFORE_FIX.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/contents/reports%2Frelease-audit-v0.2%2FREPAIR_REGRESSION_BEFORE_FIX.md?ref=396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@\n+# Repair regression recorded before correction\n+\n+Tested commit: `1fecfc2587c5d89d350017a2a7a98ca78e933b9f`.\n+\n+The disposable fresh checkout passed 703/703 normal, no-opt and repeat tests, but the separate canonical corpus gate passed only 66/68. I03 changed from CONTRADICTED to REJECTED_MALFORMED; I08 changed from UNSUPPORTED_PROFILE to REJECTED_MALFORMED. The added request-context schema constrained the caller-selected action and authority too narrowly, preventing the existing adapter from evaluating its declared semantic relation. This is a MEDIUM regression in the repair; it is not evidence that frozen 4888 had these two failures.\n+\n+Exact command receipts, full outputs, source inventory and unchanged literal vector expectations: `repair/fresh/`. Fix the schema boundary and add explicit regressions without changing any vector or native semantics. Rerun the entire canonical gate on the next exact committed checkout."},{"sha":"23a4953df471a7c22bd2075ffb951b52e4fe260e","filename":"reports/release-audit-v0.2/capture-license/FINDING_BEFORE_FIX.md","status":"added","additions":9,"deletions":0,"changes":9,"blob_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/blob/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/reports%2Frelease-audit-v0.2%2Fcapture-license%2FFINDING_BEFORE_FIX.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/raw/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/reports%2Frelease-audit-v0.2%2Fcapture-license%2FFINDING_BEFORE_FIX.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/contents/reports%2Frelease-audit-v0.2%2Fcapture-license%2FFINDING_BEFORE_FIX.md?ref=396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@\n+# LIC-CAP-01 — audit capture rights, before sanitization\n+\n+Severity: HIGH for publication of the audit branch; no verifier runtime effect.\n+\n+Independent review of newly collected audit bytes found unnecessary upstream patch/source/body captures in three JSON reports. The original raw captures and their exact hashes were recorded before correction. Six repositories with absent or unclear grants account for 87 patch fields; the complete metadata-only field inventory records every omission without reproducing those source bytes. Repository ownership does not supply a grant.\n+\n+A final deletion commit alone would leave those raw blobs in pushed ancestry. Preserve the exact raw audit commits in a local work/ Git bundle; curate only agent-created commits after frozen4888, replacing API patch/body/content captures with metadata/hash records. Frozen4888, v0.1/main, all runtime/vendor/legal/old evidence bytes stay unchanged. Record every old/new audit commit mapping and sanitized file mapping. Rerun final exact-checkout canonical validation.\n+\n+This is an explicitly disclosed transformation of new audit captures, not retroactive modification of frozen product evidence. Original execution receipts continue to identify the original commits where commands