tion. V0.2 copies and executes only `shared-validation/engagement.js` from `559e47f2cd2ffcbd8ad38293da89448d8ec3152d` under its retained Unlicense grant, through the bounded native signed-action adapter. Not copied as runtime/data: `shared-validation/engagement-store.js`, `src/services/publicEngagementService.ts`, `src/services/reactionOutboxService.ts`, `tools/coordination-impact-v2/`. No upstream service/store/UI/SQL deployment or coordination receipt corpus is copied. Supplied retry relation checks are product code around that native signature primitive. Exact signed retries do not establish live admission atomicity, target existence, viewing, human uniqueness or independent coordination judgments.\"\n+}"},{"sha":"16c0a26eb5b0523f091663eafd7fb7b8d1cf8124","filename":"reports/release-audit-v0.2/capture-license/audit02-final-provenance-review.md","status":"added","additions":49,"deletions":0,"changes":49,"blob_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/blob/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/reports%2Frelease-audit-v0.2%2Fcapture-license%2Faudit02-final-provenance-review.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/raw/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/reports%2Frelease-audit-v0.2%2Fcapture-license%2Faudit02-final-provenance-review.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/contents/reports%2Frelease-audit-v0.2%2Fcapture-license%2Faudit02-final-provenance-review.md?ref=396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@\n+# Final independent provenance and corpus closure review\n+\n+Frozen candidate `4888a0584369a91075eb2bdbd9a2ff6b99c46588`. Repaired and metadata-curated code HEAD `eb942148eeb489db809b39e053ec905105cc3056`, tree `3fa1cea8387f733cab6a0868acf6060ec958b06d`. This is the independently reviewed code identity; root owns final documentation closure and the final A–T release verdict.\n+\n+## Coverage and independence\n+\n+- **68 stored vectors:63 LOAD_BEARING,5 REDUNDANT,0 SELF_REFERENTIAL,0 DECORATIVE,0 UNCLEAR.** Redundant controls are G09,G10,G19,I01,I05. G09/G01 and G10/G05 share actual compatibility branches through routing aliases; G19 repeats G04; I01/G13 and I05/G14 are exact input aliases. Every vector remains accounted with exact claim, invariant, expected native/layer/product result, required reasons, oracle, positive control and catalog-witness mapping.\n+- **43 public historical repositories,74 original source records,8 new integrations across 6 source repositories;51/51 source pins and 396/396 declared paths checked.** All source trees were complete, with no truncated response. Historical accounts are preserved; future/methodology/historical roles are not promoted to execution.\n+- **91/91 selected vendor/source files** match newly fetched exact public bytes and local SHA256/Git blobs (77 retained + 14 new, including 4 new license files). Seven npm legal files match. Root LICENSE is byte-identical to official Apache-2.0 text, SHA256 `cfc7749b96f63bd31c3c42b5c471bf756814053e847c10f3eb003417bc523d30`.\n+- **18/18 new author/path declarations** match. The historical 108-entry ledger has 68 ORIGINAL_CODE records, each backed by commit evidence;170 referenced declarations across161 unique commit endpoints resolve without explicit author-login mismatches. Review-only, original code, shared implementation and upstream dependency roles stay distinct; repository ownership is not the proof.\n+- **140/140 independent Python finite oracle checks** pass. They cover SHA256, one-leaf corpus identity, public action-ID encoding, field equality and PRF arithmetic. Product literal expectations are detached from verifier output, but native builders and Interpoll commitment helpers remain shared inputs. These counts establish bounded product witnesses, not full upstream crypto/canonicalization/conformance, a closed reason-code set, or external organizational independence.\n+\n+## Frozen-material preservation\n+\n+| Category | Files | Byte-identical to frozen 4888 | Changed |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| all_frozen_vectors | 70 | 70 | None |\n+| original_v01_vectors | 31 | 31 | None |\n+| vendor | 100 | 100 | None |\n+| root_legal | 4 | 4 | None |\n+| package_dependency_legal | 4 | 4 | None |\n+\n+The 74 original source records,43 repository accounts,8 integration records,3 fragment identities and original product-extension catalog are structurally unchanged from frozen 4888. Source-catalog updates add a dated live observation without changing runtime pins/grants. Protected legal/package/vendor/vector bytes remain frozen.\n+\n+## Corrected source-state and exclusion documentation\n+\n+PR57 was OPEN at the exact historical source observation, then merged at `2026-10-11T22:35:33Z`; current observed recompute-kit main is `3c3923956200d01ab74c2dcbb49b268739943bda`. Runtime stays pinned to older main `1a37bcaf91918fd8a98f164d97d0fddbc28c6755`, with native `contractMode:null` and separately labeled product `MAIN_SELF_GRADING`. Newly merged reporter behavior is not silently implemented. PRF PR14 remains separately OPEN/EXPERIMENTAL at `f525737069dc4cef7741f805d08a988912f4454f`.\n+\n+README, PROVENANCE, FULL_WORK_REUSE_MAP and Trustless adapter documentation now separate those observations. The file-exclusion companion explicitly identifies new PRF/Trustless/SemanticABI native selections, and root has corrected the Interpoll engagement.js exception in pending closure documentation:\n+\n+V0.1 did not copy the native action implementation. V0.2 copies and executes only `shared-validation/engagement.js` from `559e47f2cd2ffcbd8ad38293da89448d8ec3152d` under its retained Unlicense grant, through the bounded native signed-action adapter. Not copied as runtime/data: `shared-validation/engagement-store.js`, `src/services/publicEngagementService.ts`, `src/services/reactionOutboxService.ts`, `tools/coordination-impact-v2/`. No upstream service/store/UI/SQL deployment or coordination receipt corpus is copied. Supplied retry relation checks are product code around that native signature primitive. Exact signed retries do not establish live admission atomicity, target existence, viewing, human uniqueness or independent coordination judgments.\n+\n+## Audit-evidence rights finding and closure\n+\n+Expanded review found unnecessary raw GitHub patch/body/content source captures in three new audit-report files. The earlier91-file vendor legal conclusion was valid for selected runtime files but did not cover these additional tracked audit bytes. Some patches came from absent/unclear-grant sources or separately owned source/data. This was recorded before sanitization and does not establish a runtime defect.\n+\n+Uniform metadata curation removed 1,082 source patch strings,4 API body captures and 86 API content captures. SHA256/length, author, commit/blob identities and changed paths remain. All 137 currently present non-API semantic body/content witnesses are preserved. Current sanitizer DRY_RUN finds **0 source captures requiring omission**. Numeric metadata counters named patch are not source bodies.\n+\n+Raw history is preserved only in local work bundle, SHA256 `bdcda1d52ff39859be852c110c32fc010649a24e54268fad1d608ea9669aff3b`. Five newly created post4888 audit commits were mapped to curated commits; frozen 4888 and all non-report blobs per old/new commit pair are identical. All five raw audit commits and all three raw capture blobs are unreachable from reviewed HEAD. Every original/sanitized capture hash mapping matches. This addresses ancestry as well as the visible tree; final publication must use the curated identity/source export, not the quarantined raw bundle.\n+\n+Independent committed source-lock verification: **344/344**, SHA256 `3c7399a199fcff7fd4f381746d0a22071800065a9798b422fd49a36c0889f4e4`. Root's pending documentation edits temporarily make the working lock stale; this is expected closure work, not a newly demonstrated product defect. The final report/closure commit must refresh and revalidate it.\n+\n+## Report boundaries\n+\n+Frozen 624-test/68-vector green results did not override later unsupported-requirement and mutation-classification defects. Keep frozen findings, repaired outcomes, the documented intermediate703-test/66-vector schema regression, and final exact committed recheck separate. Root is running the final fresh canonical gate; no expected 707 count is promoted here to an observed result.\n+\n+No private Vértice runtime/dependency, full upstream conformance, remote Interpoll server/SQL execution, quantum provider/hardware authenticity, arbitrary scope entailment, production certification, sole ownership or revenue allocation is established. QEV/PQ/stochastic/v1 carriers remain independently bounded. Root owns final projection/mutation/UI/CLI/malformed-input results, affected-test counts, full canonical gate and final A–T verdict.\n+\n+Evidence: `audit02-final-provenance-review.json`, `audit02-curation-independent-review.json`, `audit02-audit-capture-license-before.json/.md`, `audit02-audit-capture-license-after.json`, original corpus/source/path/author/public observations and V0_2_VECTOR_WITNESS_MATRIX.md. This sub-review made no product or upstream edits."},{"sha":"b8ba27e6718beffe5e2ff86c78b1aecc60935b28","filename":"reports/release-audit-v0.2/capture-license/before-inventory.json","status":"added","additions":14319,"deletions":0,"changes":14319,"blob_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/blob/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/reports%2Frelease-audit-v0.2%2Fcapture-license%2Fbefore-inventory.json","raw_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/raw/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/reports%2Frelease-audit-v0.2%2Fcapture-license%2Fbefore-inventory.json","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/contents/reports%2Frelease-audit-v0.2%2Fcapture-license%2Fbefore-inventory.json?ref=396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775"},{"sha":"fbce1217d257cea90176486b005eabcecd5480c7","filename":"reports/release-audit-v0.2/capture-license/curate-history.py","status":"added","additions":36,"deletions":0,"changes":36,"blob_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/blob/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/reports%2Frelease-audit-v0.2%2Fcapture-license%2Fcurate-history.py","raw_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/raw/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/reports%2Frelease-audit-v0.2%2Fcapture-license%2Fcurate-history.py","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/contents/reports%2Frelease-audit-v0.2%2Fcapture-license%2Fcurate-history.py?ref=396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@\n+import pathlib,subprocess,json,hashlib,importlib.util,os\n+ws=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\n+repo=ws/'outputs/receiptos-verify';frozen='4888a0584369a91075eb2bdbd9a2ff6b99c46588'\n+def git(*args,input=None,env=None):return subprocess.check_output(['git',*args],cwd=repo,input=input,env=env)\n+assert not git('status','--porcelain=v1','--untracked-files=all')\n+oldhead=git('rev-parse','HEAD').decode().strip();branch=git('branch','--show-current').decode().strip();assert branch=='feat/v0.2-generic-trustless-boundary'\n+bundle=ws/'work/v02-raw-audit-unpublished.bundle';\n+if not bundle.exists():git('bundle','create',str(bundle),branch,'^'+frozen)\n+else:git('bundle','verify',str(bundle))\n+spec=importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('san',ws/'work/audit02-sanitize-captures.py');mod=importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec);spec.loader.exec_module(mod)\n+paths=[r['path'] for r in json.loads((ws/'work/audit02-audit-capture-license-before.json').read_text())['files']]\n+index=ws/'work/v02-curation.index';env={**os.environ,'GIT_INDEX_FILE':str(index)}\n+mapping=[];parent=frozen;changes=[]\n+for old in git('rev-list','--reverse',frozen+'..'+oldhead).decode().splitlines():\n+ git('read-tree',old,env=env);current=[]\n+ for path in paths:\n+  raw=git('show',old+':'+path);records=[];data=mod.walk(json.loads(raw),records=records);clean=(json.dumps(data,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\\n').encode()\n+  oid=git('hash-object','-w','--stdin',input=clean).decode().strip();git('update-index','--add','--cacheinfo','100644,'+oid+','+path,env=env)\n+  current.append({'path':path,'beforeSHA256':hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest(),'afterSHA256':hashlib.sha256(clean).hexdigest(),'afterBytes':len(clean),'omittedFields':len(records)})\n+ manifestpath='reports/release-audit-v0.2/corpus/evidence-manifest.json'\n+ if git('ls-tree',old,'--',manifestpath).strip():\n+  rawm=git('show',old+':'+manifestpath);manifest=json.loads(rawm)\n+  for row in manifest['files']:\n+   matches=[c for c in current if c['path'].endswith('/'+row['path'])]\n+   if matches:\n+    c=matches[0];row['bytes']=c['afterBytes'];row['sha256']=c['afterSHA256'];row['originalRawSHA256']=c['beforeSHA256']\n+  manifest['captureSanitization']={'originalRawManifestSHA256':hashlib.sha256(rawm).hexdigest(),'omissions':'Unnecessary API patch/body/content; exact originals quarantined locally; metadata-only mapping retained.','files':current}\n+  cleanm=(json.dumps(manifest,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\n').encode();oid=git('hash-object','-w','--stdin',input=cleanm).decode().strip();git('update-index','--add','--cacheinfo','100644,'+oid+','+manifestpath,env=env)\n+ tree=git('write-tree',env=env).decode().strip();message=git('show','-s','--format=%B',old)\n+ new=git('commit-tree',tree,'-p',parent,input=message).decode().strip()\n+ beforecode=[r for r in git('ls-tree','-r',old).splitlines() if not r.split(b'\\t',1)[1].startswith(b'reports/')];aftercode=[r for r in git('ls-tree','-r',new).splitlines() if not r.split(b'\\t',1)[1].startswith(b'reports/')];assert beforecode==aftercode\n+ mapping.append({'original_local_commit':old,'sanitized_commit':new,'tree':tree,'non_report_blobs_identical':True,'file_mappings':current});parent=new\n+record={'schema':'receiptos.audit.local-history-curation.v1','frozen_anchor':frozen,'old_head':oldhead,'new_head':parent,'branch':branch,'raw_bundle':str(bundle),'raw_bundle_sha256':hashlib.sha256(bundle.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),'mapping':mapping,'boundary':'Only agent-created local audit commits after frozen anchor curated; frozen/main/tags and all non-report blobs preserved. Raw originals remain unpublished work evidence. Execution receipts retain original identities.'}\n+(workout:=ws/'work/v02-audit-curation.json').write_text(json.dumps(record,indent=2)+'\\n',encoding='utf-8',newline='\\n')\n+git('update-ref','refs/heads/'+branch,parent,oldhead);git('reset','--hard',parent)\n+index.unlink();print(json.dumps({'old_head':oldhead,'new_head':parent,'commits_curated':len(mapping),'frozen_anchor':frozen,'raw_bundle_sha256':record['raw_bundle_sha256']}))"},{"sha":"7f1379250d0399718c44b9cfc78985051975ffcb","filename":"reports/release-audit-v0.2/capture-license/final-scan.json","status":"added","additions":1711,"deletions":0,"changes":1711,"blob_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/blob/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/reports%2Frelease-audit-v0.2%2Fcapture-license%2Ffinal-scan.json","raw_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/raw/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/reports%2Frelease-audit-v0.2%2Fcapture-license%2Ffinal-scan.json","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/contents/reports%2Frelease-audit-v0.2%2Fcapture-license%2Ffinal-scan.json?ref=396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,1711 @@\n+{\n+  \"schema\": \"receiptos.audit.capture-sanitization.v1\",\n+  \"mode\": \"DRY_RUN\",\n+  \"files\": [],\n+  \"omittedFieldCounts\": {},\n+  \"omittedFields\": [],\n+  \"retainedSemanticBodyContent\": [\n+    {\n+      \"file\": \"reports/release-audit-v0.2/capture-license/audit02-final-provenance-review.json\",\n+      \"jsonPath\": \"capturePublicationFinding/omittedFieldCounts/body\",\n+      \"valueType\": \"int\",\n+      \"utf8