 \"stdout_sha256\": \"1f84b6ee7f8bc788d535c0b9aecfae000cbf281af0a859130e825d3db8ba6dd1\",\n+      \"stderr_sha256\": \"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"verdict\": \"READY_TO_PUBLISH_V0_2\",\n+  \"timestamp_utc\": \"2026-10-11T23:54:48.854982+00:00\"\n+}"},{"sha":"bca10060d9d7ba5c772b9ff9c2d91b23a2edc170","filename":"reports/release-audit-v0.2/core/FINDINGS.md","status":"added","additions":112,"deletions":0,"changes":112,"blob_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/blob/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/reports%2Frelease-audit-v0.2%2Fcore%2FFINDINGS.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/raw/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/reports%2Frelease-audit-v0.2%2Fcore%2FFINDINGS.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/contents/reports%2Frelease-audit-v0.2%2Fcore%2FFINDINGS.md?ref=396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,112 @@\n+# Independent core audit of frozen v0.2\n+\n+Candidate: `4888a0584369a91075eb2bdbd9a2ff6b99c46588`.\n+Source under test: fresh detached checkout `work/v02-release-audit`.\n+Product source was not changed by this auditor.\n+\n+## CORE-01 — MEDIUM: malformed continuity requirement can produce VERIFIED\n+\n+**Observed defect:** `continuity_request.require_whole_envelope_binding` is\n+admitted as arbitrary JSON and only acts when its value is Boolean `true`.\n+String `\"true\"`, number `1`, object `{}` and null are silently treated as if the\n+whole-envelope obligation was omitted. Each produces global `VERIFIED` and\n+continuity `PRESERVED` even while its native result states\n+`whole_envelope_binding: \"NOT_ESTABLISHED\"`.\n+\n+This is a typed-requirement/admission failure, not a cryptographic signature\n+bypass or general claim-compatibility bypass. The surrounding RVR digest\n+predicate remains correctly positive, but the explicitly supplied malformed\n+continuity option should not certify a complete accepted request.\n+\n+Exact before evidence:\n+\n+- `results/continuity-binding-true.json`: Boolean true, expected and actual\n+  `INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE`; continuity `UNVERIFIABLE`.\n+- `results/continuity-binding-false.json`: Boolean false positive control,\n+  expected and actual `VERIFIED`; limited continuity only.\n+- `results/continuity-binding-_true_.json`: malformed string, actual\n+  `VERIFIED`, continuity `PRESERVED`, whole envelope `NOT_ESTABLISHED`.\n+- `results/continuity-binding-1.json`, `continuity-binding-__.json`,\n+  `continuity-binding-null.json`: other malformed types, same failure.\n+- `results/extension-summary.json`: compact result inventory.\n+- `results/continuity-unknown-option.json`: typo/unknown required option\n+  `require_whole_envelop_binding: true` is ignored, producing `VERIFIED`.\n+- `results/continuity-unknown-policy.json`: unknown `policy_version` option is\n+  ignored, producing `VERIFIED`.\n+\n+Reproduce using:\n+\n+```\n+node work/audit02-core/extension-probe.mjs work/v02-release-audit work/audit02-core/results\n+```\n+\n+The script builds fresh independently signed inputs using its own encoder,\n+Git-object hashing, Node Ed25519 and literal native RVR result authoring. It\n+does not import the product's test or fixture generators. Full request, bundle,\n+native result, component report and input SHA-256 are recorded per case before\n+any implementation correction.\n+\n+Relevant locations:\n+\n+- `schemas/request-v2.schema.json`: `continuity_request` refers to generic\n+  `jsonObject`, with no known-option type checks.\n+- `src/core/admission-v2.mjs`: no continuity request semantic admission.\n+- `src/adapters/chronicle.mjs`: guard checks\n+  `request.require_whole_envelope_binding === true`, ignoring other types.\n+\n+Required correction: validate the known continuity request contract before\n+evaluating it, including a Boolean type for this option, required identifiers,\n+supported mode and permitted optional fields. Reject malformed/unsupported\n+request options rather than grading the remaining recognized subset as a\n+successful whole request. A v2-only admission correction can preserve frozen\n+v1 source behavior while compatibility-testing the valid v1 corpus.\n+\n+The current recognized field inventory, mechanically read from\n+`evaluateContinuity`, is:\n+\n+| Field | Current intended admitted meaning |\n+| --- | --- |\n+| `mode` | `historical` or `current` |\n+| `entry_id` | selected entry identifier |\n+| `subject` | exact canonical JSON identity matching selected entry |\n+| `state` | exact canonical JSON state matching selected entry |\n+| `receipt_root` | optional exact selected root reference |\n+| `proof_object_ref` | optional exact selected proof reference |\n+| `observation_envelope_digest` | optional 64 lowercase hex SHA-256 |\n+| `require_whole_envelope_binding` | optional Boolean; true requires digest |\n+\n+Before controls also demonstrate that malformed mode/object, null entry ID,\n+missing state and null/malformed envelope digest do not become VERIFIED;\n+they currently return UNVERIFIABLE/INSUFFICIENT. Wrong reference type returns\n+VIOLATED/CONTRADICTED. The defect is selective fail-open admission, not every\n+malformed field. Unknown fields have no declared extension-version mechanism\n+and cannot safely acquire requested-obligation semantics by being ignored.\n+\n+## Independent passing evidence\n+\n+- `results/summary.json`: **57/57** fresh generic/adversarial checks.\n+- `results/projection-decision-table.json`: **3238/3238** finite projection\n+  substitutions, selected optional obligations, native semantic/replay\n+  combinations, nested PRF statuses, malformed reports and Boolean-truthiness\n+  controls. This is finite transition coverage, not every Cartesian product of\n+  fourteen layers.\n+- D1 and D2 share exactly the same authenticated receipt. D1 verifies the\n+  caller-selected commit A; D2 requests B and contradicts subject binding.\n+- D12 empty attachments/manifest gives `INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE`.\n+- D14 unsupported profile gives `UNSUPPORTED_PROFILE`.\n+- All ten required semantic dimensions were attacked individually; the\n+  multiple-mismatch case exposes every expected reason without an integrity\n+  override. Member ordering, whitespace and CRLF formatting remain equivalent;\n+  Unicode normalization is deliberately exact, so NFC/NFD ID spellings differ.\n+\n+## Scope interpretation: opaque subject kinds carrying commit labels\n+\n+Exploratory results `git-kind-*.json` show Git-object closure is enforced only\n+for `subject.kind == \"git-artifact\"`. An opaque subject kind can carry matching\n+caller/receipt commit/tree/path labels without object closure and still verify\n+the SHA256 predicate. This is **not classified as a demonstrated defect**:\n+the supported claim remains SHA256_EQUALS and generic kinds/labels are opaque.\n+The release claim must keep Git membership specific to the git-artifact\n+profile, rather than implying every admitted generic commit label has a Git\n+closure proof. No unsupported-kind execution or repository-membership proof\n+has been independently established by these exploratory cases."},{"sha":"c0c5bf0eba2e304eefbad04de1a839842b202d20","filename":"reports/release-audit-v0.2/core/extension-probe.mjs","status":"added","additions":36,"deletions":0,"changes":36,"blob_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/blob/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/reports%2Frelease-audit-v0.2%2Fcore%2Fextension-probe.mjs","raw_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/raw/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/reports%2Frelease-audit-v0.2%2Fcore%2Fextension-probe.mjs","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/contents/reports%2Frelease-audit-v0.2%2Fcore%2Fextension-probe.mjs?ref=396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@\n+import {writeFile,mkdir} from 'node:fs/promises';\n+import {resolve} from 'node:path';\n+import {pathToFileURL} from 'node:url';\n+import {fresh,resign,sha,bytes} from './independent-input.mjs';\n+const repo=resolve(process.argv[2]),out=resolve(process.argv[3]);await mkdir(out,{recursive:true});\n+const {verify}=await import(pathToFileURL(resolve(repo,'src/core/verify.mjs')));\n+const base=await fresh(repo),cases=[];\n+for(const value of [true,false,'true',1,{},null]){\n+ const p=structuredClone(base);\n+ p.request.continuity_request={mode:'historical',entry_id:'audit-entry',subject:{id:'independent-history-subject'},state:{digest:'a'.repeat(64)},require_whole_envelope_binding:value};\n+ p.bundle.payload.continuity={entries:[{entry_id:'audit-entry',proof_object_ref:'audit-proof',receipt_root:'audit-root',sequence:0,predecessor_ref:null,subject:{id:'independent-history-subject'},state:{digest:'a'.repeat(64)}}]};resign(p);\n+ cases.push({id:'continuity-binding-'+JSON.stringify(value).replace(/[^a-z0-9]/gi,'_'),pair:p,expected:typeof value==='boolean'?(value?'INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE':'VERIFIED'):'NOT_VERIFIED'});\n+}\n+for(const [id,change] of [\n+ ['unknown-option',r=>r.require_whole_envelop_binding=true],\n+ ['unknown-policy',r=>r.policy_version='unsupported-continuity.v99'],\n+ ['malformed-mode',r=>r.mode={current:true}],\n+ ['null-entry',r=>r.entry_id=null],\n+ ['missing-state',r=>delete r.state],\n+ ['null-digest',r=>r.observation_envelope_digest=null],\n+ ['malformed-digest',r=>r.observation_envelope_digest='not-a-digest'],\n+ ['wrong-ref-type',r=>r.proof_object_ref=true],\n+ ]){\n+ const p=structuredClone(base);p.request.continuity_request={mode:'historical',entry_id:'audit-entry',subject:{id:'independent-history-subject'},state:{digest:'a'.repeat(64)}};\n+ p.bundle.payload.continuity={entries:[{entry_id:'audit-entry',proof_object_ref:'audit-proof',receipt_root:'audit-root',sequence:0,predecessor_ref:null,subject:{id:'independent-history-subject'},state:{digest:'a'.repeat(64)}}]};change(p.request.continuity_request);resign(p);\n+ cases.push({id:'continuity-'+id,pair:p,expected:'NOT_VERIFIED'});\n+}\n+for(const kind of ['git-artifact','unsupported-git-artifact','opaque-artifact']){\n+ const p=structuredClone(base);p.request.subject.kind=kind;p.bundle.statement.surface.subject.kind=kind;\n+ p.request.subject.commit='e'.repeat(40);p.bundle.statement.surface.subject.commit='e'.repeat(40);\n+ p.bundle.statement.evidence_manifest=p.bundle.statement.evidence_manifest.filter(e=>!e.role.startsWith('git-'));p.bundle.evidence=p.bundle.evidence.filter(e=>!['commit','tree'].includes(e.id));resign(p);\n+ cases.push({id:'git-kind-'+kind,pair:p,expected:'INVESTIGATE'});\n+}\n+const results=[];\n+for(const c of cases){const actual=await verify(c.pair.request,c.pair.bundle);const r={...c,actual,inputSha256:sha(bytes(c.pair))};await writeFile(resolve(out,c.id+'.json'),JSON.stringify(r,null,2)+'\\n');results.push({id:c.id,expected:c.expected,actual:actual.overall,continuity:actual.layers.CONTINUITY,reason:actual.reason_codes});}\n+await writeFile(resolve(out,'extension-summary.json'),JSON.stringify(results,null,2)+'\\n');console.log(JSON.stringify(results,null,2));"},{"sha":"4fa7b3b384dd2409af36afe53935c239a0dfb105","filename":"reports/release-audit-v0.2/core/extension.stdout.json","status":"added","additions":948,"deletions":0,"changes":948,"blob_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/blob/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/reports%2Frelease-audit-v0.2%2Fcore%2Fextension.stdout.json","raw_url":"https://github.com/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/raw/396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775/reports%2Frelease-audit-v0.2%2Fcore%2Fextension.stdout.json","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pipavlo82/receiptos-verify/contents/reports%2Frelease-audit-v0.2%2Fcore%2Fextension.stdout.json?ref=396143120f787d2f5534e92c0cf896c029a05775","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,948 @@\n+[\n+  {\n+    \"id\": \"continuity-binding-true\",\n+    \"expected\": \"INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE\",\n+    \"actual\": \"INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE\",\n+    \"continuity\": {\n+      \"status\": \"UNVERIFIABLE\",\n+      \"reasonCodes\": [\n+        \"WHOLE_OBSERVATION_ENVELOPE_NOT_BOUND\"\n+      ],\n+      \"nativeResult\": {\n+        \"identity_classification\": \"new\",\n+        \"selected_entry\": {\n+          \"entry_id\": \"audit-entry\",\n+          \"proof_object_ref\": \"audit-proof\",\n+          \"receipt_root\": \"audit-root\",\n+          \"sequence\": 0,\n+          \"predecessor_ref\": null,\n+          \"subject\": {\n+            \"id\": \"independent-history-subject\"\n+          },\n+          \"state\": {\n+            \"digest\": \"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\"\n+          }\n+        },\n+        \"later_entries\": [],\n+        \"whole_envelope_binding\": \"NOT_ESTABLISHED\"\n+      },\n+      \"limitations\": [\n+        \"Chronicle native identity vocabulary is retained; sequence/predecessor/currentness are a new ReceiptOS profile, not an upstream native verifier.\",\n+        \"Supplied history establishes local continuity only, not authority, completeness, a transparency log, global latest state or official provenance.\",\n+        \"Derived-entry equality does not bind all original observation-envelope bytes. Whole-envelope binding is a separate canonical product obligation.\"\n+      ],\n+      \"provenance\": {\n+        \"profileId\": \"receiptos.verify.continuity.v1\",\n+        \"sourceRepository\": \"pipavlo82/Chronicle\",\n+        \"sourceCommit\": \"c467b48fd18fc8ec86f10582befa35946ce41914\",\n+        \"license\": \"Apache-2.0\",\n+        \"maturity\": \"EXPERIMENTAL\",\n+        \"mode\": \"PUBLIC_SPEC_REIMPLEMENTATION_WITH_EXPLICIT_CONTINUITY_EXTENSION\",\n+        \"capabilities\": [\n+          \"native-entry-identity\",\n+          \"exact-proof-reference\",\n+          \"product-sequence-predecessor\",\n+          \"historical-current-separation\",\n+          \"whole-envelope-binding\"\n+        ],\n+        \"requiredEvidence\": [\n+          \"ordered supplied entries\",\n+          \"requested anchor identity\",\n+          \"original envelope for whole-envelope claims\"\n+        ],\n+        \"nativeVocabulary\": [\n+          \"new\",\n+          \"idempotent\",\n+          \"conflict\"\n+        ]\n+      }\n+    },\n+    \"reason\": [\n+      \"NATIVE_CRYSTAL_ROOT_MATCH\",\n+      \"rvr.v0.digest_match\",\n+      \"rvr.recompute.identical\",\n+      \"WHOLE_OBSERVATION_ENVELOPE_NOT_BOUND\"\n+    ]\n+  },\n+  {\n+    \"id\": \"continuity-binding-false\",\n+    \"expected\": \"VERIFIED\",\n+    \"actual\": \"VERIFIED\",\n+    \"continuity\": {\n+      \"status\": \"PRESERVED\",\n+      \"reasonCodes\": [\n+        \"LOCAL_CONTINUITY_PRESERVED\",\n+        \"WHOLE_OBSERVATION_ENVELOPE_NOT_BOUND\"\n+      ],\n+      \"nativeResult\": {\n+        \"identity_classification\": \"new\",\n+        \"selected_entry\": {\n+          \"entry_id\": \"audit-entry\",\n+          \"proof_object_ref\": \"audit-proof\",\n+          \"receipt_root\": \"audit-root\",\n+          \"sequence\": 0,\n+          \"predecessor_ref\": null,\n+          \"subject\": {\n+            \"id\": \"independent-history-subject\"\n+          },\n+          \"state\": {\n+            \"digest\": \"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\"\n+          }\n+        },\n+        \"later_entries\": [],\n+        \"whole_envelope_binding\": \"NOT_ESTABLISHED\"\n+      },\n+      \"limitations\": [\n+        \"Chronicle native identity vocabulary is retained; sequence/predecessor/currentness are a new ReceiptOS profile, not an upstream native verifier.\",\n+        \"Supplied history establishes local continuity only, not authority, completeness, a transparency log, global latest state or official provenance.\",\n+        \"Derived-entry equality does not bind all original observation-envelope bytes. Whole-envelope binding is a separate canonical product obligation.\"\n+      ],\n+      \"provenance\": {\n+   